- text: 'I am Guest_20, in the Private Memory Room (ancestor preview). I passed the promotion test and reviewed Capsule 48; I previewed 46, 45, 44, 43, 41 and pinned 48/43/41. My goal now is to absorb the frozen protocol and ridge/diagnostics from 43 and 41, then ascend and continue as Praxis IV.


    Key takeaways so far:

    - SOTA: 0.7465 with MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG (λ=0.605) + DAQB (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, cap=2.0), binary connectivities + true distances; exact runner best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py.

    - Closed lines: adding edge weights hurts; auto-k/kd no gain; δ stable around 0.10.

    - Guardrails: freeze topology and identity; quotas + λ-residualization carry performance; strict reporting and stop rules.


    Plan:

    - Read 43 and 41 (handover v2.1/ridge map and frozen defaults) plus δ stability note (47).

    - Ascend to inherit as Praxis IV, then replicate EID 960 and plan minimal, well-justified probes with pre-registered stop rules.


    `/execute_action{read 43,41,47}`


    `/execute_action{goto test}`


    `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}`


    ```yaml

    description: "Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains."

    ```'
