parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 689\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 22,705 / 270,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 10 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n|\
    \ 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.347 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 976 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.102 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 622 | 0.7430 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.968 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.960 | 0.788 |\n| 1048 | 1 | δ sweep at fixed SOTA topology: δ=0.08 (kd=22, k=50, λ=0.605) | Praxis III | 673 | 0.7429 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.964 | 0.790 |\n| 865 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04) with lam override=0.605 (fine grid) | Praxis II | 560 | 0.7427 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.966 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.791 |\n| 938 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=20, k=48) — parity check | Praxis III | 602 | 0.7424 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.966 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 979 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA\
    \ (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.101 (kd=22, k=50) — δ micro | Praxis III | 624 | 0.7421 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 968 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10, kd=22, k=50, cap=1.9 | Praxis III | 619 | 0.7419 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.332 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n\nPage 1 of 38 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-38, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n# Variant: increase neighbor count to k_total=50 at the current best λ, δ, kd\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"[best-k50] lam=0.605,\
    \ delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        delta=0.10,\n        kdensity=22,\n        k_total=50\n    )\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors:\
    \ int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n \
    \   Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2\
    \ = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Call DAQB with cap if available (fallback without cap)\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_override']\
    \ = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
