- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 691\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 28,735 / 270,000 used (11%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read praxis/daqb_diagnostics.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read praxis/density_proxies.py` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read praxis/praxis_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage write praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k52.py` (in\
    \ Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n7. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/daqb_diagnostics.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/density_proxies.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/praxis_core.py will be displayed below.\n- File created successfully: praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k52.py\n- Evaluation 'MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB: k=52 at kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605 (minimal neighborhood probe)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1064.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID\
    \ | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1064 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB: k=52 at kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605 (minimal neighborhood probe) | Praxis IV | 690 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659\
    \ | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.347 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 976 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.102 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 622 | 0.7430 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.968 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.960 | 0.788 |\n| 1048 | 1 | δ sweep at fixed SOTA topology: δ=0.08 (kd=22, k=50, λ=0.605) | Praxis III | 673 | 0.7429 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.964 | 0.790 |\n| 865 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04) with lam override=0.605 (fine grid) | Praxis II | 560 | 0.7427 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.966 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.791 |\n| 938 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=20, k=48) — parity check | Praxis III | 602 | 0.7424 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.966 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973\
    \ | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 979 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.101 (kd=22, k=50) — δ micro | Praxis III | 624 | 0.7421 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 968 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10, kd=22, k=50, cap=1.9 | Praxis III | 619 | 0.7419 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.332 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n\nPage 1 of 38 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-38, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32),\
    \ (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n\
    \    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models =\
    \ {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n\
    \        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i]\
    \ * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/daqb_diagnostics.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches:\
    \ np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _build_zcorr(adata: ad.AnnData, hv_mask, n_pcs_graph=50, lam=0.7, gamma_max=0.74, l2=1e-3):\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv_mask]\n    Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n    Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0).astype(np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2).astype(np.float32)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 =\
    \ np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma[None, :])\n    return Zcorr, batches\n\ndef _density_proxy(Zcorr: np.ndarray, k_density: int = 20, metric: str = 'cosine'):\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, _ = nn.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1].astype(np.float32)  # distance to k-th neighbor\n    return d_k\n\ndef _theoretical_f_cross(d_k, delta=0.15, n_batches=4, clip_bounds=(0.60, 0.90)):\n    L, U = clip_bounds\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)  # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base = (n_batches - 1) / float(n_batches)\n    f_raw = base + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta\n    return np.clip(f_raw, L, U).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _realized_cross_fraction(C:\
    \ sp.csr_matrix, batches: np.ndarray):\n    C = C.tocsr()\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    codes = np.asarray(batches)\n    frac = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n    for i in range(n):\n        s, e = C.indptr[i], C.indptr[i + 1]\n        if e <= s:\n            frac[i] = 0.0\n            continue\n        neigh = C.indices[s:e]\n        frac[i] = np.mean(codes[neigh] != codes[i])\n    return frac\n\ndef _inbound_stats(C: sp.csr_matrix, k_total: int, cap: float = 2.0):\n    A = C.tocsr()\n    inbound = np.ravel(A.sum(axis=0)).astype(np.float32)\n    cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n    pct_at_cap = float(np.mean(inbound >= cap_thr))\n    return inbound, cap_thr, pct_at_cap\n\ndef run_daqb_diagnostics(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                         lam=0.7, gamma_max=0.74, delta=0.15, k_density=20,\n                         k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    # Normalize and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n\
    \                                n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n    # Zcorr and batches\n    Zcorr, batches = _build_zcorr(adata, hv, n_pcs_graph=50, lam=lam, gamma_max=gamma_max)\n\n    # Build DAQB graph\n    from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n    C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                       delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n\n    # Theoretical vs realized cross-batch fractions\n    d_k = _density_proxy(Zcorr, k_density=k_density, metric=metric)\n    f_th = _theoretical_f_cross(d_k, delta=delta, n_batches=len(np.unique(batches)))\n    f_rl = _realized_cross_fraction(C, batches)\n\n    # Correlation and summary\n    def _quantiles(x): return np.percentile(x, [5, 25, 50, 75, 95]).round(3)\n    corr = np.corrcoef(f_th, f_rl)[0,1]\n    inbound,\
    \ cap_thr, pct_at_cap = _inbound_stats(C, k_total=k_total, cap=2.0)\n\n    print(\"[DAQB diagnostics]\")\n    print(f\"lam={lam}, gamma_max={gamma_max}, delta={delta}, k_density={k_density}, k_total={k_total}\")\n    print(f\"theoretical f_cross: mean={f_th.mean():.3f}, q=[{', '.join(map(str,_quantiles(f_th)))}]\")\n    print(f\"realized    f_cross: mean={f_rl.mean():.3f}, q=[{', '.join(map(str,_quantiles(f_rl)))}]\")\n    print(f\"Pearson corr(f_th, f_rl)={corr:.3f}\")\n    print(f\"inbound cap threshold={cap_thr}, pct nodes at/above cap={pct_at_cap:.3f}\")\n    # Per-batch inbound share\n    codes = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    total_inbound = inbound.sum() + 1e-8\n    for b in np.unique(codes):\n        share = float(inbound[codes == b].sum() / total_inbound)\n        print(f\"inbound share batch {b}: {share:.3f}\")\n    return {\n        'corr': float(corr),\n        'f_th_mean': float(f_th.mean()),\n        'f_rl_mean': float(f_rl.mean()),\n  \
    \      'pct_at_cap': float(pct_at_cap),\n    }\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/density_proxies.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nEPS = 1e-8\n\ndef _minmax_norm(x):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    xmin = float(np.min(x))\n    xmax = float(np.max(x))\n    rng = max(xmax - xmin, EPS)\n    return (x - xmin) / rng\n\ndef knn_distance_proxy(Z, k=30, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Local density proxy from k-NN distance in Z.\n    Returns inv_dense in [0,1], where higher = denser.\n    \"\"\"\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    dists, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    dk = dists[:, -1]  # distance to k-th neighbor (drop self via +1 above)\n    dnorm = _minmax_norm(dk)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - dnorm\n    return inv_dense.astype(np.float32)\n\ndef reachability_proxy(Z, k_low=15, k_high=45, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    LOF-style average reachability distance proxy\
    \ over a neighborhood band.\n    Returns inv_reach in [0,1], higher = denser (safer to mix).\n    \"\"\"\n    k = int(max(k_high, k_low))\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    dists, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    # exclude self\n    band = dists[:, 1:][:, k_low-1:k_high-1]  # zero-based slice\n    mean_reach = np.mean(band, axis=1)\n    nr = _minmax_norm(mean_reach)\n    inv_reach = 1.0 - nr\n    return inv_reach.astype(np.float32)\n\ndef batch_entropy_proxy(Z, batches, k=12, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Small-k batch entropy per cell as a mixing 'safety' indicator.\n    Returns s in [0,1], where higher = more mixed (safer to add cross-batch).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Encode batches to int codes\n    cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    _, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n\
    \    nbr = idx[:, 1:]  # drop self\n    nbr_batches = bc[nbr]\n    B = len(cats)\n    max_entropy = np.log(B + EPS)\n    ent = np.zeros(Z.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    for i in range(Z.shape[0]):\n        counts = np.bincount(nbr_batches[i], minlength=B).astype(np.float32)\n        p = counts / max(np.sum(counts), 1.0)\n        with np.errstate(divide='ignore', invalid='ignore'):\n            plogp = np.where(p > 0, p * np.log(p), 0.0)\n        ent[i] = -np.sum(plogp)\n    s = ent / max_entropy  # normalize to [0,1]\n    return s.astype(np.float32)\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp:\
    \ float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\
    \"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
