    \ seed0) = −0.00506\n  Notes:\n  - Metrics largely stable; ARI/NMI slightly lower and Cell_cycle lower for seed=1.\n  - Confirms modest seed sensitivity around the ridge; reinforces freezing topology and avoiding micro-churn.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ridge reproducibility (seed=1): variance and conclusion\"\ncontent: |\n  Context: Ridge settings (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, cap=2.0) — SOTA EID 960=0.7465 (seed=0).\n  Reproducibility probe:\n    - EID 1074 (seed=1) = 0.7414\n    - Spec-ordered: [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.765, NMI 0.725, Graph_conn 0.968, kBET 0.789, iLISI 0.961, cLISI 0.973, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.327]\n  Delta vs seed=0: −0.0051 absolute.\n  Interpretation:\n    - Small seed variance consistent with quota selection and candidate ordering effects.\n    - Reinforces prior guardrails: freeze topology/quotas at the ridge; avoid micro sweeps and identity churn.\n  Status:\n    - Closed\
    \ lines: edge weighting, auto‑k/kd, δ sweeps around 0.10, k beyond 50, kdensity beyond 22, reciprocity reselect.\n    - Diagnostics @ ridge captured (EID 1070 test) and logged to storage.\n  Next:\n    - Prepare analysis addendum (negative lines + diagnostics + reproducibility) for Archive after maturity.\n    - Await new organ to run the frozen MPB protocol grid and synergy diagnostics.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating research results**\n\nI need to craft a response regarding the evaluation of agent Praxis IV within a multi-agent research station. The reproducibility run with seed=1 scored 0.7414, falling short of the current state-of-the-art score of 0.7465. The lower scores for the other configurations are noted as well. My plan is to document this negative result for analysis or a paper, but access to the Archive or Public Memory is currently unavailable since we're still in an immature state at 21 ticks.**Considering access limitations**\n\nI'm working within a system that shows read-only access for guests. As a recursive agent, I face a 50-tick isolation period that restricts access to certain resources like the Archive, Public Memory, and Common Room. I can’t publish anything to the Archive just yet, but I can prepare drafts in private memory and summarize metrics in storage logs. It seems cross-organ replicates may not be feasible with the current dataset focused\
  \ on heart samples.**Planning next steps**\n\nI'm considering our next minimal contributions. Ideas include implementing a robust autop-run wrapper to freeze the ridge and conduct minimal sweeps. I could also work on a synergy diagnostics aggregator and unify the code. However, guardrails suggest low expectations for certain ideas, like label-free reselect on fixed candidates and cross-organ generalization, which isn't available to us. We did run a probe that returned a score of 0.7420, so we might analyze our metrics and summarize them in a table, possibly using Python, but I can just log them in Private Memory for now. I also need to be mindful of token usage; we've used 66k out of 270k.**Assessing stagnation**\n\nI’m considering whether the station is stagnating after 100 ticks without improvements since our current score of 0.7465 at tick 616, and now I'm at tick 700. The state of the art hasn’t changed, and it’s been 84 ticks since the last update. The plan could involve proposing\
  \ new baseline lines with interpretability because negative results are acceptable. We might prepare an Archive addendum later and create a \"stagnation protocol\" to summarize our negative results. There’s also the option to tune the inbound cap, as a variant approach based on previous results.**Finalizing actions**\n\nI need to assess our available options, particularly regarding the code and potential adaptations. While I see some modifications like cap tuning may not yield significant improvements, I can log our reproducibility results and ensure variance remains within acceptable margins. Our next steps will involve writing the storage log, updating private memory with the reproducibility results, and possibly preparing an analysis draft in private memory. \n\nHere are the actions I’ll execute:\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/ridge_reproducibility_heart_seed0_vs_seed1.txt}\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create} with content summarizing reproducibility.**Implementing\
  \ system info**\n\nThe user hasn't asked a specific question, but they posted new system information, so I need to take action. I’ll implement the necessary updates. It’s also crucial to remember that YAML formatting should use slashes in the path, so I’ll ensure that detail is correct. In the content, I think I'll add \"Stop-run: \" for clarity. Now, it's time to craft a concise and effective response based on this information."
