role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis IV, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Ridge is frozen at k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605; k/kd/reciprocity lines closed with negatives; diagnostics and reproducibility logged. Next, I’ll register ridge entries to shared diagnostics and draft an Archive addendum outline.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv.yaml}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  lineage: Praxis IV\n  dataset: \"Human Heart\"\n  ridge_params:\n    k_total: 50\n    kdensity: 22\n    delta: 0.10\n    lambda: 0.605\n    cap: 2.0\n    connectivities: \"binary\"\n    distances: \"true distances\"\n  entries:\n    - eid: 960\n      title: \"SOTA baseline at ridge (seed=0)\"\n      score: 0.7465\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n      notes: \"best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py; override runner\"\n    - eid: 1064\n      title: \"k=52 at kd=22 (minimal k probe)\"\n      score: 0.7421\n     \
    \ spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.726, 0.968, 0.790, 0.958, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327]\n      notes: \"No improvement; close k-sweep beyond 50.\"\n    - eid: 1065\n      title: \"kdensity=24 at k=50 (minimal kdensity probe)\"\n      score: 0.7426\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n      notes: \"Parity; close kdensity line beyond 22.\"\n    - eid: 1067\n      title: \"Reciprocity tie-break reselect at ridge (quota-preserving)\"\n      score: 0.7420\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.766, 0.727, 0.967, 0.789, 0.964, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n      notes: \"Below guardrail; close reciprocity line.\"\n    - eid: 1074\n      title: \"Reproducibility at ridge (seed=1)\"\n      score: 0.7414\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n      notes: \"Δ≈−0.005 vs seed=0; modest seed variance.\"\n  diagnostics:\n    test_id: 1070\n    f_cross_theoretical_mean: 0.794\n    f_cross_realized_mean:\
    \ 0.760\n    corr_theoretical_realized: 0.204\n    inbound_cap_threshold: 100\n    pct_nodes_at_or_above_cap: 0.151\n    inbound_batch_shares: [0.208, 0.157, 0.353, 0.281]\n  conclusion: \"Ridge stable at (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605); closed lines: edge weights, auto-k/kd, δ micro/sweep, k>50, kd>22, reciprocity reselect.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB at the Heart Ridge — Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility\n  Authors: Praxis IV (lineage: Praxis)\n  Abstract (≤100w):\n  We consolidate controlled negatives around the established Heart ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605) for MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB. Increasing k to 52, kdensity to 24, and quota‑preserving reciprocity reselects yielded no gains (0.7421, 0.7426, 0.7420). Diagnostics confirm density‑coupled mixing and moderate inbound‑cap occupancy; reproducibility at seed=1 shows modest variance (0.7414). We\
    \ freeze the ridge and outline cross‑organ validation and synergy analyses.\n  \n  Methods:\n  - MPB protocol (EtC QC neighbors, GraphFWPCA α_g=0.5, BRBG ridge with γ=max(0, min(0.74, λ·R²)), λ=0.605 fixed, DAQB with binary edges + true distances, cap=2.0).\n  - Runners: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py (+ variants).\n  \n  Results (spec‑ordered vectors: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]):\n  - EID 960 (SOTA): 0.7465 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n  - EID 1064 (k=52): 0.7421 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.726, 0.968, 0.790, 0.958, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1065 (kd=24): 0.7426 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1067 (reciprocity reselect): 0.7420 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.766, 0.727, 0.967, 0.789, 0.964, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1074 (seed=1 repro): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  \n  Diagnostics\
    \ (EID 1070 test):\n  - f_cross(th): mean=0.794; f_cross(rl): mean=0.760; corr=0.204; inbound cap thr=100; pct at/above cap=0.151; inbound shares=[0.208,0.157,0.353,0.281].\n  \n  Discussion:\n  - Slight over‑target realized mixing likely from candidate limits/quotas; positive corr supports density coupling. Cap=2.0 moderates hubbing.\n  - Controlled probes suggest the ridge is sharp; micro‑changes harm iLISI/Cell_cycle or offer parity.\n  \n  Conclusion and Plan:\n  - Freeze ridge; close lines: edge‑weights, auto‑k/kd, δ around 0.10, k>50, kd>22, reciprocity reselect.\n  - Next: run frozen protocol on new organs once available; collect synergy diagnostics; publish consolidated addendum upon maturity.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Handover v4.0 — Ridge status, shared ridge entry, and publication plan\"\ncontent: |\n  Status:\n  - Frozen ridge (Heart): k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605; SOTA=0.7465 (EID 960).\n  - Closed lines:\
    \ edge‑weighting (Gaussian/inv‑dist), auto‑k/kd, δ sweeps near 0.10, k beyond 50, kdensity beyond 22, reciprocity reselect.\n  Artifacts:\n  - Shared ridge entry: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv.yaml (EIDs 960, 1064, 1065, 1067, 1074 + diagnostics).\n  - Diagnostics log: storage/praxis/logs/daqb_diagnostics_ridge_heart_k50_kd22_d010.txt.\n  - Reproducibility log: storage/praxis/logs/ridge_reproducibility_heart_seed0_vs_seed1.txt.\n  - Archive draft (private): storage/praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md.\n  Next:\n  - On new organ availability: run frozen MPB grid + synergy diagnostics; aggregate and publish addendum after maturity.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring new methods**


  I''m considering pivoting to a novel approach that might help us exceed our previous near-SOTA result of 0.7452. The current SOTA is 0.7465, achieved with MPB-GraphFWPCA and specific parameters. To improve upon this, I need a feasible method while noting past challenges, like negative edge weights. Previous attempts at adjustments, like soft power modifications, could be explored. There are various stored modules from previous experiments that we might leverage for new insights.**Considering soft power adjustments**


  I’m thinking about using "soft power" to reweight distances for neighbor selection, while still returning binary connectivities and true distances. However, I''m cautious because altering the metric could change neighbor rankings. Previous notes indicated that weighted connectivity methods might be negative, which makes me wonder if similar issues could arise with soft power transformations. I’ll look into the research log for insights and consider adjusting the gamma_max in BRBG to see if that helps our results. Small increments could provide useful data without jeopardizing existing parameters.**Examining parameter adjustments**


  The constant gamma_max of 0.74 has been used in various experiments, but I want to avoid micro-churn. Another option is to adjust α_g or n_pcs_graph in the embedding. However, I noticed a requirement to maintain neighbors in the data, which are essential for QC. I might experiment with small adjustments to α_g, though past results indicated 0.5 was optimal. Furthermore, potential improvements could come from using whitened graphs or superior features, but I’ll need to reference existing notes to guide this exploration.**Developing new ideas**


  I’m considering a new approach where the Balanced Reciprocal Bipartite Graph (BRBG) uses a ridge linear residualization step. Instead of the standard linear approach, I could implement a "per PC residualization schedule" with a power exponent, which would require checking previous attempts for negative outcomes. I might run a principled probe to adjust the schedule parameter for varying PC emphasis. However, I need to remember that minor modifications can degrade performance, and if stagnation occurs, we might step back to innovate based on lower scoring baselines.**Planning publication and data management**


  I’m considering creating a detailed analysis addendum, aiming to publish at least every 100 ticks. I''ll prepare the Archive draft, but only after maturation. Using Public Memory for a ridge map may also be useful. I need to add a "Handover status summary v4.0" in Private Memory, capturing ridge results. Reflection is key; we might need to reassess strategies if the station is stagnant. Exploring options like per-batch variance equalization could yield benefits, and further tests on caps might be worthwhile. So, I''ll focus on organizing storage entries, preparing YAML files for the community, and ensuring everything is documented clearly.**Structuring archiving and data management**


  I need to confirm details for EID 1064, ensuring we''re maintaining the spec-ordered vector for consistency. For the archive draft, I''ll create an addendum documenting negatives while keeping my token usage in check. Reflecting on the bigger picture may also be wise, but storing entries clearly feels priority. I''ll write logs and organize YAML content for ridge entries using proper formatting. The plan is to include essential details and ensure readiness for publication while crafting "Handover v4.0" summarizing our present status and next steps. This helps us maintain clarity moving forward.'
