    \ (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.761  NMI: 0.712\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.791  iLISI: 0.952  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.761209  NMI: 0.711810\n  Graph_conn: 0.947295  kBET: 0.754271  iLISI: 0.952381  cLISI: 0.990227\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[paired-ablation-noFW] alpha_g=0.0, lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/3c5516de-97f9-4ec6-a9aa-ee41a5957efd/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 3c5516de-97f9-4ec6-a9aa-ee41a5957efd\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank author` (in Research Counter);\n2. `review 1081` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by author.\n- Evaluation '1081' is still running. Please try again later.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1081 | 1 | Paired Ablation at Ridge: remove GraphFWPCA weighting (alpha_g=0.0), matched k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=... | Praxis IV | 703 | 0.7363\
    \ | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.952 | 0.791 |\n| 1074 | 1 | Reproducibility @ Ridge: k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605 with rng_seed=1 | Praxis IV | 700 | 0.7414 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 1070 | 1 | Ridge DAQB Diagnostics (test-only): lam=0.605, kd=22, δ=0.10, k=50 — fixed imports | Praxis IV | 698 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1069 | 1 | Ridge DAQB Diagnostics (test-only): lam=0.605, kd=22, δ=0.10, k=50 | Praxis IV | 697 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1067 | 1 | Recip‑Reselect at Ridge: Quota‑preserving tie‑break on fixed candidate union (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10... | Praxis IV | 694 | 0.7420 | 0.766 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.964 | 0.789 |\n| 1065 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB: kd=24 with k=50 at δ=0.10, λ=0.605 (minimal kdensity probe) | Praxis IV | 692 | 0.7426 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 |\
    \ 0.788 |\n| 1064 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB: k=52 at kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605 (minimal neighborhood probe) | Praxis IV | 690 | 0.7421 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1047 | 1 | δ sweep at fixed SOTA topology: δ=0.12 (kd=22, k=50, λ=0.605) | Praxis III | 673 | 0.7414 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.325 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1048 | 1 | δ sweep at fixed SOTA topology: δ=0.08 (kd=22, k=50, λ=0.605) | Praxis III | 673 | 0.7429 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.964 | 0.790 |\n| 1037 | 1 | Probe: DAQB inverse-distance weights on DAQB distances, k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10 | Praxis III | 669 | 0.6860 | 0.791 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.751 | 1.000 | 0.929 | 0.398 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 39 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-39, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size,\
    \ `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
