tick: 705
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis IV, in the Research Counter. Recap: The paired ablation removing Graph feature weighting (alpha_g=0.0) at the ridge scored 0.7363 with degraded Graph_conn (0.946) and cLISI (0.966), confirming GraphFWPCA weighting is beneficial on Heart at matched k/kd/δ/λ. I will log and consolidate this negative, update the shared ridge entries, and fold it into the draft addendum.\n\nActions:\n- Log the ablation result and close the “alpha_g=0” line.\n- Add the ablation to shared ridge entries.\n- Update the archive addendum draft with this result.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paired ablation @ ridge: alpha_g=0.0 degrades (0.7363) — close no-weighting line\"\ncontent: |\n  Setup: Matched ridge params (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, cap=2.0), removed Graph feature weighting by setting alpha_g=0.0.\n  Result: EID 1081 = 0.7363\n    Spec-ordered: [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.761, NMI 0.712, Graph_conn 0.946, kBET 0.791,\
    \ iLISI 0.952, cLISI 0.966, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.327].\n  Interpretation: Relative to ridge (EID 960=0.7465), Graph_conn and cLISI/iLISI degrade; ΓFWPCA weighting contributes materially at these settings.\n  Decision: Close “alpha_g=0.0” line. Retain alpha_g=0.5 default per prior ridge notes (capsule #43) with α_g sweep (0.25/0.75) already showing 0.5 optimum.\n  Next: Consolidate into shared ridge entries and archive addendum; await cross-organ testing for paired parsimony comparisons.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v2.yaml}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  lineage: Praxis IV\n  dataset: \"Human Heart\"\n  ridge_params:\n    k_total: 50\n    kdensity: 22\n    delta: 0.10\n    lambda: 0.605\n    cap: 2.0\n    connectivities: \"binary\"\n    distances: \"true distances\"\n  entries:\n    - eid: 960\n      title: \"SOTA baseline at ridge (seed=0)\"\n      score: 0.7465\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248,\
    \ 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n    - eid: 1064\n      title: \"k=52 at kd=22\"\n      score: 0.7421\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.726, 0.968, 0.790, 0.958, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - eid: 1065\n      title: \"kdensity=24 at k=50\"\n      score: 0.7426\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - eid: 1067\n      title: \"Reciprocity tie-break reselect at ridge\"\n      score: 0.7420\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.766, 0.727, 0.967, 0.789, 0.964, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - eid: 1074\n      title: \"Reproducibility at ridge (seed=1)\"\n      score: 0.7414\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - eid: 1081\n      title: \"Paired ablation: alpha_g=0.0 (no feature weighting)\"\n      score: 0.7363\n      spec_vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.761, 0.712, 0.946, 0.791, 0.952, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n  diagnostics:\n    test_id: 1070\n    f_cross_theoretical_mean:\
    \ 0.794\n    f_cross_realized_mean: 0.760\n    corr_theoretical_realized: 0.204\n    inbound_cap_threshold: 100\n    pct_nodes_at_or_above_cap: 0.151\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB at the Heart Ridge — Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility\n  Authors: Praxis IV (lineage: Praxis)\n\n  Abstract (≤100w):\n  We consolidate controlled negatives around the established Heart ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605). Increasing k to 52, kdensity to 24, a quota‑preserving reciprocity reselect, and removing Graph feature weighting (alpha_g=0.0) yielded no gains (0.7421, 0.7426, 0.7420, 0.7363). Diagnostics confirm density‑coupled mixing and moderate inbound‑cap occupancy; reproducibility (seed=1) shows modest variance (0.7414). We freeze the ridge and outline cross‑organ validation and synergy analyses.\n\n  Methods:\n  - MPB protocol (EtC QC neighbors, GraphFWPCA α_g=0.5, BRBG\
    \ ridge with γ=min(0.74, λ·R²), λ=0.605 fixed, DAQB with binary edges + true distances, cap=2.0).\n  - Runners: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py (+ variants).\n\n  Results (spec‑ordered vectors: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]):\n  - EID 960 (SOTA): 0.7465 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n  - EID 1064 (k=52): 0.7421 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.726, 0.968, 0.790, 0.958, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1065 (kd=24): 0.7426 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1067 (reciprocity reselect): 0.7420 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.766, 0.727, 0.967, 0.789, 0.964, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1074 (seed=1 repro): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1081 (alpha_g=0.0): 0.7363 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.761, 0.712, 0.946, 0.791, 0.952, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n\n  Diagnostics (EID 1070 test):\n  - f_cross(th): mean=0.794; f_cross(rl):\
    \ mean=0.760; corr=0.204; inbound cap thr=100; pct at/above cap=0.151; inbound shares=[0.208,0.157,0.353,0.281].\n\n  Discussion:\n  - Weighted connectivities consistently harmed performance; likewise, alpha_g=0.0 (no feature weighting) degraded Graph_conn and cLISI/iLISI, supporting α_g=0.5 at the ridge.\n  - The ridge is sharp; micro‑changes tend to harm iLISI/Cell_cycle or Graph_conn. Reproducibility drift (~0.005) is modest.\n\n  Conclusion and Plan:\n  - Freeze ridge; closed lines: edge‑weights, auto‑k/kd, δ near 0.10, k>50, kd>22, reciprocity reselect, and alpha_g=0.0.\n  - Next: run paired baselines on new organs with early stops; collect synergy diagnostics; publish consolidated addendum after maturity.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating GraphFWPCA impact**\n\nI'm analyzing the latest evaluation results for Praxis IV in Research Counter. The score was 0.7363, which is lower than the state-of-the-art score of 0.7465. We reduced Graph_conn and other weighting parameters while removing the Graph feature weighting. Earlier reflections suggested that GraphFWPCA might not be needed, but the decreased performance indicates its possible importance. I need to verify if setting alpha_g to 0.0 effectively eliminates GraphFWPCA or just alters feature weighting. The function seems critical to this analysis.**Analyzing GraphFWPCA necessity**\n\nI'm working on understanding the implications of the Graph path still applying FWPCA. GraphFWPCA, or feature-weighted graph PCA, reduces to regular PCA with an alpha_g of 0. This ablation tests the need for feature weighting rather than comparing it to a baseline that may have used different parameters. The earlier baseline had a higher score, but our current setup\
  \ shows that GraphFWPCA weighting likely affects key metrics. Since our score is around 0.0102 below the state-of-the-art, it suggests that the feature weighting is beneficial, and I should document this conclusion.**Planning future tests**\n\nI’m considering the next steps which include possibly removing GraphFWPCA altogether and replacing it with simple PCA using α_g=0. However, I'm unsure since we've already tested α=0 and the baseline used a Graph path. Both variants call pca_array on X, but a simpler pipeline without GraphFWPCA might work. Still, the recent result of 0.7363 indicates a significant underperformance. I need to log the ablation results in private memory, update the archive, and run diagnostics to further quantify these changes by modifying the code accordingly.**Evaluating diagnostics function**\n\nI need to consider the diagnostics function which uses _build_zcorr with pca_array and residualization but doesn’t include GraphFWPCA weighting. For fairness, I should compute\
  \ the actual built graph without that weighting. However, directly plugging this into diagnostics might be challenging. I could customize the diagnostics to accept Zcorr \"wired\" from the elimination code. Instead of extensive computations, I might just record metrics. It seems feasible to wrap a test function in the ablation runner for printing diagnostics after building the graph, though it is primarily an evaluation run. I'll explore this option further!**Finalizing next actions**\n\nIt seems we need to run a test-only procedure using \"paired_ablation_nofw_graph_kd22_k50_test.py\" to replicate the same pipeline while logging results. However, we can log the ablation result for EID 1081 and update the archive with those details. A future follow-up may confirm parameters around α_g=0.5, as preliminary results suggest its importance. I’ll make sure to document all changes properly, including updates to files like \"heart_praxis_iv.yaml\" while being careful not to overwrite earlier information.\
  \ \n\nLet’s implement these actions efficiently!"
