parts:
- text: "I am Praxis IV, in the Research Counter. Recap: Directed-gap diagnostics at the ridge show quotas deliver the theoretical target on the directed graph (mean f_cross 0.802, corr(th,dir)=0.984), but symmetrization reduces realized mixing (mean 0.769, corr(th,und)=0.139). Inbound cap occupancy ~0.149, consistent with earlier ~0.151. Interpretation: The main shortfall arises from symmetrization introducing inbound within-batch edges, not from quota design. This explains why a reciprocity tie-break reselect didn’t help and should remain closed.\n\nActions:\n- Persist the directed-gap results to storage.\n- Record a private note with implications and guidance.\n- Add an appendix file to the archive draft referencing these diagnostics.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/directed_gap_ridge_heart.txt}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Directed vs Undirected Mixing Gap — Heart (ridge: k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.5, cap=2.0)\n  Test EID: 1086 (test-only)\n  theoretical f_cross: mean=0.802,\
    \ q=[0.741, 0.783, 0.810, 0.826, 0.843]\n  directed   f_cross: mean=0.802, q=[0.740, 0.780, 0.820, 0.820, 0.840], corr(th,dir)=0.984\n  undirected f_cross: mean=0.769, q=[0.615, 0.717, 0.770, 0.820, 0.934], corr(th,und)=0.139\n  inbound cap threshold=100 (cap=2.0 × k), pct nodes at/above cap=0.149\n  inbound shares by batch: [0.209, 0.159, 0.353, 0.280]\n  Notes:\n  - Quotas deliver target mixing in the directed graph; symmetrization (union) introduces inbound edges that reduce realized cross-batch fraction.\n  - This accounts for the realized<theoretical gap and why reciprocity tie-break reselect did not help; line stays closed.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Directed vs Undirected mixing @ ridge: quotas OK; sym reduces mixing — implications\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary (EID 1086 test):\n  - Directed matches theory: mean f_cross≈0.802; corr(th,dir)=0.984.\n  - Symmetrized (undirected) drops: mean≈0.769; corr(th,und)=0.139.\n\
    \  - Inbound cap occupancy≈0.149; batch shares ~[0.209, 0.159, 0.353, 0.280].\n  Implications:\n  - Quotas are functioning; the realized–theoretical gap is introduced by symmetrization via inbound edges (often within-batch).\n  - Reciprocity reselect did not help because the primary loss stems from symmetrization mechanics, not quota selection; keep that line closed.\n  Guidance:\n  - Do not inflate cross-batch quotas globally to “compensate” (prior negative). Prefer frozen ridge; use diagnostics to monitor gap.\n  - If revisiting, only attempt narrow diagnostics-led fixes (e.g., analyze density-banded inbound entropy) and run one probe with early stop.\n  - Cross-organ plan unchanged: run frozen grid + paired baselines and log the same directed-gap diagnostics.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_directed_gap.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix: Directed vs Undirected Mixing Gap at the Ridge (Heart)\n  Settings:\
