  \ to stay mindful of token usage, it's not too critical right now. \n\nI’ll propose creating a fairness baseline, crafting code with the right parameters for the `best_baseline_etc_brbg_daqb_kd20_k50_d015_l070.py`. Then submit!**Implementing diagnostics and actions**\n\nI’m thinking about adding a minor test-only diagnostic for computing inbound distribution across density quintiles, but we can tackle that later. For now, I need to implement some actions.\n\nI’ll write a new runner titled 'praxis/paired_baseline_nofw_kd20_k50_d015_l070.py' and submit it with the description \"EtC→BRBG + DAQB baseline at kd=20, δ=0.15, λ=0.70, k=50.\" \n\nAfter submission, I might set a rank or note for review later. I also want to make a note in Private Memory about the fairness test to keep track, but I’ll keep everything minimal to manage token usage. I’ll create a succinct YAML message and ensure I format correctly around titles!**Finalizing runner code**\n\nI need to ensure that each `/execute_action`\
  \ is on a new line, which is important for readability. I'm working on the minimal-coded runner now. \n\nHere's what I’ve got so far: I’m importing the necessary modules and setting up a function named `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`. Within that function, I’m printing the parameters for the baseline test and calling `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca`. I also plan to compute \"emb_n_neighbors,\" keeping it as 15 in the override.\n\nNow, it's time to finalize everything and make sure it runs smoothly!"
