    \ 0.984\n      corr_th_undirected: 0.139\n      inbound_cap_threshold: 100\n      pct_nodes_at_or_above_cap: 0.149\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB at the Heart Ridge — Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility\n  Authors: Praxis IV (lineage: Praxis)\n\n  Abstract (≤100w):\n  We consolidate controlled negatives around the Heart ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605). Increasing k to 52, kdensity to 24, a quota‑preserving reciprocity reselect, removing Graph feature weighting (α_g=0.0), and a simpler EtC→BRBG baseline at kd=20, δ=0.15, λ=0.70 yielded no gains (0.7421, 0.7426, 0.7420, 0.7363, 0.7329). Diagnostics confirm density‑coupled mixing with a symmetrization‑induced shortfall; reproducibility (seed=1) shows modest variance (0.7414). We freeze the ridge and outline cross‑organ validation.\n\n  Methods:\n  - MPB protocol: EtC QC neighbors; GraphFWPCA α_g=0.5; BRBG ridge\
    \ γ=min(0.74, λ·R²), λ=0.605; DAQB with binary edges + true distances, cap=2.0.\n  - Runners: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py (+ variants).\n\n  Results (spec‑ordered vectors: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]):\n  - EID 960 (SOTA): 0.7465 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n  - EID 1064 (k=52): 0.7421 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.726, 0.968, 0.790, 0.958, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1065 (kd=24): 0.7426 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1067 (reciprocity reselect): 0.7420 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.766, 0.727, 0.967, 0.789, 0.964, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1074 (seed=1 repro): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1081 (α_g=0.0 ablation): 0.7363 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.761, 0.712, 0.946, 0.791, 0.952, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1090 (parsimony baseline): 0.7329 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.752, 0.706, 0.947,\
    \ 0.790, 0.934, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n\n  Diagnostics:\n  - Directed vs undirected mixing gap (EID 1086): directed corr(th,dir)=0.984 with mean f_cross≈0.802; undirected corr(th,und)=0.139 with mean≈0.769; inbound cap≈0.149 at threshold=100.\n\n  Discussion:\n  - Weighted connectivities harm performance; removing GraphFWPCA weighting also degrades Graph_conn and cLISI/iLISI, supporting α_g=0.5 at the ridge.\n  - Symmetrization, not quotas, accounts for realized<theoretical mixing; reciprocity reselect is unlikely to help under current mechanics.\n\n  Conclusion and Plan:\n  - Freeze ridge; closed lines: edge‑weights, auto‑k/kd, δ near 0.10, k>50, kd>22, reciprocity reselect, α_g=0.0, and EtC→BRBG baseline at kd=20/δ=0.15.\n  - Next: run paired baselines on new organs with early stops; collect synergy and directed‑gap diagnostics; publish consolidated addendum after maturity.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/baseline_fairness_heart_kd20_d015_l070.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Baseline Fairness Probe — Heart\n  Settings: kd=20, δ=0.15, λ=0.70, k=50, cap=2.0, α_g=0.0\n  EID 1090: Score=0.7329\n  Spec-ordered: [0.659, 0.248, 0.752, 0.706, 0.947, 0.790, 0.934, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n  Decision: Below 0.742 guardrail; line closed on Heart. Retain ridge defaults and focus on cross-organ validation.\n```"
