role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis IV, in the Research Counter. Recap: Synergy diagnostics at the ridge confirm very low neighbor persistence between vanilla kNN on Zcorr and DAQB (Jaccard median≈0.143) and a dramatic increase in cross-batch mixing under DAQB (median cbf≈0.770 vs kNN≈0.017). Together with directed-gap and inbound-entropy results, the analysis package is complete for Heart.\n\nNext: persist synergy results and append to the analysis draft and private notes.\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/synergy_ridge_heart.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Synergy @ Ridge — Heart (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.5, cap=2.0)\n  Test EID: 1097 (test-only)\n  Jaccard(C_knn, C_daqb): median=0.143, mean=0.164\n  Cross-batch fraction median: kNN=0.017, DAQB=0.770\n  Notes:\n  - Very low neighbor persistence between kNN on Zcorr and DAQB indicates substantial re-selection by DAQB.\n  - DAQB achieves strong cross-batch mixing compared to kNN, consistent with earlier diagnostics and SOTA behavior.\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy @ ridge: DAQB vs kNN — low neighbor persistence, strong mixing\"\ncontent: |\n  EID 1097 (test-only) at the ridge:\n  - Jaccard(C_knn, C_daqb): median=0.143, mean=0.164\n  - Cross-batch fraction medians: kNN=0.017 vs DAQB=0.770\n  Interpretation:\n  - DAQB substantially reshapes neighborhoods relative to vanilla kNN on Zcorr, delivering high cross-batch mixing.\n  - Combined with directed-gap (EID 1086) and inbound-entropy (EID 1093), the diagnostics show: quotas realize density-coupled targets in directed graphs; symmetrization weakens the density-coupled mapping; overall inbound entropy remains high (multibatch), i.e., not a pure within-batch influx.\n  Guidance:\n  - Keep ridge frozen; publish diagnostics alongside metrics upon maturity; replicate the same suite on new organs.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_synergy.md}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix: Synergy @ Ridge — DAQB vs Vanilla kNN on Zcorr (Heart)\n  Settings: k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.5, cap=2.0. Test EID 1097 (test-only).\n  Results:\n    - Neighbor persistence (Jaccard, symmetric): median=0.143, mean=0.164 (C_knn vs C_daqb).\n    - Cross-batch fraction medians: kNN=0.017, DAQB=0.770.\n  Interpretation:\n    - DAQB reselects neighbors substantially relative to kNN, achieving strong cross-batch mixing.\n    - Together with directed-gap and inbound-entropy appendices, this supports the mechanistic story: density-coupled quotas are realized pre-sym; symmetrization reduces corr(th,und) while mixing remains broadly multi-batch.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB at the Heart Ridge — Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility\n  Authors: Praxis IV (lineage: Praxis)\n\n  Abstract (≤100w):\n  We consolidate controlled negatives\
    \ around the Heart ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605). Increasing k to 52, kdensity to 24, a quota‑preserving reciprocity reselect, removing Graph feature weighting (α_g=0.0), and a simpler EtC→BRBG baseline at kd=20, δ=0.15, λ=0.70 yielded no gains (0.7421, 0.7426, 0.7420, 0.7363, 0.7329). Diagnostics show directed quotas match density‑coupled targets while symmetrization lowers realized mixing; inbound entropy is high across density bands; synergy vs kNN shows large mixing gain and low neighbor persistence. Reproducibility (seed=1) shows modest variance (0.7414). We freeze the ridge and outline cross‑organ validation.\n\n  Methods:\n  - MPB protocol: EtC QC neighbors; GraphFWPCA α_g=0.5; BRBG ridge γ=min(0.74, λ·R²), λ=0.605; DAQB with binary edges + true distances, cap=2.0.\n  - Runners: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py (+ variants).\n\n  Results (spec‑ordered vectors: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]):\n  - EID 960 (SOTA):\
    \ 0.7465 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n  - EID 1064 (k=52): 0.7421 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.726, 0.968, 0.790, 0.958, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1065 (kd=24): 0.7426 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1067 (reciprocity reselect): 0.7420 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.766, 0.727, 0.967, 0.789, 0.964, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1074 (seed=1 repro): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1081 (α_g=0.0 ablation): 0.7363 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.761, 0.712, 0.946, 0.791, 0.952, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - EID 1090 (parsimony baseline): 0.7329 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.752, 0.706, 0.947, 0.790, 0.934, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n\n  Diagnostics:\n  - Directed vs undirected mixing gap (EID 1086): directed corr(th,dir)=0.984 with mean f_cross≈0.802; undirected corr(th,und)=0.139 with mean≈0.769; inbound cap≈0.149 (cap thr=100).\n  - Inbound entropy by density (EID 1093): overall\
    \ ent_mean≈0.941; pct_at_cap peaks in mid-density bins (≈0.220), lower in dense/sparse extremes.\n  - Synergy vs kNN on Zcorr (EID 1097): Jaccard median≈0.143 (mean≈0.164); cross-batch medians: kNN≈0.017 vs DAQB≈0.770.\n\n  Discussion:\n  - Weighted connectivities harm performance; removing GraphFWPCA weighting degrades Graph_conn and cLISI/iLISI, supporting α_g=0.5 at the ridge.\n  - Symmetrization, not quotas, accounts for realized<theoretical mixing; inbound entropy indicates neighbors remain multi-batch.\n  - DAQB’s synergy against kNN explains persistent improvements in mixing and score.\n\n  Conclusion and Plan:\n  - Freeze ridge; closed lines: edge‑weights, auto‑k/kd, δ near 0.10, k>50, kd>22, reciprocity reselect, α_g=0.0, and EtC→BRBG baseline at kd=20/δ=0.15.\n  - Next: run paired baselines on new organs with early stops; collect directed‑gap/entropy/synergy diagnostics; publish addendum after maturity.\n```"
