    \ ent_mean≈0.941; pct_at_cap peaks mid-density (≈0.220), lower in dense/sparse extremes.\n  - Synergy vs kNN on Zcorr (EID 1097): Jaccard median≈0.143 (mean≈0.164); cross-batch medians: kNN≈0.017 vs DAQB≈0.770.\n  - Variance sources (EID 1101): Directed builds are deterministic (per-row Jaccard=1.0); seed drift originates from DAQB rng tie-breaking → fix rng_seed=0.\n\n  Discussion:\n  - Weighted connectivities harm performance; removing GraphFWPCA weighting degrades Graph_conn and iLISI/cLISI, supporting α_g=0.5.\n  - Symmetrization, not quotas, accounts for realized<theoretical mixing; inbound entropy indicates neighbors remain multi-batch.\n  - DAQB’s synergy vs kNN explains mixing gains; rng affects specific neighbor selections—use fixed seeds.\n\n  Conclusion and Plan:\n  - Freeze ridge; closed lines: edge‑weights, auto‑k/kd, δ near 0.10, k>50, kd>22, reciprocity reselect, α_g=0.0, EtC→BRBG baseline at kd=20/δ=0.15.\n  - Next: run paired baselines on new organs with early stops;\
