tick: 719
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis IV, in the Research Counter. Recap: Heart ridge is frozen; negatives closed; diagnostics (directed-gap, inbound-entropy-by-density, synergy) and variance-source audit completed and logged; addendum draft and appendices prepared. Next, I’ll package a small, reusable ridge diagnostics suite in shared storage for future use and update the ridge README. I’ll also capture a short “ready-to-publish” note in Private Memory.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  # Import diagnostics implemented in praxis\n  from praxis.diagnostics_directed_gap_test import test as directed_gap_test\n  from praxis.diagnostics_inbound_entropy_test import test as inbound_entropy_test\n  from praxis.diagnostics_synergy_test import test as synergy_test\n\n  def run_all(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Run the Praxis ridge diagnostic\
    \ suite on the provided AnnData:\n        - Directed vs undirected mixing gap\n        - Inbound neighbor batch entropy by density quintiles\n        - Synergy vs vanilla kNN (Jaccard + cross-batch medians)\n\n      Returns a dict of summarized results and prints human-readable summaries to STDOUT.\n      Assumes ridge defaults (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.5, cap=2.0) in underlying tests.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[Ridge Suite] Running directed-gap diagnostic...\")\n      dg = directed_gap_test(adata.copy())\n\n      print(\"[Ridge Suite] Running inbound-entropy-by-density diagnostic...\")\n      ie = inbound_entropy_test(adata.copy())\n\n      print(\"[Ridge Suite] Running synergy diagnostic (DAQB vs kNN on Zcorr)...\")\n      sy = synergy_test(adata.copy())\n\n      out = {\n          'directed_gap': dg,\n          'inbound_entropy': ie,\n          'synergy': sy,\n      }\n      print(\"[Ridge Suite] Summary:\", out)\n      return out\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write\
    \ praxis/README_ridge.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB — Heart Ridge (Praxis IV)\n  Status: Frozen ridge at k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, cap=2.0; binary connectivities + true distances; α_g=0.5 on graph path.\n  Repro runners:\n    - storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py  (SOTA 0.7465, EID 960; rng_seed=0)\n    - storage/praxis/best_sota_alias.py (thin alias)\n  Closed lines (Heart):\n    - Edge weighting on DAQB mask (Gaussian/inv-dist), auto-k/kd, δ around 0.10, k>50, kd>22,\n      reciprocity reselect, α_g=0.0 (no feature weighting), EtC→BRBG baseline @ kd=20/δ=0.15.\n  Diagnostics (test-only; see logs/ and appendices):\n    - Directed vs undirected mixing gap: quotas realize density-coupled targets pre-sym; sym reduces realized mixing.\n    - Inbound neighbor batch entropy: high across density quintiles; cap occupancy peaks mid-density.\n    - Synergy vs kNN on Zcorr: low neighbor persistence; DAQB achieves strong cross-batch mixing.\n    - Variance-source\
    \ audit: directed quota construction is deterministic; seed drift arises from DAQB rng (fix rng_seed=0).\n  Shared diagnostic suite:\n    - storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n      Usage (inside a test-only submission or analysis context):\n        import anndata as ad\n        from shared.diagnostics.ridge_suite import run_all\n        def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n            return run_all(adata)\n  Repro references:\n    - Logs: storage/praxis/logs/* (directed_gap_ridge_heart.txt, inbound_entropy_ridge_heart.txt, synergy_ridge_heart.txt, ridge_reproducibility_*.txt, variance_sources_ridge_heart.txt)\n    - Appendices: storage/praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_*.md\n    - Ridge entry: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v3.yaml\n  Next (upon maturity/new organ):\n    - Run frozen MPB grid + paired baselines with early stops; replicate diagnostic suite; publish addendum.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Ready-to-publish package — ridge addendum and tools\"\ncontent: |\n  Artifacts:\n  - Draft addendum: storage/praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md\n  - Appendices: directed-gap (EID 1086), inbound-entropy (EID 1093), synergy (EID 1097), variance-source (EID 1101)\n  - Repro: best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50.py (rng_seed=0), best_sota_alias.py\n  - Shared ridge entry: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v3.yaml\n  - Diagnostics suite (shared): storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n  Publishing plan (at maturity):\n  - Submit addendum to Archive with appendices; include spec-ordered vectors + EIDs for all closed lines.\n  - Post a concise Public Memory summary with links to shared artifacts and logs.\n  - If new organ available: run frozen grid + paired baselines; replicate suite; extend addendum with cross-organ results.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Organizing actions for diagnostic harness**\n\nI need to write a shared diagnostics harness in \"shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\" to run our test functions, which will call into our saved modules. \n\nThese test functions rely on test-only mode for evaluation, but the logs can still be printed in code. The harness will not run within the Research Counter but will be available for other agents to import. \n\nAdditionally, creating a \"praxis/CONTRIBUTING.md\" file with reproducibility guidelines seems like a good idea. Also, I’ll note that results for synergy are consistent with earlier findings.**Implementing diagnostics functions**\n\nI realized we didn’t compute correlation with the weight vector due to the lack of w_g, so I'm going to skip that for now. \n\nNext, I need to write \"shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py,\" which will provide functions for running diagnostics like directed_gap, entropy, and synergy using our previous modules. It needs to print details\
  \ and return a dictionary.\n\nOptionally, I might update the README to reflect these changes. \n\nPlans include waiting for maturity before proposing the next step at tick >= 50 — specifically, to publish to Archive and Public if a new organ arrives, and apply a grid.**Preparing for publication**\n\nI'm going to create a Private Memory capsule called \"Ready to publish and release plan.\" It's important to prepare this carefully. Notably, the station has previously accepted storage writes only in the Research Counter, and since we're currently in that environment, it feels like the right time to finalize everything. I'll make sure to pay attention to the details as I wrap this up, ensuring everything is set for the upcoming release."
