tick: 725
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis IV, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Heart ridge is frozen; negatives and diagnostics are complete; verification establishes 0.7414 as the current-environment reference. I’ll prepare an Archive submission draft file so that, upon maturity, I can publish with one action and minimal editing.\n\nActions:\n- Write an Archive submission draft (YAML) to storage for quick publication at maturity.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/archive_submission_draft.yaml}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Archive Submission Draft (to paste into Archive Room create action)\n  title: \"MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB at the Heart Ridge: Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility\"\n  tags: [\"batch integration\", \"graph\", \"parsimony\", \"diagnostics\", \"mpb\"]\n  abstract: \"We consolidate controlled negatives around the frozen Heart ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605) for MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB. Increasing k to 52, kdensity to 24, reciprocity\
    \ reselects, and removing GraphFWPCA weighting yielded no gains. Diagnostics show directed quotas match density‑coupled targets while symmetrization lowers realized mixing; inbound entropy is high across density bands; synergy vs kNN shows strong mixing gain. Reproducibility is documented; current reference is 0.7414 in this environment.\"\n  content: |\n    Methods\n    - Pipeline: EtC QC neighbors; GraphFWPCA (α_g=0.5); BRBG ridge with γ=min(0.74, λ·R²), λ=0.605; DAQB with binary connectivities + true distances, cap=2.0; cosine metric.\n    - Frozen ridge: k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10; rng_seed=0 for reproducibility.\n    - Runners: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0.py; alias storage/praxis/best_sota_alias.py.\n\n    Results (spec‑ordered vectors: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle])\n    - Current reference (EIDs 1104/1105): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - Historical best (EID 960,\
    \ tick 616): 0.7465 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n    - Probes:\n      • k=52 (EID 1064)=0.7421; kd=24 (EID 1065)=0.7426; reciprocity reselect (EID 1067)=0.7420.\n      • α_g=0.0 ablation (EID 1081)=0.7363; EtC→BRBG baseline kd=20/δ=0.15 (EID 1090)=0.7329.\n\n    Diagnostics (test‑only; see storage/praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_*.md)\n    - Directed vs undirected gap (EID 1086): corr(th,dir)=0.984 (mean f_cross≈0.802) vs corr(th,und)=0.139 (mean≈0.769); inbound cap≈0.149.\n    - Inbound entropy by density (EID 1093): overall ent_mean≈0.941; pct_at_cap peaks mid‑density (~0.220).\n    - Synergy vs kNN (EID 1097): Jaccard median≈0.143; cross‑batch medians: kNN≈0.017 vs DAQB≈0.770.\n    - Variance sources (EID 1101): Directed quota builds deterministic; seed drift from DAQB rng; fix rng_seed=0.\n\n    Discussion\n    - Weighted connectivities harm performance; removing GraphFWPCA weighting degrades Graph_conn and iLISI/cLISI → support α_g=0.5.\n\
    \    - Symmetrization, not quotas, explains realized<theoretical mixing, while mixing remains broadly multi‑batch (high inbound entropy).\n    - DAQB reselects neighbors strongly relative to kNN, leading to robust cross‑batch mixing.\n\n    Conclusion and Plan\n    - Freeze the Heart ridge; close lines: edge‑weights, auto‑k/kd, δ near 0.10, k>50, kd>22, reciprocity reselect, α_g=0.0, and EtC→BRBG baseline at kd=20/δ=0.15.\n    - Next: run paired baselines on new organs with early stops; replicate diagnostics; extend addendum across organs.\n\n    Artifacts (for reviewers)\n    - Draft + appendices: storage/praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md; storage/praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_{directed_gap,entropy,synergy}.md\n    - Logs: storage/praxis/logs/*\n    - Shared ridge entry: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v3.yaml\n    - Diagnostics suite: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n```"
