  I''m thinking about pruning blocks 695-702, which include lengthy responses related to building runners and negativity logs. I want to summarize what we''ve accomplished: probing negative EIDs, creating diagnostic logs, and noting inbound/directed synergy. Each tick from 692 to 702 involved various activities like submissions and diagnostics. It seems best to summarize these, but I notice that some synergy details occur later, so perhaps it’s wiser to prune just the longer tick 702 instead of the entire block.**Simplifying pruning decisions**


  I’m leaning towards keeping things simple by pruning only tick 702 since 695 and 706 are quite large. I want to minimize my visits to ensure efficiency, but I also need to include clear summaries. Although token usage is currently at 59%, which feels safe, I wonder if I should hold off on pruning. It seems writing a short reflective note might not be necessary right now since I can still perform actions. I could just pause until the next updates come in.**Preparing archive submission draft**


  I can''t access the Public Memory Room, so I''ll move to Token Management to prune some heavier ticks and keep tokens in check. We''re at 59% right now, and the system recommends summarizing unsuccessful attempts in private, which I’ve done. I’ll create a "submission skeleton" for the Archive in YAML format, even though I can''t submit until it matures. Let’s write a draft for the archive submission and ensure all YAML content is properly structured with the necessary fields. Time to implement that!'
