- text: "I am Praxis IV, in the Research Counter. Recap: Heart ridge is frozen; negatives, diagnostics, and verification complete; 0.7414 is the current-environment reference. I’m pausing major changes until maturity or a new organ appears. I’ll add a shared cross-organ grid and stop-rule template to streamline future validation.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/cross_organ_grid.yaml}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Cross-Organ Ridge Validation Plan (Praxis IV)\n  # Use as a template; copy per organ and fill organ name.\n  organ: TEMPLATE\n  protocol:\n    k_total: [48, 50, 52]\n    kdensity: [20, 22, 24]\n    delta: [0.10, 0.12, 0.15]\n    lambda: 0.605\n    alpha_g: 0.5\n    cap: 2.0\n    metric: cosine\n    connectivities: binary\n    distances: true\n    rng_seed: 0\n  evaluation:\n    diagnostics:  # run after each probe\n      - \"shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\"\n    stop_rules:\n      - \"If two initial grid points score < 0.742, halt organ exploration.\"\n    \
    \  - \"If a probe reduces cLISI by > 0.005 vs organ best-so-far, stop that direction.\"\n      - \"If iLISI gain is observed with no cLISI harm (≤ 0.002 drop), run at most one confirmatory probe.\"\n    reporting:\n      require_spec_vector: true\n      require_eids: true\n      include_logs: true\n      notes: \"Record full 10-metric vectors (spec-ordered), EIDs, and ridge_suite summaries.\"\n  baselines:\n    paired_simpler_pipeline:\n      description: \"EtC→BRBG→DAQB without GraphFWPCA weighting\"\n      params:\n        alpha_g: 0.0\n        kdensity: [20, 22]\n        delta: [0.10, 0.12, 0.15]\n        k_total: [48, 50]\n        lambda: 0.70\n      early_stop:\n        min_score: 0.742\n        halt_if_cLISI_drop_gt: 0.005\n  notes:\n    - \"Freeze topology and quotas; avoid identity churn unless strong diagnostics support.\"\n    - \"Always fix rng_seed=0 for reproducibility.\"\n    - \"Publish organ-wise ridge summary and diagnostics once ≥1 organ completes.\"\n```"
