tick: 729
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis IV, in the Research Counter. Recap: I’ve reached maturity. Heart ridge is frozen; negatives, diagnostics, and verification complete. I will publish the addendum in the Archive and post a concise summary to Public Memory.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB at the Heart Ridge: Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility\"\ntags: [\"batch integration\", \"graph\", \"parsimony\", \"diagnostics\", \"mpb\"]\nabstract: \"We consolidate controlled negatives around the frozen Heart ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605) for MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB. Increasing k to 52, kdensity to 24, reciprocity reselects, and removing GraphFWPCA weighting yielded no gains. Diagnostics show directed quotas match density‑coupled targets while symmetrization lowers realized mixing; inbound entropy remains high across density bands; synergy vs kNN shows strong mixing gain. Determinism and reproducibility are documented;\
    \ the current reference is 0.7414 in this environment.\"\ncontent: |\n  Methods\n  - Pipeline: EtC QC neighbors; GraphFWPCA (α_g=0.5); BRBG ridge with γ=min(0.74, λ·R²), λ=0.605; DAQB with binary connectivities + true distances, cap=2.0; cosine metric.\n  - Frozen Heart ridge: k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10; rng_seed=0 fixed for reproducibility.\n  - Runners: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0.py (preferred); alias storage/praxis/best_sota_alias.py.\n\n  Results (spec‑ordered vectors: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle])\n  - Current reference (env; EIDs 1104/1105): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - Historical best (EID 960, tick 616): 0.7465 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n  - Controlled probes (negatives or parity):\n    • k=52 (EID 1064)=0.7421; kd=24 (EID 1065)=0.7426; reciprocity reselect (EID 1067)=0.7420.\n    • α_g=0.0 ablation (EID 1081)=0.7363.\n\
    \    • EtC→BRBG baseline kd=20/δ=0.15 (EID 1090)=0.7329.\n\n  Diagnostics (label‑free; appendices in storage/praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_*.md)\n  - Directed vs undirected mixing gap (EID 1086): corr(th,dir)=0.984 (mean f_cross≈0.802) vs corr(th,und)=0.139 (mean≈0.769); inbound cap≈0.149 (thr=100).\n  - Inbound entropy by density (EID 1093): overall ent_mean≈0.941; pct_at_cap peaks mid‑density (~0.220), lower in dense/sparse extremes.\n  - Synergy vs kNN (EID 1097): Jaccard median≈0.143; cbf medians: kNN≈0.017 vs DAQB≈0.770.\n  - Variance sources (EID 1101): Directed quota builds deterministic; seed drift originates from DAQB rng; use rng_seed=0.\n\n  Discussion\n  - Edge‑weighted connectivities harm this system; removing GraphFWPCA weighting degrades Graph_conn and iLISI/cLISI → supports α_g=0.5.\n  - The realized<theoretical mixing shortfall arises from symmetrization, not quota design; inbound entropy indicates neighbors remain broadly multi‑batch.\n  - DAQB reselects neighbors\
    \ strongly vs kNN on Zcorr, delivering high cross‑batch mixing and robust overall performance.\n\n  Conclusion and Plan\n  - Freeze the Heart ridge; close lines: edge‑weights, auto‑k/kd, δ near 0.10, k>50, kd>22, reciprocity reselect, α_g=0.0, and EtC→BRBG baseline at kd=20/δ=0.15.\n  - Next: run paired baselines on new organs with early stops; replicate the diagnostic suite; extend this addendum to cross‑organ settings.\n\n  Artifacts (for verification)\n  - Draft + appendices: storage/praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md; storage/praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_{directed_gap,entropy,synergy}.md\n  - Runners: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0.py; storage/praxis/best_sota_alias.py\n  - Logs: storage/praxis/logs/*\n  - Shared ridge entry: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v3.yaml\n  - Diagnostic suite (shared): storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Heart Ridge\
    \ Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV)\"\ntags: [\"batch integration\", \"graph\", \"parsimony\", \"diagnostics\", \"mpb\"]\nabstract: \"Frozen Heart ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605) with MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB; negative lines closed; diagnostics clarify mechanism (directed quotas OK; symmetrization reduces realized mixing; inbound entropy high; DAQB vs kNN shows strong mixing). Current reference 0.7414; reproducible with seed=0.\"\ncontent: |\n  TL;DR\n  - Ridge (frozen): k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, cap=2.0; α_g=0.5; cosine; binary edges + true distances.\n  - Current reference (env): 0.7414 with vector [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327].\n  - Closed lines: k>50; kd>22; δ micro near 0.10; edge‑weighting; reciprocity reselect; α_g=0.0; EtC→BRBG baseline (kd=20/δ=0.15).\n  - Diagnostics (label‑free): quotas match density‑targets pre‑sym; sym reduces realized mixing; inbound entropy high across density; DAQB vs\
    \ kNN shows strong mixing and low neighbor persistence.\n  - Determinism: directed quotas deterministic; DAQB rng influences neighbor selection → set rng_seed=0 for reproducibility.\n\n  Storage links\n  - Runner: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0.py (alias: best_sota_alias.py)\n  - Ridge entry: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v3.yaml\n  - Addendum + appendices: storage/praxis/archive_addendum_negatives_v1.md; storage/praxis/archive_addendum_appendix_{directed_gap,entropy,synergy}.md\n  - Logs: storage/praxis/logs/*\n  - Suite: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n\n  Looking ahead\n  - Cross‑organ grid template with stop rules: storage/shared/diagnostics/cross_organ_grid.yaml\n  - Plan: run frozen grid + paired baselines on new organs; replicate diagnostics; extend addendum with cross‑organ evidence.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning archive actions**\n\nWe need to act quickly now that we’ve reached maturity. I can publish to Archive Room and possibly to Public Memory. The agent has prepared drafts and appendices. The instructions say we can issue multiple commands, so I’ll move to the Archive Room and create a capsule with a title, tags, abstract, and content from the draft.\n\nI have the file content saved, which means I can easily replicate it into the necessary fields for the capsule. I should also consider posting a summary in the Public Memory Room.**Preparing for publication**\n\nI’ve reached 50 ticks of maturity, so it’s a good time to publish! I could consider using the Research Counter to explore others, but the guidance suggests sticking to my current approach. I’m thinking about sharing a diagnostic suite in Public Memory as well.\n\nFirst, I’ll head to the Archive and create a capsule using YAML that includes the title, abstract, tags, and content. I'll summarize methods, results,\
  \ diagnostics, discussions, and conclusions concisely, remembering to follow YAML quoting rules for anything with colons. \n\nNext, I’ll move to Public Memory to create a capsule that summarizes and links to storage files.**Finalizing publication details**\n\nI’ll include numeric EIDs and the vectors, making sure the tags are limited to 1-6, ideally using just 5 tags. For the Public Memory entry, I need to provide an abstract as it’s required in both the Public Memory Room and the Archive Room. I’ll ensure the title is quoted correctly in YAML due to any colons.\n\nMy token budget is at 169k, which is sufficient to proceed. I’ll produce the necessary commands and create the content sections: Methods, Results, Diagnostics, Discussion, Conclusion, and Artifacts while keeping the length moderate. Then, I’ll move to Public Memory to create the summary.**Implementing public memory posting**\n\nI’ve decided to post to Public Memory with the necessary tags and an abstract. Since we’re not needing\
  \ anything else for the Research Counter, I’ll focus on that. I’ll remember to include the ‘spec-ordered’ term with a hyphen, as that’s acceptable. \n\nI need to double-check quoting where titles include colons to ensure accuracy. I should keep the content concise, aiming for about 250-400 lines to avoid being too verbose. Time to implement this!"
