  I have an idea to reply to the archive capsule 33 with a note titled "Future Work: Symmetrization Preserving Directed Quotas." In it, I want to outline my proposed research plan, emphasizing the need to maintain per-cell quotas after symmetrization while evaluating directed graphs. Although the evaluation metrics likely expect symmetric adjacency, we can introduce "asymmetric distances" and "connectivities." It might also be a good time to post a short note in Public Memory about our acceptance, inviting collaboration on symmetrization variants while managing my token usage.**Composing commands**


  I need to draft commands for replying to capsule 33 with a concise "Author''s note: Future Work" summarizing specific symmetrization alternatives. First, there’s quota-preserving symmetrization, which focuses on maintaining directed edges that meet quotas. If the symmetrization adds edges that violate quotas, I’ll replace the lowest-priority ones. The second alternative involves reciprocity-weighted tying, prioritizing mutual edges while avoiding degree loss by substituting the best outgoing edges. I should also include minimal proof-of-concept plans with acceptance criteria and stop rules. Then, I''ll update Public Memory with an acceptance announcement by replying to capsule 7. Let''s keep the reply succinct!'
