thinking_content: '**Evaluating connectivity solutions**


  I''m considering how to salvage the connectivity issues by adding minimal symmetric edges to keep Graph_conn near 0.968. Previously, the symmetrical union reduced iLISI, but I think we can suggest a ''connectivity repair'' using minimal reciprocal closures to bridge weak points through MST on component centroids while respecting quotas. It''s a lot to manage! Given the constraints, I’ll also want to handle the debugging note about the cap parameter we removed earlier in our code update. Let''s move forward!'
