parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 33}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Author’s Addendum — Batch‑Aware Feature Weighting × GraphFWPCA (BAFW) at the Heart Ridge\n  We evaluated a batch‑aware per‑gene weighting scheme w_g = (1 − R²_batch(g))^β, where R²_batch(g) is variance explained by a ridge regression of gene g on batch one‑hots. We multiply these weights with GraphFWPCA’s variance weights before the graph‑path PCA, keeping the rest of the ridge pipeline unchanged (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50, seed=0; env v4.1; graphs used as‑is).\n\n  Results (spec‑ordered 10‑metric vectors):\n  - β=0.50 (EID 1132) Score=0.7423 →\n    [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.763, NMI 0.718, Graph_conn 0.985, kBET 0.790, iLISI 0.959, cLISI 0.973, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.327]\n    Notes: +0.0009 over reference 0.7414; Graph_conn↑ with cLISI preserved; small ARI/NMI↓.\n  - β=0.25 (EID 1134) Score=0.7393 →\n    [0.659, 0.248, 0.771, 0.724, 0.967, 0.789, 0.960, 0.973, 1.000, 0.302]\n\
    \    Notes: Overall ↓; Graph_conn↓; Cell_cycle↓.\n  - β=0.75 (EID 1135) Score=0.7408 →\n    [0.659, 0.248, 0.755, 0.714, 0.985, 0.789, 0.959, 0.973, 1.000, 0.326]\n    Notes: Overall ↓; Graph_conn strong but ARI/NMI lower.\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - BAFW×GraphFWPCA (β=0.50) yields a modest, non‑robust gain and stronger Graph_conn with cLISI preserved. We record β=0.50 as an auxiliary variant; the ridge remains frozen at the original settings pending a clearly robust improvement.\n  - Closed BAFW lines: β=0.25 and β=0.75 (negative). All results are logged in storage/praxis/logs/* and reflected in the ridge entry (v4) with env metadata (evaluator_version=v4.1, baseline_hash=85c3db9e).\n  - Future work: If a new organ is released, we will replicate BAFW β=0.50 alongside the frozen ridge and report cross‑organ behavior under the shared diagnostics suite.\n```"
