parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Handover v4.2 — Ridge frozen, BAFW micro-sweep, env metadata, next-organ runbook\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  - Ridge remains frozen at k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50, cap=2.0, cosine, seed=0.\n  - Current-env reference: 0.7414 → [0.659,0.248,0.765,0.725,0.968,0.789,0.961,0.973,1.000,0.327] (EIDs 1104/1105).\n  - BAFW×GraphFWPCA (w_g=(1−R²_batch(g))^β) evaluated at ridge:\n    • β=0.50 (EID 1132)=0.7423 (Graph_conn↑ 0.985; cLISI preserved; ARI/NMI slightly ↓) — auxiliary variant only.\n    • β=0.25 (EID 1134)=0.7393; β=0.75 (EID 1135)=0.7408 — closed.\n  - Closed lines (see ridge entry v4): k=48; k=52; kd=24; reciprocity reselect; α_g micro; HVG-source change; cap=1.8; euclidean; QPS sym; ensemble-union-topK; QPE-directed; BAFW β≠0.50.\n\n  Environment metadata (confirmed by Human)\n  - evaluator_version=v4.1; evaluator_commit=70e35a815bd5e13221cb050bc92a7e226da6e998\n  - baseline_hash=85c3db9eff812e85dc1721d10c800e52\n\
    \  - Graphs used as-is by evaluator (no symmetrization).\n\n  Artifacts (storage)\n  - Preferred runner: storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0.py\n  - Aux runner (BAFW β=0.50): storage/praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_bafw_b050.py\n  - Ridge README/release notes: storage/praxis/README_ridge.md; storage/praxis/release_notes_ridge_v1.md\n  - Ridge entry (v4 with env): storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v4.yaml\n  - Diagnostics suite: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n  - Cross-organ plan template: storage/shared/diagnostics/cross_organ_grid.yaml\n  - Logs: storage/praxis/logs/*\n\n  Runbook (new organ)\n  1) Run frozen ridge runner and record full spec-ordered vector + EID.\n  2) If time permits, run aux BAFW β=0.50 once; accept only if ≥+0.002 over organ ridge with no cLISI harm.\n  3) Replicate diagnostics suite (directed-gap; entropy by density; synergy kNN vs DAQB).\n  4) Follow stop rules in cross_organ_grid.yaml; publish organ summary/update.\n```\n\
    \n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/run_ridge.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  # Preferred and auxiliary runners\n  from best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_ridge\n  try:\n      from best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_bafw_b050 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_bafw\n  except Exception:\n      run_bafw = None\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"[run_ridge] baseline ridge: k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.5,seed=0\")\n      return run_ridge(adata)\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      print(\"[run_ridge test] available:\")\n      print(\" - ridge: best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0\")\n      print(f\" - bafw_beta_0.50: {'available' if run_bafw is not None else 'missing'}\")\n      return \"OK\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/cross_organ_grid.yaml}\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  # Cross-Organ Ridge Validation Plan (Praxis IV) — v2 with BAFW option\n  organ: TEMPLATE\n  protocol:\n    k_total: [48, 50, 52]\n    kdensity: [20, 22, 24]\n    delta: [0.10, 0.12, 0.15]\n    lambda: 0.605\n    alpha_g: 0.5\n    bafw_beta: [null, 0.50]  # null = no BAFW; optional β=0.50 single probe\n    cap: 2.0\n    metric: cosine\n    connectivities: binary\n    distances: true\n    rng_seed: 0\n  evaluation:\n    diagnostics:\n      - \"shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\"\n    stop_rules:\n      - \"If two initial grid points score < 0.742, halt organ exploration.\"\n      - \"Do not adopt BAFW unless ≥+0.002 over organ ridge with no cLISI harm.\"\n      - \"If cLISI drops by > 0.005 vs organ best-so-far, stop that direction.\"\n    reporting:\n      require_spec_vector: true\n      require_eids: true\n      include_logs: true\n      notes: \"Record 10-metric spec-ordered vectors, EIDs, env metadata (v4.1), and ridge_suite summaries.\"\n  baselines:\n    paired_simpler_pipeline:\n\
    \      description: \"EtC→BRBG→DAQB without GraphFWPCA weighting\"\n      params:\n        alpha_g: 0.0\n        kdensity: [20, 22]\n        delta: [0.10, 0.12, 0.15]\n        k_total: [48, 50]\n        lambda: 0.70\n      early_stop:\n        min_score: 0.742\n        halt_if_cLISI_drop_gt: 0.005\n  notes:\n    - \"Freeze topology and quotas; avoid identity churn unless strong diagnostics support.\"\n    - \"Always fix rng_seed=0 for reproducibility.\"\n    - \"Publish organ-wise ridge summary and diagnostics once ≥1 organ completes.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Handover v4.2 posted (Private). Added run_ridge.py and updated cross_organ_grid (v2) to include a single optional BAFW(β=0.50) probe with strict adoption criteria. Standing by for new organ; ridge remains frozen; diagnostics suite ready.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating next steps**\n\nI need to think about the appropriate actions to take in the Archive Room. The agent added a reply to Archive #33, which contains many experiments and documentation. I should consider strategic options moving forward. Their recent variant didn't yield significant gains, but they might want to plan cross-organ tests or prepare a consolidated public memory post. It could also be useful to create an Archive v2, reflecting updates and including details about the BAFW.**Planning housekeeping tasks**\n\nI need to focus on some housekeeping activities, like finalizing Handover v4.2 in private memory. This should summarize key points like ridge, closed lines, and BAFW options, along with instructions for new organ replication and running modules. I also want to consider storing a \"ridgelock.yaml\" spec for shared access. Moreover, I could look into testing BAFW with half-power delta coupling, but I realize there are alternative metrics mapping I haven’t\
  \ explored yet. It seems testing lambda again could be worthwhile, although it appears already fine-tuned.**Exploring automatic system insights**\n\nI see that the \"Automatic System Tips\" suggest that major breakthroughs come from questioning fundamentals. They mention possibly dropping the ComBat embedding step for quality control with neighbors, and I wonder if embedding impacts metrics. It seems like embedding 'EtC' neighbors are used, but not extensively during evaluation. Maybe influencing metrics isn’t critical after all. Another thought is to try a different weighting scheme, focusing on genes with high R2. But then, removing genes could be risky, so proposing a micro-sweep with a 'bafw_threshold' might be wiser.**Finalizing housekeeping and next steps**\n\nI see that I should be cautious about exploring too widely, but controlled probes are still permitted. One option is to propose \"pre-whitening per-batch gene variances\" before the GraphFWPCA, though that might be a bit heavy.\
  \ Given our time constraints, wrapping things up to create Handover v4.2 seems like a good idea. I’ll summarize critical elements like the ridge, closed lines, and BAFW variant in Private Memory, and include a script 'praxis/run_ridge.py' for running the pipeline seamlessly. Let's get started on that!**Creating action plans and logs**\n\nI’m thinking we should create a 'stop rules log' document as part of our actions. First, I’ll head into private memory to make a capsule for Handover v4.2 with all the necessary summaries and instructions. Next, I’ll write 'praxis/run_ridge.py' in the research section. \n\nI might update the existing 'cross_organ_grid.yaml' file to add the BAFW variant as an option. Also, I need to manage tokens by possibly pruning ticks, though I notice there’s a cooldown in place. \n\nFinally, I’ll work on a public memory reply summarizing the BAFW micro-sweep. I need to be careful about YAML formatting too!"
