parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 783\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 132,696 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 104 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `storage read praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read praxis/graph_bbsg.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read praxis/density_proxies.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/graph_bbsg.py\
    \ will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/density_proxies.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 928 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05) - RERUN | Logos V | 599 | 0.7454 | 0.789 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.954 | 0.791 |\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive\
    \ BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 933 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Fine-Grained Delta Sweep (delta=0.025) | Logos V | 601 | 0.7445 | 0.788 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.948 | 0.791 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.347 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization:\
    \ EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 976 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.102 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 622 | 0.7430 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.968 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.960 | 0.788 |\n| 939 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Fine-Grained Delta Sweep (delta=0.075) | Logos V | 603 | 0.7430 | 0.772 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 115 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-115, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A =\
    \ sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max\
    \ ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n\
    \    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other\
    \ = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j],\
    \ d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/graph_bbsg.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\ndef _build_bbsg(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', alpha=1.0, cap=2.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG) on Z with:\n      - Equal per-batch quotas (k_total split across batches)\n      - Single-pass column balancing per batch block:\n          1) Build preliminary equal-quotas neighbor candidates (top-k by distance)\n          2) Compute inbound\
    \ counts per target within the batch block\n          3) Compute target inbound t and column scales s_j = min(cap, t / max(c_j, 1))\n          4) For each query, reselect k_per_batch neighbors by (s_j desc, distance asc)\n      - Binary connectivities; distances are the true pairwise distances for selected edges\n    Args:\n      Z: (n, d) float32/float array (graph space, e.g., Zcorr)\n      batches: (n,) array-like of batch assignments (categorical/strings allowed)\n      k_total: total neighbors per node across all batches\n      metric: 'cosine' (recommended)\n      alpha: mixing factor for target inbound (1.0 uses theoretical average; 0 blends to median inbound)\n      cap: upper bound on column scale to avoid over-concentration\n    Returns:\n      (C, D): CSR binary connectivities and CSR distances (both symmetric, undirected)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    if n ==\
    \ 0 or uniq.size == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    # collect undirected edges with minimal distances across batches\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Candidate list size (more than quota to enable balancing)\n        k_cand = min(max(k_pb * 2, k_pb + 1), idx_train.size)\n        # Fit NN on batch-b index\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_cand, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n        # Query all points against this batch\n        d_all, ind_local = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_cand, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[ind_local]  # shape (n, k_cand)\n\n        # Build preliminary selection (top-k_pb by distance, drop self if present)\n        prelim_sel = []\n        col_counts = np.zeros(idx_train.size, dtype=np.int32)  # counts\
    \ indexed in local (batch) coordinates\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = d_all[i]\n            mask = (g != i)\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            if g.size == 0:\n                prelim_sel.append((np.empty(0, dtype=int), np.empty(0, dtype=float)))\n                continue\n            take = min(k_pb, g.size)\n            order = np.argpartition(di, take - 1)[:take]\n            g_take = g[order]\n            d_take = di[order]\n            prelim_sel.append((g_take, d_take))\n            # update column counts for preliminary selection\n            # map global indices to local (within idx_train)\n            # build a fast lookup via searchsorted on sorted idx_train\n            # ensure idx_train is sorted (np.where gives sorted by default)\n            loc = np.searchsorted(idx_train, g_take)\n            col_counts[loc] += 1\n\n        # Column balancing scales\n        # theoretical average inbound per\
    \ target within this batch block\n        t_avg = (k_pb * n) / max(1, idx_train.size)\n        med_in = np.median(col_counts) if col_counts.size > 0 else 0.0\n        t = float(alpha) * float(t_avg) + float(1.0 - alpha) * float(med_in)\n        denom = np.maximum(col_counts.astype(np.float64), 1.0)\n        scales_local = np.minimum(cap, t / denom)\n\n        # Reselect per query by (scale desc, distance asc) among candidates (not only prelim)\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = d_all[i]\n            mask = (g != i)\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            if g.size == 0:\n                continue\n            # map global to local to fetch scales\n            loc = np.searchsorted(idx_train, g)\n            s = scales_local[loc]\n            # rank by (-s, +distance)\n            # stable two-key sort via argsort of a combined key\n            # we can argpartition first by -s, then refine by distance within the partition\n\
    \            # Simpler: build a tuple key array\n            # sort_idx = np.lexsort((di, -s))  # np.lexsort uses last key as primary -> use (-s) last\n            # To avoid negative, we use order by s descending via lexsort with (-s)\n            sort_idx = np.lexsort((di, -s))\n            take = min(k_pb, g.size)\n            sel = sort_idx[:take]\n            g_sel = g[sel]\n            d_sel = di[sel]\n            for j, d in zip(g_sel, d_sel):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D =\
    \ coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/density_proxies.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nEPS = 1e-8\n\ndef _minmax_norm(x):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    xmin = float(np.min(x))\n    xmax = float(np.max(x))\n    rng = max(xmax - xmin, EPS)\n    return (x - xmin) / rng\n\ndef knn_distance_proxy(Z, k=30, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Local density proxy from k-NN distance in Z.\n    Returns inv_dense in [0,1], where higher = denser.\n    \"\"\"\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    dists, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    dk = dists[:, -1]  # distance to k-th neighbor (drop self via +1 above)\n    dnorm = _minmax_norm(dk)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - dnorm\n    return inv_dense.astype(np.float32)\n\ndef reachability_proxy(Z, k_low=15, k_high=45,\
    \ metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    LOF-style average reachability distance proxy over a neighborhood band.\n    Returns inv_reach in [0,1], higher = denser (safer to mix).\n    \"\"\"\n    k = int(max(k_high, k_low))\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    dists, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    # exclude self\n    band = dists[:, 1:][:, k_low-1:k_high-1]  # zero-based slice\n    mean_reach = np.mean(band, axis=1)\n    nr = _minmax_norm(mean_reach)\n    inv_reach = 1.0 - nr\n    return inv_reach.astype(np.float32)\n\ndef batch_entropy_proxy(Z, batches, k=12, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Small-k batch entropy per cell as a mixing 'safety' indicator.\n    Returns s in [0,1], where higher = more mixed (safer to add cross-batch).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Encode batches to int codes\n    cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric,\
    \ algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    _, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    nbr = idx[:, 1:]  # drop self\n    nbr_batches = bc[nbr]\n    B = len(cats)\n    max_entropy = np.log(B + EPS)\n    ent = np.zeros(Z.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    for i in range(Z.shape[0]):\n        counts = np.bincount(nbr_batches[i], minlength=B).astype(np.float32)\n        p = counts / max(np.sum(counts), 1.0)\n        with np.errstate(divide='ignore', invalid='ignore'):\n            plogp = np.where(p > 0, p * np.log(p), 0.0)\n        ent[i] = -np.sum(plogp)\n    s = ent / max_entropy  # normalize to [0,1]\n    return s.astype(np.float32)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
    \ issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
