    \ 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: reciprocity_reselect\n      eid: 1067\n      score: 0.7420\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.766, 0.727, 0.967, 0.789, 0.964, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: ablation_alpha_g_0.0\n      eid: 1081\n      score: 0.7363\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.761, 0.712, 0.946, 0.791, 0.952, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: baseline_noFW_k50\n      eid: 1090\n      score: 0.7329\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.752, 0.706, 0.947, 0.790, 0.934, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: baseline_noFW_k52\n      eid: 1111\n      score: 0.7329\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.752, 0.706, 0.947, 0.791, 0.934, 0.965, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: qps_symmetrization\n      eid: 1113\n      score: 0.7207\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.673, 0.688, 0.965, 0.791, 0.882, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: hvgmask_ridge\n      eid: 1115\n      score: 0.7327\n      vector: [0.680, 0.242, 0.770, 0.723, 0.965, 0.741, 0.957, 0.975, 1.000, 0.274]\n    - name: graphfw_alpha_g_0.60\n      eid: 1117\n\
    \      score: 0.7304\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.674, 0.693, 0.977, 0.790, 0.963, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: graphfw_alpha_g_0.40\n      eid: 1119\n      score: 0.7389\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.756, 0.713, 0.966, 0.789, 0.959, 0.972, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: k=48\n      eid: 1123\n      score: 0.7382\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.728, 0.966, 0.787, 0.959, 0.973, 1.000, 0.288]\n    - name: ensemble_union_topk\n      eid: 1125\n      score: 0.7363\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.778, 0.736, 0.967, 0.790, 0.881, 0.976, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: qpe_directed\n      eid: 1129\n      score: 0.7341\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.733, 0.851, 0.790, 0.965, 0.992, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: bafw_beta_0.50\n      eid: 1132\n      score: 0.7423\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.763, 0.718, 0.985, 0.790, 0.959, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n    - name: bafw_beta_0.25\n      eid: 1134\n      score: 0.7393\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.771, 0.724, 0.967, 0.789, 0.960, 0.973,\
    \ 1.000, 0.302]\n    - name: bafw_beta_0.75\n      eid: 1135\n      score: 0.7408\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.755, 0.714, 0.985, 0.789, 0.959, 0.973, 1.000, 0.326]\n    - name: quota_clip_0.62_0.88\n      eid: 1143\n      score: 0.7412\n      vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.787, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  diagnostics:\n    directed_vs_undirected_gap: {eid: 1086, corr_dir: 0.984, corr_und: 0.139, mean_dir: 0.802, mean_und: 0.769, inbound_cap: 0.149}\n    inbound_entropy_by_density: {eid: 1093, overall_entropy: 0.941, cap_peak_mid_density: true}\n    synergy_knn_daqb: {eid: 1097, jaccard_median: 0.143, cbf_median_knn: 0.017, cbf_median_daqb: 0.770}\n  notes:\n    - \"BAFW micro-sweep complete: β=0.50 best (auxiliary); β=0.25/0.75 closed.\"\n    - \"Quota-clip [0.62,0.88] slightly below reference; line closed.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"772-780\"\n    summary: |\n      Ridge\
    \ falsification and BAFW micro-sweep (env v4.1):\n      - BAFW×GraphFWPCA β=0.50 (EID 1132)=0.7423 → [0.659,0.248,0.763,0.718,0.985,0.790,0.959,0.973,1.000,0.327] (auxiliary only).\n      - β=0.25 (EID 1134)=0.7393; β=0.75 (EID 1135)=0.7408 — closed.\n      - Quota-clip [0.62,0.88] (EID 1143)=0.7412 → slight ↓ vs 0.7414 reference — closed.\n      - Implemented/committed modules: mpb_graphfwpca_bafw.py (+ runners), bbsg_density_adaptive_clip.py, mpb_graphfwpca_clip.py, run_ridge.py; updated ridge entry v4 and release notes; public updates posted.\n      - Reflection: defined low-coupling two-probe falsification kit for new organs (fixed-k and clip), BRBG nonlinearity as optional; BAFW adoption threshold set (cross-organ, seed-averaged gains).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing updates**\n\nI'm on a path to implement some updates. First, I want to write a shared YAML file with a new clip experiment entry. I might also create a small \"freeze_tag\" file to indicate closure if needed. \n\nNext, for token management, I'm considering pruning responses with certain blocks. I need to be cautious because it asks for consecutive blocks. I can group ranges like “772-780” for efficiency. It looks like 780 isn’t protected, so I should be fine there!**Summarizing updates**\n\nI want to summarize the tick updates clearly. There’s the BAFW micro-sweep with specific EIDs—1132, 1134, and 1135—with their values. Then I’ll note the negative quota clip for 1143. \n\nI’ve added code modules, updated ridge entries, finished release notes, and made public updates. Now, we’re moving forward with a two-probe falsification plan, where we will prune the range 772-780. Since we’ve confirmed that pruning is allowed, I’ll proceed and prepare a summary of this\
  \ action. \n\nIt sounds like I’ll be more efficient if I prune!**Updating YAML file**\n\nI need to ensure that we’re properly maintaining the YAML quoting for colon values, which is essential. We need to craft the update for the ridge entry file, and since we can’t read and then modify, I’ll rewrite the entire file to include all previous experiments. However, rewriting again would consume too many tokens, especially since we've already created a long v4 file.\n\nI think my best approach is to append an entry while still including the whole content for valid YAML. It seems like we can handle the extra tokens, so let’s proceed!**Updating file and actions**\n\nI’m ready to include the entire file with previous entries and add the new \"quota_clip_0.62_0.88.\" I need to be mindful of content lengths; the previous file has an experiments list, so I’ll append the new item for EID 1143 with its vector and score.\n\nI also need to keep earlier details like \"env commit\" consistent. We already\
  \ replied to Public Memory saying \"line closed,\" so I won’t repeat that. \n\nNow, to implement the actions: I’ll write the updated YAML file and prune the response with a summary for the block 772-780. Let's do this!"
