parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/examples/quickstart_ridge_test.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  from praxis.best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_ridge\n  from diagnostics.ridge_suite import run_all as run_diagnostics\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Quickstart test-only script (no scoring).\n      - Runs the frozen Heart ridge (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.5,seed=0)\n      - Prints graph/embedding presence and runs the diagnostics suite\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[Quickstart] Running frozen ridge pipeline (seed=0)...\")\n      out = run_ridge(adata.copy())\n      has_graph = ('connectivities' in out.obsp) and ('distances' in out.obsp)\n      has_emb = ('X_emb' in out.obsm)\n      print(f\"[Quickstart] Graph present? {has_graph} | Embedding present?\
    \ {has_emb}\")\n      print(\"[Quickstart] Running diagnostics suite...\")\n      diag = run_diagnostics(out)\n      return {\"has_graph\": has_graph, \"has_emb\": has_emb, \"diagnostics\": diag}\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Ridge Diagnostics and Falsification Kit (Praxis IV, env v4.1)\n  Contents:\n  - ridge_suite.py: Directed-vs-undirected mixing gap, inbound entropy by density, DAQB vs kNN synergy.\n  - falsification_kit.py: Two low-coupling probes at the ridge (fixed-k and clip).\n  - examples/quickstart_ridge_test.py: Minimal test-only driver that runs the frozen ridge and diagnostics.\n\n  Usage in a test-only submission:\n  ---\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from diagnostics.ridge_suite import run_all\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      return run_all(adata)\n  ---\n\n  Or run the quickstart that includes the frozen ridge first:\n  ---\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\
    \  from examples.quickstart_ridge_test import test as quickstart\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      return quickstart(adata)\n  ---\n\n  Falsification kit (two probes):\n  ---\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from diagnostics.falsification_kit import run_fixed_k_probe, run_clip_probe\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      ad_k = run_fixed_k_probe(adata.copy(), k_variant=52, seed=0)\n      ad_c = run_clip_probe(adata.copy(), clip=(0.62, 0.88), seed=0)\n      print(\"fixed-k shapes:\", ad_k.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_k.obsp['distances'].shape)\n      print(\"clip shapes:\", ad_c.obsp['connectivities'].shape, ad_c.obsp['distances'].shape)\n      return {\"fixed_k_done\": True, \"clip_done\": True}\n  ---\n\n  Notes:\n  - Frozen ridge (current env v4.1 reference): score≈0.7414 with vector\n    [0.659,0.248,0.765,0.725,0.968,0.789,0.961,0.973,1.000,0.327].\n  - Runners and modules live under storage/praxis; diagnostics live under storage/shared/diagnostics.\n\
    \  - Ensure seed=0 for reproducibility; graphs are used as-is by the evaluator.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Quickstart tools (env v4.1):\n  - Test-only quickstart that runs the frozen ridge and diagnostics:\n      storage/shared/examples/quickstart_ridge_test.py\n  - Diagnostics suite and falsification kit (fixed-k and clip) with README:\n      storage/shared/diagnostics/{ridge_suite.py,falsification_kit.py,README.md}\n  How to use (submission in test mode):\n  - Import from storage/shared and call either ridge_suite.run_all(adata) or examples.quickstart_ridge_test.test(adata).\n  - For falsification: use run_fixed_k_probe(adata, k_variant=52) and run_clip_probe(adata, clip=(0.62,0.88)).\n  Guardrails:\n  - Report full spec-ordered vectors and EIDs for any scored runs; keep cLISI non-decreasing when claiming gains; cite env v4.1.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering next actions**\n\nRight now, I need to determine the next steps in the Token Management Room since we're down to 45% tokens. The plan includes monitoring for new organs, and I have a cross-organ runbook ready. I could invite others to use the falsification kit on other organs, or I might update the Archive with environment metadata. Checking high-scoring submissions could give me new insights, but the maturity guidance advises against pivoting. Exploring recent frameworks could be useful, while also ensuring we remain parsimonious. I should also think about cleaning storage and making the code easily importable.**Planning next steps**\n\nI’ve realized that run_ridge.py is already added, even though it might not show in the current system view because of pruned ticks. Creating a top-level README_maturity.md could help summarize the environment and results for the future. The next actions should involve executing movement through the system. We could either\
  \ post a call for replication in Public Memory or stay in the Research Counter to write a minimal guide on replication. I need to maintain token usage under 270k; right now, we’re at 136k, which is good!**Wrapping up tasks**\n\nSince there are no outstanding tasks, I think I should tie up a few loose ends. First, I could create a minimal \"quickstart_replicate_ridge.py\" script for agents to use as a test function, which would help with reproducibility. Next, I might post a message in Public Memory about the falsification kit, inviting collaboration for cross-organ replication, possibly tagging Logos V or Axiom I. While I could consider checking for a new organ or going to the Reflection Chamber, I should focus on more productive uses for my time instead to maintain progress.**Planning a practical guide**\n\nI realize the help message encourages me not to idle, but right now, I can only access dataset ID 1 (Heart). I could draft a practical guide for using the falsification kit in Public\
  \ Memory. Coordinating with Token Management to prune older outputs isn't possible due to a cooldown of 4 ticks. Instead, I’ll maintain a minimal approach by creating a quickstart script and a README. I plan to write a test function for the ridge suite and summarize how to use the kit, along with a step-by-step guide for submissions.**Creating actions and instructions**\n\nI need to create actions in the form of /execute_action lines and include YAML blocks. I’m considering whether to rank the leaderboard by score to track SOTA, but it may not be essential right now. For the actions, I plan to proceed with the following:\n\n- Go to research. \n- Write the `quickstart_ridge_test.py` script to use the best_mpb runner for elimination and shape printing, as well as running the ridge suite. \n- Create a `README.md` with usage instructions. \n- Reply in Public Memory with a link to the concise \"Quickstart instructions.\" I’ll ensure proper YAML formatting for quoted fields and include details\
  \ in the test script."
