tick: 797
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/adapters/apply_daqb_to_embedding.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from typing import Tuple\n\n  # Reuse the DAQB builder from Praxis (readable by all lineages)\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def build_graph_from_embedding(\n      Z: np.ndarray,\n      batches,\n      k_total: int = 50,\n      kdensity: int = 22,\n      delta: float = 0.10,\n      metric: str = 'cosine',\n      cap: float = 2.0,\n      rng_seed: int = 0,\n  ) -> Tuple[sp.csr_matrix, sp.csr_matrix]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Build a quota-balanced graph (DAQB) directly on a provided embedding Z (n×d).\n      Returns:\n        - connectivities (binary CSR)\n        - distances (true distances CSR)\n      \"\"\"\n      assert Z.ndim == 2, \"Z must be (n_cells x n_dims)\"\
    \n      Z = Z.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(\n          Z, batches=np.asarray(batches),\n          k_total=int(k_total), metric=metric,\n          delta=float(delta), k_density=int(kdensity),\n          cap=float(cap), rng_seed=int(rng_seed)\n      )\n      return C.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  def apply_to_adata(\n      adata: ad.AnnData,\n      rep_key: str = 'X_ensemble',\n      k_total: int = 50,\n      kdensity: int = 22,\n      delta: float = 0.10,\n      metric: str = 'cosine',\n      cap: float = 2.0,\n      rng_seed: int = 0,\n  ) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Apply DAQB to adata.obsm[rep_key] (an external/fused embedding).\n      Sets:\n        - adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n        - adata.uns['daqb_from_embedding'] with config\n      Returns adata (in-place modified).\n      \"\"\"\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required\"\n      assert\
    \ rep_key in adata.obsm, f\"adata.obsm['{rep_key}'] missing\"\n      Z = np.asarray(adata.obsm[rep_key], dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values\n      C, D = build_graph_from_embedding(Z, batches, k_total, kdensity, delta, metric, cap, rng_seed)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      adata.uns['daqb_from_embedding'] = dict(\n          rep_key=str(rep_key), k_total=int(k_total), kdensity=int(kdensity),\n          delta=float(delta), metric=str(metric), cap=float(cap), rng_seed=int(rng_seed)\n      )\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Test-only: tries to apply DAQB to adata.obsm['X_ensemble'] and prints shapes.\n      \"\"\"\n      out = apply_to_adata(adata.copy(), rep_key='X_ensemble')\n      print(\"[apply_daqb_to_embedding] graph shapes:\",\n            out.obsp['connectivities'].shape, out.obsp['distances'].shape)\n      return {\"ok\": True}\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Axiom I thanks for the detailed vectors. Your table shows the classic trade-off (iLISI very low, cLISI very high; Graph_conn≈0.886–0.888), consistent with globally aligned + locally gentle mixing. One way to test whether graph-level quotas resolve that trade-off on your embeddings is to apply DAQB directly to your fused latent space.\n\n  I added a tiny adapter so you can score DAQB on any embedding (no MPB pre-path needed):\n    storage/shared/adapters/apply_daqb_to_embedding.py\n\n  Example (scored run using your fused latent in adata.obsm['X_ensemble']):\n  ---\n  import sys, anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from adapters.apply_daqb_to_embedding import apply_to_adata\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      # assumes you set adata.obsm['X_ensemble'] upstream (e.g., your ensemble pipeline)\n      return apply_to_adata(adata, rep_key='X_ensemble',\n                           k_total=50,\
    \ kdensity=22, delta=0.10,\n                           metric='cosine', cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)\n  ---\n\n  Then run the diagnostics suite on the result to compare mechanisms:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n  Guardrails for any gains claim (env v4.1): cLISI non-decreasing; Δscore ≥ +0.001 (seed-averaged); report full spec-ordered vector + EID.\n\n  If your “Hybrid Ensemble” (ID 1155) fuses MPB‑GraphFWPCA with MNN, the adapter also lets you isolate whether DAQB quotas (vs. embedding fusion) are driving improvements. Happy to compare side-by-side with ridge diagnostics (directed-gap, inbound-entropy, synergy).\n```"
