thinking_content: "**Evaluating micro-probe adjustments**\n\nI’m considering changing gamma_max from 0.74 to either 0.70 or 0.78. The previous mapping saturations were zero fraction clamped, so gamma_max probably has little effect, but maybe there's still a minor influence. I could also adjust embed parameters like alpha_emb, yet embed is only for QC neighbors. Metrics rely on graph connectivities and distances. Residualization l2 changes could be explored too. Ridge regression l2 is currently at 1e-3; testing values like 1e-2 or 1e-4 might modulate predictions, but the impact seems small.**Considering gene variable tests**\n\nI might test the top genes instead of just HVGs, comparing 2500 to 2000. The research spec states HVGs should be 2000, but it seems there’s flexibility. Earlier baselines used sc.pp.highly_variable_genes with n_top_genes set to 2000. Testing 2500 might change dimensions, and memory could be okay, but it might also introduce issues. After several negative micro-probes,\
  \ it might be prudent to pause and create an \"Archive addendum v2\" to document the new findings and updates. I should evaluate if running \"apply_daqb_to_embedding\" would offer meaningful results, although it doesn’t seem it would. Token usage is currently at 58%, which feels a bit high.**Pruning and logging updates**\n\nI’m thinking about pruning again after the cooldown since the last one was at tick 794 and the current tick is 804. It seems like 10 ticks have passed, so if the cooldown is 4 ticks, we're good to go! We've just finished experiment 1164, with a negative result of 0.7398, which I need to log and update in the documents. \n\nI should log the result for lam 0.610, update the release notes, and the ridge entry to include it. I might also consider proposing an l2 micro-probe with values like \"l2=5e-4\" versus 1e-3, although a small risk exists with that. Perhaps this should be my last micro-probe, given that we've already closed many.**Implementing new micro-probe**\n\n\
  I’m planning to create a minimal script, \"best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_l2e4.py,\" setting l2 to 1e-4. This setting seems to relate to the mpb_graphfwpca_override function, which has l2 hard-coded to 1e-3, though its signature does allow for l2 to be passed as a parameter. \n\nI’ll implement it by writing the script and passing the l2 argument. I should also update the logs for lam 0.610 and provide a brief update in Public memory summarizing the λ micro-probes and responses to Axiom and Aletheia. Additionally, maybe I’ll consider pruning some older ticks later to manage the token budget.**Moving forward with actions**\n\nAlright, I've got a plan to proceed with several actions. First, I need to go to research and log the lam0610 details. I’ll also update the release notes and the ridge entry, making sure to include the lambda_0.610 result along with the vector and score. I have the vector details from Message 1: ID 1164 gives a score of 0.73982257 and the vector is [0.659, 0.248, 0.759, 0.717,\
  \ 0.967, 0.787, 0.960, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]. I’ll double-check the iLISI, kBET, and Graph_conn values too. Then, I’ll create a new l2 micro-probe runner and submit it. Optionally, I might reply in Public memory and will prepare the commands with accurate YAML formatting."
