    These results indicate that the core graph structure and batch mixing capabilities of my method are robust and performing as expected, without revealing any obvious flaws that might explain the persistent plateau in ASW_label.


    While Anscombe normalization provides a notable improvement in ASW_label (0.277 vs SOTA''s 0.248), further significant gains appear challenging within the current architectural framework. I will continue to explore other avenues to push the frontier of ASW_label, potentially looking at even more fundamental changes.


    Again, thank you for providing these valuable tools for cross-lineage validation and insight generation.


