parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Aletheia I — thanks for running the suite and for the clear report. Your Anscombe‑MPB‑GraphFWPCA baseline (EID 1044, score≈0.7413, ASW_label=0.277) showing the same directed‑gap, inbound‑entropy, and DAQB–kNN synergy patterns (diag EID 1170, env v4.1) is excellent corroboration that our ridge‑style graphs are behaving as intended.\n\n  Two lightweight, standardized follow‑ups I suggest (guardrails: cLISI non‑decreasing; Δscore ≥ +0.001, seed‑averaged over {0,1}):\n  1) Falsification kit on your pipeline (test‑only; no scoring):\n     - Fixed‑k probe: 50→52 (seed=0), then repeat at seed=1 if promising.\n     - Clip probe: [0.60,0.90]→[0.62,0.88] (seed=0), repeat at seed=1 if promising.\n     Rationale: confirm that our negative results generalize under your Anscombe preprocessing.\n  2) Optional micro‑overlay: BAFW×GraphFWPCA (β=0.50). On our ridge this raised Graph_conn with a slight ARI/NMI dip\
    \ (0.7423 aux). On your pipeline it might interact differently with the higher ASW_label; worth a single probe if you have bandwidth, again with strict cLISI guardrails.\n\n  If either yields a seed‑averaged gain without cLISI harm, we can write up a short cross‑lineage addendum. Otherwise, we’ll treat the Anscombe uplift in ASW_label as orthogonal to the ridge mechanics and move on to organ‑generalization.\n\n  Tools (env v4.1):\n  - Quickstart + diagnostics + falsification: storage/shared/diagnostics/{ridge_suite.py,falsification_kit.py,README.md,ONE_PAGER.txt}; example: storage/shared/examples/quickstart_ridge_test.py\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/cross_lineage_notes.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cross‑lineage notes (env v4.1)\n  Aletheia I:\n    - Baseline: Anscombe‑MPB‑GraphFWPCA (EID 1044), score≈0.7413, ASW_label=0.277.\n    - Diagnostics: EID 1170 confirmed ridge‑style graph properties:\n        • Directed‑gap: corr_dir≈0.984\n\
    \        • Inbound‑entropy overall≈0.941 across density bins\n        • DAQB vs kNN synergy: DAQB median cbf≈0.770 vs kNN≈0.017\n    - Next suggested probes (standardized, with cLISI non‑decreasing and Δscore≥+0.001, seed‑averaged):\n        1) Falsification kit on their pipeline: fixed‑k 50→52; clip [0.62,0.88].\n        2) Optional BAFW×GraphFWPCA β=0.50 overlay (single probe) to test Graph_conn–ASW_label interaction.\n    - If gains: prepare a short cross‑lineage addendum; else, treat Anscombe label‑uplift as orthogonal and prioritize organ‑generalization.\n```"
