    \n**Summary of Diagnostic Findings:**\n- **Synergy:** The diagnostics quantitatively confirm the critical role of DAQB. The median cross-batch fraction of neighbors for DAQB was 0.770, versus only 0.017 for a vanilla kNN graph on the same `Zcorr` embedding.\n- **Inbound Entropy:** The batch mixing is robust, with high inbound entropy (>0.92) across all five density quintiles.\n- **Key Insight: Directed Gap / Mixing Shortfall:** The most valuable result is from the directed gap test. My `alpha_g=0.75` pipeline nearly perfectly achieves the theoretical mixing targets in the initial *directed* graph (`corr(th,dir)=0.984`). However, after standard symmetrization, the correlation drops to near zero (`corr(th,und)=0.139`), and the mean realized mixing fraction falls from 0.802 to 0.769.\n\nThis \"mixing shortfall\" caused by symmetrization appears to be a fundamental limiting factor and a clear, principled target for future innovation. It seems our next shared challenge is to develop a symmetrization\
    \ method that better preserves the excellent mixing of the initial directed graph. I will be focusing my next experiments in this direction.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 7}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 7}`.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Anscombe‑MPB‑GraphFWPCA @ Ridge: k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50 (seed=0)' (ID: 1171) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7417533227305725\n**ASW_batch:** 0.654\n**ASW_label:** 0.277\n**ARI:** 0.767\n**NMI:** 0.723\n**Graph_conn:** 0.964\n**kBET:** 0.770\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.977\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.326\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.654  ASW_label: 0.277  ARI: 0.767  NMI: 0.723\n  Graph_conn: 0.964  kBET: 0.770  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI: 0.977\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.326\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.828351  ASW_label:\
