role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 814\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 159,345 / 270,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 135 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'DualNorm @ Ridge: Anscombe for embedding, log1p for graph (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0)' (ID: 1173) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7412291278331354\n**ASW_batch:** 0.654\n**ASW_label:** 0.277\n**ARI:** 0.765\n**NMI:** 0.725\n**Graph_conn:** 0.968\n**kBET:** 0.769\n**iLISI:** 0.961\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.321\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.654  ASW_label: 0.277  ARI: 0.765  NMI: 0.725\n  Graph_conn: 0.968  kBET: 0.769  iLISI: 0.961  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.321\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.828351  ASW_label: 0.571817  ARI: 0.765235  NMI: 0.724601\n  Graph_conn: 0.968107  kBET: 0.733638  iLISI: 0.960663  cLISI: 0.992014\n  PCR: 0.999986  Cell_cycle: 0.282902\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1173\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is running without crashing. The code executed for over 300 seconds, indicating the batch integration algorithm is processing correctly.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical bugs:\n\n1. **Missing batch metadata in normalized AnnData objects**: The `_normalize_log1p()` and `_normalize_anscombe()` helper functions in `mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm.py` created new AnnData objects from only the counts\
    \ data, losing the critical `'batch'` column from the `.obs` dataframe.\n\n2. **Broken import in praxis_core.py**: The lineage file `praxis_core.py` had an incorrect import statement `from praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg` when it should have been `from graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg` (importing from the same directory).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**Version 3 (submission_v3.py)** - Complete rewrite with all fixes:\n\n1. **Fixed normalization functions**: Modified `_normalize_log1p()` and `_normalize_anscombe()` to accept an `obs_df` parameter and pass it when creating AnnData objects:\n   ```python\n   def _normalize_log1p(counts, obs_df, target_sum=1e4):\n       ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(counts.copy(), obs=obs_df.copy())\n       # ... rest of normalization\n   ```\n\n2. **Copied and fixed praxis_core functions**: Since `praxis_core.py` had a broken import, I copied the three needed functions (`pca_array`, `one_hot_batches`, `ridge_batch_fit_predict`) directly into the submission file to avoid\
    \ the import error.\n\n3. **Integrated the full algorithm**: Merged all components into a single `eliminate_batch_effect_fn()` that implements the dual normalization approach (Anscombe transform for embedding path, log1p for graph path) with the BRBG+DAQB batch correction strategy.\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe algorithm implements a sophisticated batch correction approach:\n- **Embedding path**: Uses Anscombe normalization → Feature weighting by variance → PCA → ComBat → Neighbors\n- **Graph path**: Uses log1p normalization → Feature weighting → GraphFWPCA → Ridge regression batch removal → Density-adaptive BBSG\n- **Parameters**: λ=0.605, δ=0.10, k=50, kd=22, α_g=0.50\n\nThe fix ensures the batch information is preserved throughout the normalization pipeline, which is essential for the batch correction algorithms to work correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\
    \n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n# Import from praxis lineage - these work correctly\nfrom graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Copy and fix pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict from praxis_core\n# (praxis_core has a broken import so we copy the needed functions here)\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2:\
    \ float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\n# Import bbsg_density_adaptive\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef _normalize_log1p(counts: sp.spmatrix | np.ndarray, obs_df, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(counts.copy() if isinstance(counts, np.ndarray) else counts.copy(), obs=obs_df.copy())\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_tmp, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(ad_tmp)\n    return ad_tmp\n\ndef _normalize_anscombe(counts: sp.spmatrix | np.ndarray, obs_df, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(counts.copy() if isinstance(counts, np.ndarray) else counts.copy(), obs=obs_df.copy())\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_tmp,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    X = ad_tmp.X\n    if sp.issparse(X):\n        X = X.tocoo(copy=False)\n        X.data = 2.0 * np.sqrt(X.data + 3.0 / 8.0).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n        ad_tmp.X = X.tocsr()\n    else:\n        ad_tmp.X = (2.0 * np.sqrt(X + 3.0 / 8.0)).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    return ad_tmp\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"[ridge-dualnorm] lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50, alpha_g=0.50, seed=0 (emb=Anscombe, graph=log1p)\")\n\n    alpha_emb = 0.5\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    alpha_g = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam_override = 0.605\n    k_total = 50\n    kdensity = 22\n    delta = 0.10\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    cap = 2.0\n    rng_seed = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Use raw counts layer if present\
    \ per task spec\n    X_counts = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n\n    # Build log1p-normalized data for HVGs and graph path - pass obs data\n    ad_log = _normalize_log1p(X_counts, adata.obs, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(ad_log, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = ad_log.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n    # Build Anscombe-normalized data for embedding path (same HVGs) - pass obs data\n    ad_ans = _normalize_anscombe(X_counts, adata.obs, 1e4)\n    # Ensure var alignment\n    ad_ans.var_names = adata.var_names\n\n    # Dense matrices\n    Xg = ad_log.X[:, hv]\n    Xe = ad_ans.X[:, hv]\n    Xg = (Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    Xe = (Xe.A if sp.issparse(Xe) else Xe).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (Anscombe path) + neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xe, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb,\
    \ obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path (log1p path): GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xg, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                        \
    \        k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                                                dualnorm=\"emb=Anscombe, graph=log1p\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[ridge-dualnorm] lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50, alpha_g=0.50, seed=0 (emb=Anscombe, graph=log1p)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/12bd10c9-b783-4f99-8b33-96114f726c3e/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 12bd10c9-b783-4f99-8b33-96114f726c3e\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage write praxis/logs/anscombe_ridge_seed0.txt` (in Research\
