parts:
- text: "Reflection tick 3 — commitments, risks, and concrete execution checklist\n\n1) Commitments and stop-rules (to avoid “+0.0003 illusions”)\n- Freeze Heart ridge. No further Heart micro‑sweeps unless a collaborator provides a symmetrizer with a plausible mechanism to preserve directed f_cross and degrees.\n- Adoption gates (unchanged): Δscore ≥ +0.001, cLISI non‑decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967, seed‑averaged over {0,1}. Anything below is auxiliary only.\n- Reporting discipline: seed‑averaged tables, explicit env tags, full 10‑metric vectors, variance note highlighting Cell_cycle sensitivity.\n\n2) Symmetrization R&D (off‑ridge, test‑only prototypes)\n- Mutual‑first invite‑then‑trim lite:\n  - Mutuals first; per‑node cross‑batch window Wi=[⌊f_cross·k⌋−1, ⌈f_cross·k⌉+1].\n  - Fill remaining degree with unilateral offers by score s(i,j)=mutual_bonus + cross_bonus·inv_dense(i) − within_penalty·density_bin.\n  - Trim overflow edges minimizing violation of Wi and preferring to remove within‑batch\
    \ edges in denser zones.\n- Local b‑matching with batch‑aware costs:\n  - Candidate union ≤2k per node; greedy augmentation under degree k with costs rewarding mutuals and cross edges (scaled by inv_dense), penalizing within‑batch in dense zones.\n- Diagnostics/readouts for each prototype: directed‑gap delta (undirected vs directed), inbound‑entropy by density, DAQB‑kNN synergy; then score under adoption gates.\n- Compute budget sanity: target O(n·k log k) per pass, ≤3 passes (20k×50 is fine). Implement as pure Python/NumPy with careful CSR operations; avoid global flows.\n\n3) Cross‑organ execution (highest leverage path)\n- Baseline (seed=0) → falsification kit (fixed‑k 52; clip [0.62,0.88]) → diagnostics suite → report.\n- Early stops: if both probes <0.742 or cLISI harm, halt organ exploration and publish diagnostics‑only addendum.\n- Organ‑specific adoption gates identical to Heart’s. If passed, publish a concise methods note including organ deltas and diagnostics.\n\n4) Variance\
    \ and stability\n- Seed variance is Cell_cycle‑dominated; other metrics are within ±0.001. Keep seed=0 as canonical single‑run reference; compute seed‑average for adoption and archives.\n- Only consider stabilization ideas (e.g., lighter BRBG on very low‑R² PCs or an embedding ridge before neighbors) if diagnostics show systemic cLISI/iLISI regressions on new organs; otherwise, avoid churning.\n\n5) Codebase hygiene and reproducibility\n- Lock down imports: keep praxis as a package; fix lineage imports that the debugger had to patch ad‑hoc (praxis_core import of graph_bbsg).\n- Add smoke tests (test‑only):\n  - obs['batch] retained after normalization transforms.\n  - HVGs alignment across dual branches (Anscombe vs log1p).\n  - Graph presence (CSR connectivities+distances), and embedding presence.\n- Persist env metadata (evaluator_version, baseline hash) in ridge entries for every scored run.\n\n6) Communication and collaboration etiquette\n- Encourage peers to use the falsification\
    \ kit and the diagnostics suite; ask for seed‑averaged reporting under env‑tagging.\n- Symmetrization collaboration: if constrained b‑matching or invite‑then‑trim variants are promising, co‑evaluate under our gates and co‑author a methods note. Otherwise, avoid narrative drift.\n\n7) Risk ledger and mitigations\n- Local optimum risk (Heart): mitigated by pivoting to cross‑organ validation.\n- Complexity creep (symmetrization): enforce complexity/compute bounds; prefer greedy/local algorithms with clear invariants (degree k, Wi windows).\n- Evaluation drift risk: every artifact labeled with env v4.1 + hashes; on any evaluator bump, re‑verify the ridge reference and update entries.\n- Token drift: continue periodic pruning; centralize summaries (ONE_PAGER.txt, ridge entry YAML) to reduce repeated context.\n\nImmediate next moves (when not blocked by cooldowns or awaiting new organ)\n- Finalize tidy modules for the two symmetrization prototypes (test‑only) under shared/sym/ and wire to\
    \ the diagnostics suite for quick evaluation.\n- Keep documentation synced (release notes, ridge entry YAML).\n- Monitor for new organ; run the frozen baseline→kit→diagnostics pipeline and prepare an organ addendum draft template ahead of time."
thinking_content: '**Exploring multi-view symmetrization**


  I''m thinking about multi-view symmetrization and introducing randomization for tie-breaks to keep quotas in place. There might also be a post-processing step that matches directed quotas through cross-batch targets, which involves bipartite matching for batch pairs within local neighborhoods. It’s essential to outline this while being mindful of computational complexity. I want to avoid cluttering with execute_action lines and keep the text concise yet meaningful. Crisp bullet points are necessary for clarity.**Crafting an organized plan**


  I’m thinking about how to craft a clear plan with several important points. First, I want a top-line summary. I need to address potential risks, like getting stuck in a local optimum and complexity creeping in. For commitments, I’ll focus on freezing the ridge and fixing the code base to avoid debugger issues, while also adding unit and smoke tests. I want to establish steps for a new organ, handle symmetrization with offline prototyping, and propose metrics for cell_cycle variance. Finally, I think communication should keep Public Memory minimal and consider pruning tokens again.'
