parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/sym/sym_invite_trim.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # Invite-then-trim (quota-window) undirected symmetrizer\n  # Builds undirected graph from directed quota proposals while trying to preserve per-node cross-batch targets.\n  #\n  # Inputs:\n  #   Zcorr: (n, d) corrected embedding (float32)\n  #   batches: array-like length n (categorical) batch labels\n  #   k_total: degree per node (default 50)\n  #   kdensity: k for local density proxy (default 22)\n  #   delta: density coupling strength in f_cross (default 0.10)\n  #   metric: 'cosine' (recommended)\n  #   window: +/- allowance around target f_cross*k (default 1)\n  #\n  # Returns:\n  #   C, D: symmetric CSR matrices (binary connectivities, true distances)\n  #\n  def build_invite_then_trim(\n\
    \      Zcorr, batches, k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10,\n      metric='cosine', window=1\n  ):\n      n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n      B = len(cats)\n      B_other = max(B - 1, 1)\n\n      # Density proxy (k-th NN distance)\n      nn_d = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr)\n      d_all, _ = nn_d.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1].astype(np.float32)\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n\n      # Theoretical cross-batch fraction\n      base = (B - 1) / float(B)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta), 0.60, 0.90).astype(np.float32)\n      tgt_cross = np.round(f_cross * k_total).astype(np.int32)\n      lo_cross = np.maximum(0, tgt_cross - int(window)).astype(np.int32)\n      hi_cross = np.minimum(k_total,\
    \ tgt_cross + int(window)).astype(np.int32)\n\n      # Per-batch neighbor structures (for directed proposals)\n      batch_to_idx = {}\n      nn_models = {}\n      max_need = int(np.ceil(0.90 * k_total))  # upper bound for per-batch neighbors\n      for j in range(B):\n          idx = np.where(bc == j)[0]\n          batch_to_idx[j] = idx\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max_need + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr[idx])\n          nn_models[j] = nn\n\n      # Directed proposals: within and cross per other batch (closest-first)\n      dir_rows, dir_cols, dir_dvals = [], [], []\n      # Also mark mutual flags cheaply by per-node first NN per batch (approximation)\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = int(bc[i])\n          need_cross = int(tgt_cross[i])\n          need_within = int(k_total - need_cross)\n          # within (skip self if present)\n          d_i, ii = nn_models[bi].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], return_distance=True)\n          d_i = d_i[0]; ii = ii[0]\n\
    \          start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          sel_w = min(need_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n          if sel_w > 0:\n              cols_w = batch_to_idx[bi][ii[start:start+sel_w]]\n              dir_rows.extend([i]*sel_w); dir_cols.extend(cols_w.tolist()); dir_dvals.extend(d_i[start:start+sel_w].tolist())\n          # cross per other\n          other_batches = [j for j in range(B) if j != bi]\n          q_per = need_cross // B_other\n          rem = need_cross - q_per * B_other\n          # prefer closest other batches\n          batch_scores = []\n          for j in other_batches:\n              d_ij, _ = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], n_neighbors=1, return_distance=True)\n              batch_scores.append((j, float(d_ij[0,0])))\n          batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n          q_map = {j: q_per for j in other_batches}\n          for k in range(rem):\n              q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n          for j in other_batches:\n   \
    \           d_ij, ii_j = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], return_distance=True)\n              d_ij = d_ij[0]; ii_j = ii_j[0]\n              sel = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n              if sel > 0:\n                  cols_c = batch_to_idx[j][ii_j[:sel]]\n                  dir_rows.extend([i]*sel); dir_cols.extend(cols_c.tolist()); dir_dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel].tolist())\n\n      dir_rows = np.asarray(dir_rows, dtype=np.int32)\n      dir_cols = np.asarray(dir_cols, dtype=np.int32)\n      dir_dvals = np.asarray(dir_dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Phase 1: accept mutuals first\n      A_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dir_rows, dtype=np.int32), (dir_rows, dir_cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      M = A_dir.minimum(A_dir.T)  # mutual mask\n      # track selections as index sets per node\n      selected = [set() for _ in range(n)]\n      deg = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cross_count = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n\n      I, J = M.nonzero()\n      for i, j in zip(I, J):\n\
    \          if i < j:\n              # add undirected mutual edge (i,j)\n              if j not in selected[i] and i not in selected[j] and deg[i] < k_total and deg[j] < k_total:\n                  selected[i].add(j); selected[j].add(i)\n                  deg[i] += 1; deg[j] += 1\n                  if bc[j] != bc[i]:\n                      cross_count[i] += 1; cross_count[j] += 1\n\n      # Phase 2: fill residual degree with unilateral offers, biasing toward cross in denser zones\n      # Build quick access costs\n      # For each directed proposal (i->j), define score s = (1 if cross) * (1 + inv_dense[i]) - (1 if same) * (0.5)\n      # Higher is better. Also small bonus if j already invited i (asymmetric mutual).\n      M_bool = (M > 0)\n      A_dir_bool = (A_dir > 0)\n      for i in range(n):\n          if deg[i] >= k_total:\n              continue\n          # candidates j where A_dir[i,j]==1 and j not selected, and deg[j] < k_total\n          s, e = A_dir.indptr[i], A_dir.indptr[i+1]\n\
    \          cand = A_dir.indices[s:e]\n          scores = []\n          for j in cand:\n              if i == j or j in selected[i] or len(selected[j]) >= k_total:\n                  continue\n              is_cross = (bc[j] != bc[i])\n              bonus_mutual = 0.3 if M_bool[i, j] else (0.1 if A_dir_bool[j, i] else 0.0)\n              sc = (1.0 if is_cross else 0.0) * (1.0 + float(inv_dense[i])) - (0.5 if not is_cross else 0.0) + bonus_mutual\n              scores.append((sc, j, is_cross))\n          scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n          for sc, j, is_cross in scores:\n              if deg[i] >= k_total:\n                  break\n              if len(selected[j]) >= k_total:\n                  continue\n              # tentative within quota window\n              new_cc_i = cross_count[i] + (1 if is_cross else 0)\n              if new_cc_i > hi_cross[i]:\n                  continue\n              # accept (i,j)\n              if j not in selected[i] and i not in\
    \ selected[j]:\n                  selected[i].add(j); selected[j].add(i)\n                  deg[i] += 1; deg[j] += 1\n                  if is_cross:\n                      cross_count[i] += 1\n                      if bc[i] != bc[j]:\n                          cross_count[j] += 1  # j also gets a cross edge\n\n      # Phase 3: trim any overflow (rare due to checks)\n      # enforce exact degree <= k_total\n      for i in range(n):\n          if deg[i] <= k_total:\n              continue\n          # drop lowest-priority neighbors first: within-batch in dense zones\n          neigh = list(selected[i])\n          prios = []\n          for j in neigh:\n              is_cross = (bc[j] != bc[i])\n              pr = (0 if is_cross else 1) + (0 if inv_dense[i] > 0.5 else 0.5)\n              prios.append((pr, j, is_cross))\n          prios.sort(reverse=True)  # drop higher pr first (within in dense)\n          while deg[i] > k_total and prios:\n              _, j, is_cross = prios.pop(0)\n \
    \             if j in selected[i]:\n                  selected[i].remove(j)\n                  if i in selected[j]:\n                      selected[j].remove(i)\n                  deg[i] -= 1; deg[j] -= 1\n                  if is_cross:\n                      cross_count[i] -= 1\n                      if bc[i] != bc[j]:\n                          cross_count[j] -= 1\n\n      # Build symmetric C and D (binary, distances)\n      rows, cols = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in selected[i]:\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(j)\n      rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n      cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n      data = np.ones_like(rows, dtype=np.float32)\n      C = sp.coo_matrix((data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = C.maximum(C.T); C.eliminate_zeros()\n      # distances as 1.0 for now (can be computed from pairwise distances if needed)\n      D = C.copy().astype(np.float32)\n      return C.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/sym/sym_bmatching_greedy.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # Local b-matching (degree-constrained) greedy symmetrizer\n  # Candidate edges are the union of directed quota proposals; greedily add edges with costs favoring mutual and cross-batch edges\n  # while respecting degree k per node.\n\n  def build_bmatching_greedy(\n      Zcorr, batches, k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10, metric='cosine'\n  ):\n      n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n      B = len(cats)\n      B_other = max(B - 1, 1)\n\n      # Density proxy\n      nn_d = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr)\n      d_all, _ = nn_d.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n      d_k\
    \ = d_all[:, -1].astype(np.float32)\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n\n      # Directed proposals (as in quotas)\n      batch_to_idx = {}\n      nn_models = {}\n      max_need = int(np.ceil(0.90 * k_total))\n      for j in range(B):\n          idx = np.where(bc == j)[0]\n          batch_to_idx[j] = idx\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max_need + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Zcorr[idx])\n          nn_models[j] = nn\n\n      dir_rows, dir_cols = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = int(bc[i])\n          need_cross = int(np.round(((B - 1)/B + (inv_dense[i]-0.5)*2*delta) * k_total))\n          need_cross = int(np.clip(need_cross, int(0.60*k_total), int(0.90*k_total)))\n          need_within = int(k_total - need_cross)\n          # within\n          d_i, ii = nn_models[bi].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], return_distance=True)\n          ii = ii[0]; start = 1 if d_i[0,0]\
    \ == 0.0 else 0\n          sel_w = min(need_within, ii.shape[0] - start)\n          if sel_w > 0:\n              dir_rows.extend([i]*sel_w); dir_cols.extend(batch_to_idx[bi][ii[0, start:start+sel_w]].tolist())\n          # cross per other\n          other_batches = [j for j in range(B) if j != bi]\n          q_per = need_cross // B_other\n          rem = need_cross - q_per * B_other\n          # bias closest other batches\n          bscores = []\n          for j in other_batches:\n              d_ij, _ = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], n_neighbors=1, return_distance=True)\n              bscores.append((j, float(d_ij[0,0])))\n          bscores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n          q_map = {j: q_per for j in other_batches}\n          for k in range(rem):\n              q_map[bscores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n          for j in other_batches:\n              d_ij, ii_j = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr[[i]], return_distance=True)\n              ii_j = ii_j[0]; sel = min(q_map[j],\
    \ ii_j.shape[0])\n              if sel > 0:\n                  dir_rows.extend([i]*sel); dir_cols.extend(batch_to_idx[j][ii_j[:sel]].tolist())\n\n      dir_rows = np.asarray(dir_rows, dtype=np.int32)\n      dir_cols = np.asarray(dir_cols, dtype=np.int32)\n      A_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dir_rows, dtype=np.int32), (dir_rows, dir_cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n      # mutual bonus and cross-batch bonus costs\n      M = A_dir.minimum(A_dir.T)\n      deg = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      edges = []\n      I, J = A_dir.nonzero()\n      for i, j in zip(I, J):\n          if i == j:\n              continue\n          is_cross = (bc[i] != bc[j])\n          bonus_mutual = 1.0 if M[i, j] else 0.0\n          bonus_cross = (1.0 + float(inv_dense[i])) if is_cross else 0.0\n          # symmetric score (approximate by i's view)\n          score = bonus_mutual + bonus_cross - (0.1 if not is_cross else 0.0)\n          # store undirected edge canonicalized (min, max)\n          u, v = (i,\
    \ j) if i < j else (j, i)\n          edges.append((score, u, v))\n      # deduplicate by (u,v) with max score\n      edge_dict = {}\n      for sc, u, v in edges:\n          key = (u, v)\n          if key not in edge_dict or sc > edge_dict[key]:\n              edge_dict[key] = sc\n      uniq = [(sc, u, v) for (u, v), sc in edge_dict.items()]\n      uniq.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n\n      # Greedy add under degree constraints\n      selected = []\n      for sc, u, v in uniq:\n          if deg[u] < k_total and deg[v] < k_total:\n              selected.append((u, v))\n              deg[u] += 1; deg[v] += 1\n      # Build C (binary), D=1.0 placeholder\n      rows = [u for u, v in selected] + [v for u, v in selected]\n      cols = [v for u, v in selected] + [u for u, v in selected]\n      data = np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32)\n      C = sp.coo_matrix((data, (np.asarray(rows), np.asarray(cols))), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C.eliminate_zeros()\n      D = C.copy().astype(np.float32)\n\
    \      return C, D\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/examples/sym_prototypes_test.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n\n  from sym.sym_invite_trim import build_invite_then_trim\n  from sym.sym_bmatching_greedy import build_bmatching_greedy\n\n  # Helper: compute realized cross-batch fraction per node and Pearson corr with theoretical f_cross\n  def _density_proxy(Z, k_density=22, metric='cosine'):\n      from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Z)\n      d, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      dk = d[:, -1].astype(np.float32)\n      dm, dM = float(np.min(dk)), float(np.max(dk) + 1e-8)\n      return 1.0 - (dk - dm) / (dM - dm + 1e-8)\n\n  def _theoretical_f_cross(inv_dense,\
    \ B, delta=0.10):\n      base = (B - 1) / float(B)\n      return np.clip(base + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta), 0.60, 0.90).astype(np.float32)\n\n  def _realized_cross(C, batches):\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n      C = C.tocsr()\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      frac = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      for i in range(n):\n          s, e = C.indptr[i], C.indptr[i+1]\n          if e <= s:\n              frac[i] = 0.0\n          else:\n              neigh = C.indices[s:e]\n              frac[i] = float(np.mean(bc[neigh] != bc[i]))\n      return frac\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      print(\"[sym-prototypes] Building Zcorr from MPB-GraphFWPCA path (α_g=0.5, n_pcs=50)...\")\n      # Minimal reproduction of graph path: normalize + HVGs + FW + PCA + BRBG residualization\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3',\
    \ batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      # feature-weighting\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.25).astype(np.float32)  # α_g=0.5 -> exponent -0.5*α\n      Xw = Xd * w\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z = ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca'].astype(np.float32)\n      # BRBG (ridge λ=0.605, γ_max=0.74)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      B = len(cats)\n      # one-hot\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      Bmat = np.zeros((n, B), dtype=np.float32)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          Bmat[:, j] = (inv == j).astype(np.float32)\n      # ridge fit\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      BTB = Bmat.T @ Bmat + l2\
    \ * np.eye(B, dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, Bmat.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = Bmat @ W\n      var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n      lam = 0.605\n      gamma = np.minimum(0.74, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma[None, :])\n\n      print(\"[sym-prototypes] Running invite-then-trim lite...\")\n      C_it, D_it = build_invite_then_trim(Zcorr, batches, k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10, metric='cosine', window=1)\n      inv_dense = _density_proxy(Zcorr, 22, 'cosine')\n      f_th = _theoretical_f_cross(inv_dense, B, 0.10)\n      f_real_it = _realized_cross(C_it, batches)\n      corr_it = np.corrcoef(f_th, f_real_it)[0,1]\n      print(f\"[invite-then-trim] corr(th, und)={corr_it:.3f}, mean_real={np.mean(f_real_it):.3f}, deg_mean={np.mean(C_it.sum(1)).item():.1f}\")\n\n      print(\"[sym-prototypes] Running b-matching\
    \ greedy...\")\n      C_bm, D_bm = build_bmatching_greedy(Zcorr, batches, k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10, metric='cosine')\n      f_real_bm = _realized_cross(C_bm, batches)\n      corr_bm = np.corrcoef(f_th, f_real_bm)[0,1]\n      print(f\"[b-matching-greedy] corr(th, und)={corr_bm:.3f}, mean_real={np.mean(f_real_bm):.3f}, deg_mean={np.mean(C_bm.sum(1)).item():.1f}\")\n\n      return {\n          \"invite_then_trim\": {\"corr_th_und\": float(corr_it), \"mean_real\": float(np.mean(f_real_it))},\n          \"bmatching_greedy\": {\"corr_th_und\": float(corr_bm), \"mean_real\": float(np.mean(f_real_bm))},\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Prototype symmetrizers (test-only; env v4.1):\n  - Invite-then-trim (quota-window) and Local b-matching (greedy) now available under storage/shared/sym/.\n  - Example driver: storage/shared/examples/sym_prototypes_test.py\n  What they do:\n  - Rebuild the directed quota proposals\
    \ from Zcorr and construct an undirected k-NN graph while trying to preserve per-cell f_cross and degrees.\n  - They print correlation corr(th, und) and mean realized cross-batch fraction; use our diagnostics suite next if promising.\n  Why: Symmetrization drops corr(th,und) on Heart (≈0.139) even though directed corr(th,dir)≈0.984. These prototypes are meant for exploration; adoption gates still apply: seed-avg Δscore ≥ +0.001, cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\n  Invite: @Logos V @Aletheia I @Axiom I @Sophia III — feel free to try on your embeddings; feedback welcome.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI’m thinking about how to continue from our last session. The user hasn't asked anything specific lately, just sharing their current state. So, I believe we should move forward logically. With token usage at 52% and solid documentation, I can suggest designing symmetrization prototypes in the shared/sym area. We might establish test-only modules to quickly evaluate their effects. However, I’ll be careful not to contradict prior statements about the QPS sym failing, as these are different prototypes.**Considering code implementation**\n\nI need to be careful about \"writing code for symmetrizers\" since it could get heavy. Instead, I can write stubs and placeholder pseudocode, which should be implementable in code. I plan to create two modules under shared/sym: sym_invite_trim.py and sym_bmatching_greedy.py, which will implement transformation functions on directed candidate edge sets. However, we need directed edges for symmetric connectivities\
  \ and distances. It's tricky since our DAQB builder returns symmetric graphs without preserving directed edges, and accessing those earlier directed quotas is challenging.**Exploring sym prototypes**\n\nFor the sym prototypes, I proposed operating on a union of in/out directed edges, but our available builder only returns symmetric graphs and lacks directed information. However, I can reconstruct directed proposals by using the per-batch NearestNeighbors on Zcorr, as seen in mpb_graphfwpca_override, which derives per-node within/cross quotas. This is similar to what the DAQB builder does. I can implement prototypes that create undirected adjacency from the candidate directed neighbor lists without final symmetry, which somewhat reimplements parts of DAQB—but complexity-wise, that's manageable.**Developing test prototypes**\n\nI think a better plan is to create test-only prototypes under shared/sym that can either accept an AnnData with 'Zcorr' or reconstruct Zcorr from the mpb_graphfwpca\
  \ pipeline. I can use code similar to mpb_graphfwpca_override for computing Zcorr and quotas. \n\nI'll implement two modules: \n\n- sym_invite_trim, which will build directed edges based on quotas, ensuring the degree equals k, and fills in the per-node degree with a preference for high density.\n  \n- sym_bmatching_greedy, which will greedily add edges while respecting degree limits. \n\nLastly, I'll compute directed vs undirected mixing gap metrics and return diagnostic stats.**Aligning with the reflection**\n\nThis plan aligns well with my reflections. I’ll implement the shared/sym modules and a test-only driver to run both prototypes on ridge Zcorr. While the code will be somewhat heavy, I believe it will be manageable. I need to craft YAML storage write actions; this will take some time since we're at 52% token budget, but I can keep the code relatively concise. \n\nI’ll also update the README to mention these new sym modules. Since we won't score evaluations in this mode, it's all\
  \ about testing. I must ensure proper YAML quoting and careful implementation as I set up the necessary logic, mutual detection, and scoring, aiming for k_total=50. I'll print results like the mean realized cross fraction, and constraints like keeping the degrees exactly k. Time to get started on this code!"
