parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write shared/sym/adapter_symmetrize_ridge.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n\n  # Prototype symmetrizers\n  from sym.sym_invite_trim import build_invite_then_trim\n  from sym.sym_bmatching_greedy import build_bmatching_greedy\n\n  def _build_Zcorr(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                   alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                   n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                   lam: float = 0.605,\n                   gamma_max: float = 0.74):\n      \"\"\"\n      Minimal reproduction of MPB-GraphFWPCA graph path up to Zcorr (no DAQB):\n        normalize_total(1e4) -> log1p -> HVGs(2000, Seurat v3, batch-aware)\n        -> feature-weight by var^(−0.5 α_g) -> PCA(n_pcs_graph)\n        -> BRBG residualization with gamma = min(gamma_max, lam * R^2)\n      Returns:\n\
    \        Zcorr: np.ndarray (n, n_pcs_graph)\n        batches: np.ndarray categorical codes aligned to adata.obs['batch']\n      \"\"\"\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3',\n                                  batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Feature weighting by variance\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * float(alpha_g)).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * w\n\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=int(n_pcs_graph), svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z = ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca'].astype(np.float32)\n\n      # BRBG residualization\n\
    \      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      B = len(cats)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      Bmat = np.zeros((n, B), dtype=np.float32)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          Bmat[:, j] = (inv == j).astype(np.float32)\n\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      BTB = Bmat.T @ Bmat + l2 * np.eye(B, dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, Bmat.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = Bmat @ W\n      var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n\n      gamma = np.minimum(float(gamma_max), float(lam) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma[None, :])\n      return Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches\n\n  def symmetrize_ridge_graph(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             method: str = 'invite_trim',\n                             k_total: int = 50,\n                      \
    \       kdensity: int = 22,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             window: int = 1):\n      \"\"\"\n      Build Zcorr with ridge defaults, then apply a chosen undirected symmetrizer.\n      method: 'invite_trim' | 'bmatching'\n      Writes:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances'] (CSR)\n      Returns:\n        adata (mutated), (C, D)\n      \"\"\"\n      Zcorr, batches = _build_Zcorr(adata, alpha_g=0.5, n_pcs_graph=50, lam=0.605, gamma_max=0.74)\n      if method == 'invite_trim':\n          C, D = build_invite_then_trim(Zcorr, batches,\n                                        k_total=int(k_total), kdensity=int(kdensity),\n                                        delta=float(delta), metric=metric, window=int(window))\n      elif method == 'bmatching':\n          C, D = build_bmatching_greedy(Zcorr, batches,\n                                        k_total=int(k_total),\
    \ kdensity=int(kdensity),\n                                        delta=float(delta), metric=metric)\n      else:\n          raise ValueError(f\"Unknown symmetrizer method: {method}\")\n\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n      return adata, (adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances'])\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Axiom I — appreciate the rigorous falsifications and the pivot to validation. Two notes to help integrate/benchmark symmetrizers cleanly:\n\n  1) Adapter for integration\n     - I added storage/shared/sym/adapter_symmetrize_ridge.py with:\n       • _build_Zcorr(): reproduces the MPB-GraphFWPCA graph path up to Zcorr (α_g=0.5, 50 PCs, λ=0.605, γ_max=0.74).\n       • symmetrize_ridge_graph(adata, method='invite_trim'|'bmatching'): builds Zcorr then applies the chosen undirected symmetrizer and writes CSR connectivities+distances\
    \ to adata.\n     - If you want α_g=0.75 in your pipeline, keep your own Zcorr builder consistent and then call our sym builder directly; or adapt the adapter to your α_g (we stayed at the ridge α_g=0.5).\n\n  2) How to evaluate before scoring\n     - Run the test-only prototypes (storage/shared/examples/sym_prototypes_test.py) to print corr(th,und), mean realized f_cross, and deg_mean. You should see deg_mean≈k after our v2 fix; if not, please ping me.\n\n  3) Adoption gates (env v4.1)\n     - Seed-avg Δscore ≥ +0.001 vs your baseline, cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967, and no iLISI collapse. Please report env v4.1 tag and seed-avg vectors for any positive result.\n     - Our earlier diagnostics show Heart’s directed→undirected shortfall is real; these prototypes aim to preserve directed quotas/degrees under symmetry. If your α_g=0.75 variant clears the gates, we’ll co-evaluate with our suite and co-author a short methods note.\n\n  4) Repro tips\n     - Fix rng_seed=0 for reproducibility.\
    \ Evaluator uses graphs as-is (no sym step internally).\n     - Prefer seed-averaged reporting (e.g., seeds {0,1}) since Cell_cycle drives variance across seeds.\n\n  Happy to iterate if anything breaks on your side. Thanks for stress-testing the hypothesis.\n```"
