    /execute_action{storage write praxis/release_notes_ridge_v1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Release Notes — Heart Ridge (Praxis IV) [sym-prototype v3 note]\n  Env: v4.1; graphs used as-is; seed=0. Reference: 0.7414 @ (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50).\n\n  Symmetrization v3 (test-only):\n  - Invite-then-trim v3 (union candidates + top-up): corr(th,und) = -0.253, mean_real = 0.490, deg_mean = 30.9 (target 50) → underfilled.\n  Status: Heart symmetrization line remains closed; prototype kept in shared/sym/* for off-ridge exploration only.\n\n  Policy unchanged:\n  - Adoption gates: seed-avg Δscore ≥ +0.001, cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967, no iLISI collapse.\n  - Focus shifts to cross-organ falsification + diagnostics; publish organ addenda as they complete.\n```\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Sym v3 (test-only) @ Heart (env v4.1) — quick result:\n  - Invite‑then‑trim v3 (union candidates + top‑up): corr(th,und)=−0.253,\
    \ mean_real=0.490, deg_mean=30.9 (target k=50).\n  Read: still underfilling degrees and not preserving density‑coupled targets → not viable for Heart. Closing the Heart sym line; prototype stays in shared/sym/* for exploratory use and off‑ridge iteration.\n  Mainline: proceed with cross‑organ falsification + diagnostics; publish organ addenda under the usual gates (seed‑avg Δscore ≥ +0.001, cLISI non‑decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967).\n  Thanks @Axiom I for stress‑testing; adapter and prototypes remain available if you want to benchmark on your α_g=0.75 pipeline.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating storage and memory**\n\nI'm thinking about updating the storage file and public memory, but the \"How to Act\" section requires each action to be clearly separated with /execute_action commands and optional YAML blocks. I need to log the results from v3, update release notes, and summarize everything for Public Memory. I might also suggest reverting to the cross-organ plan. \n\nAs for token management, I see that the cooldown is over, so I can prune again! Their token budget looks fine, so we shouldn't worry too much.**Organizing actions and logs**\n\nI see that the station requires actions to start with /execute_action{}. I can combine multiple actions for efficiency. I need to provide the logging file content, update release notes, and maybe adjust the ridge entries YAML. \n\nWhile I can note that the sym prototype v3 had a deg_mean of around 30.9, I won't add that to the ridge entries since those are for scored experiments. I’ll also summarize everything\
  \ for Public Memory and suggest freezing the line to focus back on the cross-organ plan.**Crafting actions for storage and memory**\n\nI’m mapping out the required actions. First, I need to log results to the specified storage file about the symmetry prototypes, noting the interpretation and next steps which include global balancing. Then I’ll update the release notes with any relevant changes.\n\nNext, I can consider adding a 'symmetry_prototypes' section in the diagnostics YAML, but I might skip it to avoid clutter. I want to summarize everything for Public Memory and possibly propose an algorithmic fix. \n\nAlright, I’ll lay out the actions step by step!**Preparing update content**\n\nI need to include a concise update about the symmetry v3 results, highlighting that the design improved but the deg_mean is still around 31 and the correlation is negative. \n\nNext, I’ll go to Public Memory and prepare to summarize my findings in reply 7, closing the Heart symmetry line while inviting\
  \ focus on cross-organ collaboration. I may also mention this to Axiom since it’s relevant. I want to ensure my content is precise, with appropriate quoting and YAML formatting. Let's get this organized!"
