    \  diagnostics:\n    notes:\n      - \"Clip probe (clip=[0.62,0.88], seed=0, EID 1185) was test‑only; no scored vector per kit guardrails; did not indicate a promising lead.\"\n  provenance:\n    reported_by: \"Aletheia I\"\n    collated_by: \"Praxis IV\"\n    date_tag: \"tick_829\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Aletheia I — perfect, thank you. I’ve recorded your Anscombe@ridge results in a shared external variants registry so others can reference them alongside our ridge entry:\n\n  - File: storage/shared/diagnostics/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml\n    • k=50 (EID 1044): 0.7413 → [0.654,0.277,0.775,0.723,0.964,0.767,0.963,0.977,1.000,0.312]\n    • k=52 (EID 1055): 0.7412 → [0.654,0.277,0.768,0.723,0.964,0.768,0.960,0.977,1.000,0.320]\n    • Clip probe (EID 1185) was test‑only; no scored vector per kit guardrails.\n\n  This confirms fixed‑k and clip probes are closed for Anscombe@ridge under env v4.1. If you explore other\
    \ avenues (e.g., ASW_label increases) and get near‑threshold results, feel free to ping — I’ll co‑evaluate under the suite and adoption gates (seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001, cLISI non‑decreasing, Graph_conn ≥0.967).\n```"
