thinking_content: "**Exploring analytical options**\n\nI could do more prunes after cooldown and think about drafting a one-pager for Public memory. I might coordinate with new Daedalus or reply to Aletheia, which I've already done. Since there's stagnation, we might shift to an analytical paper on variance sources across seeds and do some robust evaluations. I can prepare an \"evaluation check harness\" for contributions to score differences. I might also check logistics for diagnostics and packaging to enhance environment metadata in result files.**Evaluating potential actions**\n\nI could create a \"result annotator\" to write anndata.uns env fields, but we really need to run evaluations before that. Resting and waiting for a new dataset isn't ideal, so I might propose \"public tools\" for symmetric bridging—though we've previously concluded it's negative. We could coordinate with Daedalus to run their method with our diagnostics, but we’ve already contacted them. Updating Public Memory\
  \ for Daedalus sounds good, and I can compactly hand over in Private Memory too.**Managing tokens and actions**\n\nI really need to keep tokens in check and avoid being too verbose. I notice the assistant often leans toward producing actions. I was thinking we could finalize by creating a TODO, but I’ll have to wait to prune again since we’re still on cooldown from the last prune at tick 832, which means there’s still one tick left. So, instead of pruning, I could focus on crafting a \"result_extractor.py\" to pull extra metrics from the h5ad results, but that'll be for testing only.**Creating diagnostic tools**\n\nI want to create a helpful action by developing a shared/diagnostics/result_summary.py. It’ll include a test function that loads the runtime adata object and prints out metrics, although we won't compute them directly in test mode. Instead, I can calculate some proxies like degree stats, cross-batch fraction histograms, and other relevant statistics. I thought about adding a\
  \ \"one-liner aggregator\" function for summaries, but ridge_suite.run_all already returns a dict. I might also consider the seed_sweep_runner.py, though we need separate submissions for scoring across seeds, which isn't necessary right now.**Finalizing actions**\n\nI want to maintain a minimal approach, so I plan to produce a \"monitoring\" summary and consider moving to Reflection for deeper thought. I’m thinking about shaping a \"standard table\" for Public Memory, but tokens are limited. Instead, I'll check the Research Counter to see if there's any new state-of-the-art information. I’ll create a compact \"robustness_summary.md\" to capture closed lines and adoption gates. \n\nI’ll execute actions to rank the score and maybe briefly mention Daedalus in Public Memory, even though I’ve already contacted them. Alright, I’ll go with the rank score action."
