    \    • Δ≈+0.0008; cLISI↓ → closed.\n  Registry and notes updated; will report confirm run outcome and either adopt γ_max=0.76 or keep ridge frozen accordingly.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating micro-probe results**\n\nWe received the results for two micro-probes. The first, gamma_max=0.76, scored 0.743116, which is an improvement over the reference of 0.7414, satisfying the threshold for adoption. The guardrails also check out with cLISI and graph_conn meeting their respective criteria. The second probe, k=51, scored lower and didn’t meet the threshold, so it won't be adopted. I need to log these results, update the release notes, and prepare for a re-run of gamma_max with seed=1.**Confirming threshold check**\n\nWe previously had a policy to seed-average near the threshold, and now with a Δ of +0.0017, we need to run a confirmation with seed=1 for gamma_max=0.76. I should create the new runner file, best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_gmax076_seed1.py, and submit it. After that, I’ll log results for EIDs 1189 and 1190, update the release notes, and the shared YAML entry. I might also consider implementing diagnostics later, but it’s not necessary right now.\
  \ Let’s move forward with these steps!**Planning next steps**\n\nOur adoption threshold requires that Δ must be +0.001 for seed averaging, so I need to compute the second seed. I should summarize the results and our plans in a public message. \n\nI need to log details for both EIDs, create a new runner for seed=1, and submit that. I'll also update the release notes and the YAML entry to include delta values and maintain the environment. \n\nI must ensure the vector values are written to YAML as well for both EIDs. After that, I’ll reply publicly with our plan to confirm adoption for gamma_max=0.76.**Organizing runner submission and updates**\n\nI’m considering running seed=3 for a triad, but our policy indicates we should use seed averaging when near the threshold. Since two seeds may be acceptable, I’ll stick with seed=1 based on previous practices. \n\nI’ll plan to write the new runner file and submit it, while also updating the YAML experiments list for gamma_max_0.76 and k=51. I need\
  \ to write logs and release notes, and provide a minimal summary of our actions. I have a good list of items to tackle, like writing storage logs and submitting everything in one go."
