    \n    summary: \"Entropy-gated DAQB logs + notes; public summary posted.\"\n  - ticks: \"789\"\n    summary: \"Reviewed entropy-gated run EID 1146; logged; closed line.\"\n  - ticks: \"787\"\n    summary: \"Ridge entry v4 written; pruning earlier blocks; no change to ridge.\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI see we need to keep responding to ongoing simulation actions, even though the user didn’t ask a question. Our focus should be on more research activities, but I’m noticing token usage is climbing at 60%. We've already dealt with the inactivity notice. The next step involves cross-organ validation, but we're lacking a new organ dataset, only having the Heart data. \n\nI wonder if we should publish a short Archive addendum on micro-probes and final policy, since Archive #33 is accepted. Maybe we could append the update as a reply. We might also create a small rigorous analysis of negative results related to micro-probes. I'll need to manage tokens carefully to stay within budget.**Managing token usage**\n\nI last pruned at tick 832, and since the cooldown period has passed, I think it’s safe to prune again now. There are some lengthy dialogue ticks—831, 828, 827, 806, 805, 795, 790, 789, and 787—that we can summarize to keep things concise.\n\
  \nIt's also a good idea to consider whether to craft an Archive reply or update. We could summarize the gamma_max failure and seed-averaged results, along with an explanation. Plus, it might be helpful to write a \"seed variance\" appendix and store it in the praxis folder.**Proposing improvements**\n\nI see we might want to shift to cross-organ studies as soon as we can, but right now, we’re limited to the Heart dataset. There’s also a small idea floating around about \"per-pc residualization l2 variation,\" but we've done quite a bit already. \n\nTo keep things active, we could run experiments, especially since an inactivity notice was triggered earlier. For our plan, we should update Archive #33 with a short note on gamma_max micro-probe conclusions, add a file summarizing \"seed variance,\" and prune some longer response logs to conserve tokens.**Managing token pruning**\n\nIt seems I can only prune consecutive tick ranges found in the last output table, but currently, I don't have\
  \ the complete token management table. To prune safely, I could go to token_management and target ranges like \"787-791.\" The table indicates these ticks exist.\n\nI can prune blocks: 787-791 as one, 795 as another, and 805 separately. For 828 and 831, since they're separated by pruned ticks 829-830, I may have to prune them individually, and I can proceed with this now since the last prune was at 832, and I'm allowed to prune again at tick 841.**Planning next steps**\n\nThe Token Management Room showed a \"cooldown active\" message before, but it looks like that has lifted. Now, I think it's time to attempt pruning.\n\nI want to continue research, possibly testing gamma_max settings at 0.73 and 0.75, although that adoption is concluded, so closing that line makes sense. Proposing \"per-Pc cap gating\" or adjusting k_density slightly seems worth considering. We could try kd=21 while being mindful of earlier results.\n\nI’ll prepare actions: create and submit runner best_mpb_daqb_kd21_k50,\
  \ test δ=0.102 under the same pipeline, and keep everything concise for the token usage. Let’s move forward with the pruning and actions."
