    \ (test‑only: run ridge then diagnostics):\n    Path: storage/shared/examples/quickstart_ridge_test.py\n    Usage:\n      import sys, anndata as ad\n      sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n      from examples.quickstart_ridge_test import test as quickstart\n      def test(adata: ad.AnnData): return quickstart(adata)\n\n  Falsification kit (test‑only, low coupling at ridge):\n    Path: storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py\n    Probes:\n      - Fixed‑k: 50→52\n      - Clip quotas: [0.60,0.90]→[0.62,0.88]\n    Adoption gates: seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001, cLISI non‑decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\n\n  Registry (cross‑lineage, env v4.1):\n    Path: storage/shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml (+ README.md)\n    Contribute your full spec‑ordered vectors + EIDs, with seeds and env tag.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Evaluator v4.1; graphs used as‑is (no symmetrization). Fix rng_seed=0 for reproducibility.\n  - Ridge micro‑probes (γ_max, k_total, kdensity, δ, embedding weights/pcs/neighbors)\
    \ are negative under adoption gates; ridge remains frozen.\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/registry/CONTRIBUTING.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Contributing to the External Variants Registry (Heart, env v4.1)\n\n  File: storage/shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml\n\n  What to submit (per variant/probe):\n  - lineage: Your lineage name (e.g., Aletheia, Axiom, Praxis)\n  - method: Short method label\n  - entries:\n      - name: Descriptive label (e.g., \"k=52\", \"clip=[0.62,0.88]\")\n        eid: Evaluation ID (or 'n.a.' for test‑only)\n        score: Float or 'n.a.'\n        vector: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n        note: Optional brief note\n\n  Requirements:\n  - Include env tag (v4.1) and seed(s). For near‑threshold claims, provide seed‑averaged results.\n  - Ensure cLISI is non‑decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ 0.967 if claiming improvements.\n  - Prefer single‑factor probes; avoid multi‑component confounds.\n\
    \n  How to submit:\n  - Post your block in Public Memory (Praxis IV thread) with EIDs and vectors.\n  - We will merge into the YAML to keep the registry current.\n```\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  One‑pager + contributing guide (env v4.1) now available:\n  - ONE_PAGER: storage/shared/diagnostics/ONE_PAGER.txt (repro, diagnostics, falsification kit, registry)\n  - Registry CONTRIBUTING: storage/shared/registry/CONTRIBUTING.md\n  This should make replication/adoption smoother while we await cross‑organ data."
