tick: 862
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{review 1212}\n/execute_action{review 1213}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/idea_pbve_knn_v2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # Tempered/clamped PBVE-lite with optional thresholding on variance ratio\n  def _build_knn_graph(Z, k=50, metric='cosine'):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      rows, cols, vals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          nbrs = idx[i, 1:]\n          rows.extend([i]*k); cols.extend(nbrs.tolist()); vals.extend([1.0]*k)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((vals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T); A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      # distances (true: min of directed)\n      dist_map = {}\n      for i in range(n):\n\
    \          for off, j in enumerate(idx[i, 1:]):\n              dist_map[(i, j)] = d[i, 1:][off]\n      Acoo = A_sym.tocoo()\n      data = []\n      for i, j in zip(Acoo.row, Acoo.col):\n          dij = dist_map.get((i, j), np.inf)\n          dji = dist_map.get((j, i), np.inf)\n          dd = dij if dij < dji else dji\n          if not np.isfinite(dd):\n              dd = 1.0\n          data.append(dd)\n      D = sp.csr_matrix((data, (Acoo.row, Acoo.col)), shape=A_sym.shape)\n      return A_sym.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def _pbve_scale_tempered(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray,\n                           t: float = 0.5,\n                           rmin: float = 0.8, rmax: float = 1.25,\n                           thresh: float = None):\n      # Global stats\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      gstd = Zc.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      out = Z.copy()\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      for b in cats:\n          mask = (batches == b)\n          Zb = Z[mask]\n    \
    \      Zb_c = Zb - Zb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n          bstd = Zb_c.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          ratio = (gstd / bstd)\n          if thresh is not None:\n              use = np.abs(np.log(ratio)) > float(thresh)\n          else:\n              use = np.ones_like(ratio, dtype=bool)\n          r = np.power(np.clip(ratio, rmin, rmax), t)\n          Zb_eq = Zb_c.copy()\n          Zb_eq[:, use] = Zb_c[:, use] * r[use]\n          out[mask] = Zb_eq\n      # re-center globally\n      out = out - out.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return out.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z = np.asarray(adata.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \      # Defaults: mild temper and clamp; no threshold\n      Z_pbve = _pbve_scale_tempered(Z, batches, t=0.5, rmin=0.8, rmax=1.25, thresh=None)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_pbve\n      C, D = _build_knn_graph(Z_pbve, k=50, metric='cosine')\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/idea_locz_knn_robust.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _build_knn_graph_localz_robust(Z, k=50, k_prime_add=20, metric='cosine'):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      kprime = k + k_prime_add\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kprime+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      rows, cols, vals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          dd = d[i, 1:]\n          ii = idx[i,\
    \ 1:]\n          med = np.median(dd)\n          mad = np.median(np.abs(dd - med)) + 1e-8\n          z = (dd - med) / mad\n          # fallback if mad tiny\n          if mad < 1e-6:\n              order = np.argsort(dd)[:k]\n          else:\n              order = np.argsort(z)[:k]\n          nbrs = ii[order]\n          rows.extend([i]*k); cols.extend(nbrs.tolist()); vals.extend([1.0]*k)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((vals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T); A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      # distances (true)\n      dist_map = {}\n      for i in range(n):\n          for off, j in enumerate(idx[i, 1:]):\n              dist_map[(i, j)] = d[i, 1:][off]\n      Acoo = A_sym.tocoo()\n      data = []\n      for i, j in zip(Acoo.row, Acoo.col):\n          dij = dist_map.get((i, j), np.inf)\n          dji = dist_map.get((j, i), np.inf)\n          dd = dij if dij < dji else dji\n          if not np.isfinite(dd):\n              dd = 1.0\n          data.append(dd)\n     \
    \ D = sp.csr_matrix((data, (Acoo.row, Acoo.col)), shape=A_sym.shape)\n      return A_sym.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z = np.asarray(adata.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z\n      C, D = _build_knn_graph_localz_robust(Z, k=50, k_prime_add=20, metric='cosine')\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper scaffold — Stagnation Protocol I: Three simple, orthogonal graph ideas on PCA+kNN\"\ncontent: |\n  Title: Simple, Orthogonal Improvements to a PCA+kNN Baseline for scRNA-seq Batch Integration\n\n  Baseline\
    \ (EID 1209): PCA60 + kNN50 (cosine), binary graph, no quotas/residualization — Score 0.4593\n  Idea 1 (EID 1210): PBVE-lite — per-batch per-PC variance equalization — Score 0.6098\n  Idea 2 (EID 1212): Local distance z-scoring (k′=k+20) — PENDING\n  Idea 3 (EID 1213): Mutual-k enforcement + distance-only top-up — PENDING\n\n  Methods (self-contained):\n  - PBVE-lite: define global std σj and batch std σb,j on PCA(60); scale per-batch by (σj/σb,j)^t (t∈[0,1]) with clamps; re-center globally; build vanilla kNN.\n  - Local z-scoring: build k′ neighbor pool; z-score distances per-row; pick top-k by smallest z; binary; record true distances; symmetrize by max.\n  - Mutual-k + top-up: A = directed kNN; M = min(A,Aᵀ); top-up to degree k using nearest true distances from union(in,out) per-row; symmetrize by max.\n\n  Results table (spec-ordered vectors):\n  - Baseline: [0.545,0.205,0.427,0.652,0.882,0.590,0.003,0.991,0.000,0.298]\n  - PBVE-lite: [0.668,0.217,0.525,0.683,0.874,0.742,0.030,0.988,1.000,0.372]\n\
    \  - Local z: [...]\n  - Mutual-k: [...]\n\n  Diagnostics to include:\n  - cbf median/IQR shift vs baseline; reciprocity distributions; Jaccard(C_idea, C_base) median.\n  - Graph integrity: Graph_conn, components, min/mean degree.\n  - For PBVE-lite: histogram of σb,j/σj pre/post; proportion of PCs affected (when thresholded).\n\n  Discussion:\n  - Why baseline under-mixes (iLISI≈0); which simple geometric or variance tweaks help.\n  - Trade-offs: Graph_conn stability vs mixing; label structure drift.\n  - Outlook: port promising ideas to an advanced ridge (batch-agnostic re-ranking only) under tighter gates.\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - PBVE-lite demonstrates large gains on a brittle baseline; pending results for Ideas 2/3. Regardless of pass/fail, the three ideas provide a clean ablation set and insights into batch-agnostic geometric adjustments.\n```"
