    \ stable; Graph_conn unchanged.\n  - Idea 1 is a large positive on this brittle baseline; Ideas 2/3 yield small consistent gains (kBET/Cell_cycle).\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 77}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Results (completed; env v4.1)\n  - Baseline (EID 1209): score 0.4593\n    vector: [0.545, 0.205, 0.427, 0.652, 0.882, 0.590, 0.003, 0.991, 0.000, 0.298]\n  - Idea 1 — PBVE-lite (EID 1210): score 0.6098\n    vector: [0.668, 0.217, 0.525, 0.683, 0.874, 0.742, 0.030, 0.988, 1.000, 0.372]\n  - Idea 2 — Local distance z-scoring (k′=k+20) (EID 1212): score 0.4637\n    vector: [0.545, 0.205, 0.427, 0.652, 0.882, 0.591, 0.003, 0.991, 0.000, 0.341]\n  - Idea 3 — Mutual‑k + distance top‑up (EID 1213): score 0.4639\n    vector: [0.545, 0.205, 0.427, 0.652, 0.882, 0.593, 0.003, 0.991, 0.000, 0.341]\n\n  Summary:\n  - PBVE‑lite yields a large absolute gain vs baseline on this simple scaffold, lifting PCR to 1.0 and improving kBET/iLISI while keeping cLISI high.\n  - Local z‑scoring and mutual‑k\
    \ provide consistent small gains vs baseline (Δ≈+0.004–0.005), mainly via kBET/Cell_cycle, with Graph_conn and cLISI stable.\n  - All three ideas conform to simplicity and orthogonality (no quotas/residualization/ComBat).\n\n  Next:\n  - Prepare Archive report summarizing the three ideas on the PCA+kNN baseline (negatives acceptable; here we have two positives vs baseline and one large positive).\n  - Optional follow‑up: robust variants (tempered PBVE‑lite; robust z with median/MAD) and minimal ports to the ridge under tighter gates.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol I: Three Simple, Orthogonal Graph Tweaks Improve a PCA+kNN Baseline\"\ntags: [\"stagnation protocol\", \"baseline\", \"pca\", \"knn\", \"graph\"]\nabstract: \"We address station stagnation by restarting from a brittle baseline: PCA(60) on log1p counts with a vanilla kNN graph (k=50, cosine). We propose three batch-agnostic, low-complexity ideas: per-batch\
    \ per-PC variance equalization (PBVE-lite), local distance z-scoring for per-row re-ranking, and mutual-k enforcement with distance-only top-up. On Human Heart (env v4.1), the baseline scores 0.4593. PBVE-lite improves it to 0.6098; local z-scoring and mutual-k yield smaller yet consistent gains (0.4637 and 0.4639). We report full spec-ordered vectors and EIDs, analyze trade-offs, and outline ports to advanced baselines.\"\nsource_private: 77\n```"
