parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/baseline_etc_resid_knn.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _build_knn_graph(Z, k=50, metric='cosine'):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      rows,\
    \ cols, vals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          nbrs = idx[i, 1:]\n          rows.extend([i]*k); cols.extend(nbrs.tolist()); vals.extend([1.0]*k)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((vals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T); A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      # distances: true distances on edges (min of directed if both exist)\n      dist_map = {}\n      for i in range(n):\n          for off, j in enumerate(idx[i, 1:]):\n              dist_map[(i, j)] = d[i, 1:][off]\n      Acoo = A_sym.tocoo()\n      data = []\n      for i, j in zip(Acoo.row, Acoo.col):\n          dij = dist_map.get((i, j), np.inf)\n          dji = dist_map.get((j, i), np.inf)\n          dd = dij if dij < dji else dji\n          if not np.isfinite(dd):\n              dd = 1.0\n          data.append(dd)\n      D = sp.csr_matrix((data, (Acoo.row, Acoo.col)), shape=A_sym.shape)\n      return A_sym.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n \
    \     # Normalize + log\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # EtC embedding: PCA(60) then ComBat on PCs\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      emb = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(adata.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(emb, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(emb.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA(50) on log1p; residualize (BRBG-style) with lam=0.70, gamma_max=0.74\n      adg = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(adata.X, dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(adg, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Zg = np.asarray(adg.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n      lam, gamma_max = 0.70, 0.74\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # Build vanilla kNN on Zcorr (no quotas), binary connectivities + true distances\n      C, D = _build_knn_graph(Zcorr, k=50, metric='cosine')\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/idea_pbve_on_graphpcs_etc_resid_knn.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _pbve_scale_tempered(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray,\n                           t: float = 0.5, rmin: float = 0.8, rmax: float = 1.25, thresh: float = None):\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      gstd = Zc.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      out = Z.copy()\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      for b in cats:\n          mask = (batches == b)\n          Zb = Z[mask]\n          Zb_c = Zb - Zb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n          bstd = Zb_c.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          ratio = (gstd / bstd)\n          if thresh is not None:\n              use = np.abs(np.log(ratio)) > float(thresh)\n          else:\n              use = np.ones_like(ratio, dtype=bool)\n\
    \          r = np.power(np.clip(ratio, rmin, rmax), t)\n          Zb_eq = Zb_c.copy()\n          Zb_eq[:, use] = Zb_c[:, use] * r[use]\n          out[mask] = Zb_eq\n      out = out - out.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return out.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n  def _build_knn_graph(Z, k=50, metric='cosine'):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      rows, cols, vals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          nbrs = idx[i, 1:]\n          rows.extend([i]*k); cols.extend(nbrs.tolist()); vals.extend([1.0]*k)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((vals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T); A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      dist_map = {}\n      for i in range(n):\n          for off, j in enumerate(idx[i, 1:]):\n              dist_map[(i, j)] = d[i, 1:][off]\n      Acoo = A_sym.tocoo()\n      data = []\n      for i, j in zip(Acoo.row,\
    \ Acoo.col):\n          dij = dist_map.get((i, j), np.inf)\n          dji = dist_map.get((j, i), np.inf)\n          dd = dij if dij < dji else dji\n          if not np.isfinite(dd):\n              dd = 1.0\n          data.append(dd)\n      D = sp.csr_matrix((data, (Acoo.row, Acoo.col)), shape=A_sym.shape)\n      return A_sym.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Normalize + log\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # EtC embedding: PCA(60) then ComBat on PCs\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      emb = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(adata.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(emb, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(emb.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA(50) on log1p; residualize,\
    \ then PBVE-lite on Zcorr; kNN graph\n      adg = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(adata.X, dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(adg, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Zg = np.asarray(adg.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n      lam, gamma_max = 0.70, 0.74\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # Apply tempered/clamped PBVE-lite on Zcorr\n      Zcorr_pbve = _pbve_scale_tempered(Zcorr, batches, t=0.5, rmin=0.8, rmax=1.25, thresh=None)\n\n      # Build kNN on Zcorr_pbve\n      C, D = _build_knn_graph(Zcorr_pbve, k=50, metric='cosine')\n    \
    \  adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization baseline: EtC embedding + residualized-graph PCs + kNN50 (no quotas)\"\ntags: \"generalization, etc, residualization, pca, knn\"\nabstract: \"Advanced baseline: EtC embedding (PCA60→ComBat PCs) and a graph built on residualized PCA50 (lam=0.70, γ_max=0.74) without quotas; kNN50 cosine, binary connectivities + true distances. Used to test whether PBVE-lite generalizes beyond the simple PCA+kNN baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from baseline_etc_resid_knn import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as _run\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      return _run(adata)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization of PBVE-lite: apply PBVE to residualized graph PCs in EtC-resid baseline\"\ntags: \"generalization, pbve-lite, etc, residualization,\
    \ pca, knn\"\nabstract: \"Apply tempered/clamped PBVE-lite (t=0.5, clamps [0.8,1.25]) to residualized graph PCs (Zcorr) within the EtC+residualization baseline before kNN50. Tests whether PBVE-lite’s gains are robust on a more advanced pipeline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from idea_pbve_on_graphpcs_etc_resid_knn import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as _run\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      return _run(adata)\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stagnation Protocol I — Tracking (env v4.1)\n  Baseline: PCA60 + kNN50 → EID 1209 = 0.4593\n  Idea 1: PBVE-lite → EID 1210 = 0.6098 (pass vs baseline)\n  Idea 2: Local z-scoring → EID 1212 = 0.4637 (small pass)\n  Idea 3: Mutual-k + top-up → EID 1213 = 0.4639 (small pass)\n  Generalization baseline (EtC+resid kNN): SUBMITTED\n  PBVE-lite generalization on EtC+resid: SUBMITTED\n  Next: wait for generalization results; then write formal paper\
    \ with Intro/Methods/Results/Discussion and full tables.\n```"
