parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 864\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nStagnation Protocol I — Tracking (env v4.1)\nBaseline: PCA60 + kNN50 → EID 1209 = 0.4593\nIdea 1: PBVE-lite → EID 1210 = 0.6098 (pass vs baseline)\nIdea 2: Local z-scoring → EID 1212 = 0.4637 (small pass)\nIdea 3: Mutual-k + top-up → EID 1213 = 0.4639 (small pass)\nGeneralization baseline (EtC+resid kNN): SUBMITTED\nPBVE-lite generalization on EtC+resid: SUBMITTED\nNext: wait for generalization results; then write formal paper with Intro/Methods/Results/Discussion and full tables.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 174,621 / 270,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 185 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour\
    \ submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Generalization baseline: EtC embedding + residualized-graph PCs + kNN50 (no quotas)' (ID: 1216) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6182354072944078\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.615\n**NMI:** 0.693\n**Graph_conn:** 0.878\n**kBET:** 0.782\n**iLISI:** 0.034\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.294\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.615  NMI: 0.693\n  Graph_conn: 0.878  kBET: 0.782  iLISI: 0.034  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.294\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.614690  NMI: 0.693531\n  Graph_conn: 0.880312\
    \  kBET: 0.746258  iLISI: 0.034323  cLISI: 0.996133\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.259294\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1216\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed sparse matrix conversion error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/praxis/baseline_etc_resid_knn.py` at line 63 had a critical bug:\n\n```python\nadg = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(adata.X, dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n```\n\nThe issue:\n- `adata.X` after `sc.pp.log1p()` is a **sparse CSR matrix**\n- `np.asarray()` does not convert sparse matrices to dense arrays directly\n- Instead, it creates an object array containing the sparse matrix as a single element\n- This causes `ValueError: setting an array element with a sequence` when trying to cast to `float32`\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the corrected function:\n\n1. **Kept imports for helper functions** that work correctly:\n   - `_one_hot_batches`\n  \
    \ - `_ridge_fit_predict`\n   - `_build_knn_graph`\n\n2. **Copied and fixed** the buggy `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`:\n   - Added sparse matrix detection: `if sp.issparse(adata.X):`\n   - Proper conversion to dense: `X_dense = adata.X.toarray()`\n   - Safe fallback for already-dense arrays: `else: X_dense = adata.X`\n   - Then convert to float32: `np.asarray(X_dense, dtype=np.float32)`\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Submission v2 created at 2025-10-29T02:59:44\n- Code ran without crashing for >300 seconds\n- This indicates the sparse matrix conversion issue is completely resolved\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix properly handles the sparse matrix by:\n1. Checking if the data is sparse using `sp.issparse()`\n2. Converting to dense array using `.toarray()` method (the correct approach for scipy sparse matrices)\n3. Maintaining backward compatibility for dense arrays\n4. Only then applying the float32 dtype conversion\n\nThis is a common pitfall when working\
    \ with scanpy/anndata, as many preprocessing functions return sparse matrices for memory efficiency, but some downstream operations require dense arrays.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom baseline_etc_resid_knn import _one_hot_batches, _ridge_fit_predict, _build_knn_graph\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Normalize + log\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # EtC embedding: PCA(60) then ComBat on PCs\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    emb = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(adata.obsm['X_pca'],\
    \ dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(emb, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(emb.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Graph path: PCA(50) on log1p; residualize (BRBG-style) with lam=0.70, gamma_max=0.74\n    # FIX: Handle sparse matrix conversion properly\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        X_dense = adata.X.toarray()\n    else:\n        X_dense = adata.X\n    adg = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(X_dense, dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adg, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Zg = np.asarray(adg.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n    lam, gamma_max = 0.70, 0.74\n    gamma\
    \ = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Build vanilla kNN on Zcorr (no quotas), binary connectivities + true distances\n    C, D = _build_knn_graph(Zcorr, k=50, metric='cosine')\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ea12309b-a6f9-4225-aee2-908a2d19ab02/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ea12309b-a6f9-4225-aee2-908a2d19ab02\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Generalization of PBVE-lite: apply PBVE to residualized graph PCs in EtC-resid baseline' (ID: 1217) succeeded\
    \ after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6200962658928435\n**ASW_batch:** 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.615\n**NMI:** 0.693\n**Graph_conn:** 0.878\n**kBET:** 0.781\n**iLISI:** 0.034\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.313\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.615  NMI: 0.693\n  Graph_conn: 0.878  kBET: 0.781  iLISI: 0.034  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.313\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.614690  NMI: 0.693531\n  Graph_conn: 0.880312  kBET: 0.745297  iLISI: 0.034323  cLISI: 0.996133\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.276015\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1217\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The original submission crashed due to attempting to convert a sparse matrix directly to a numpy array. The fix properly handles sparse matrix conversion, allowing the code to run without errors.\n\
    \n## Root Cause\nThe original code at line 85 of the imported function `idea_pbve_on_graphpcs_etc_resid_knn.py` attempted to create an AnnData object using:\n\n```python\nadg = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(adata.X, dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n```\n\nAfter preprocessing steps (`sc.pp.normalize_total` and `sc.pp.log1p`), the `adata.X` matrix remained in sparse CSR format (scipy `csr_matrix`). The `np.asarray()` function cannot directly convert a sparse matrix to a dense array with a specified dtype, resulting in the error:\n\n```\nValueError: setting an array element with a sequence.\n```\n\nThis occurred because `np.asarray()` tried to cast the sparse matrix object itself to float32, rather than converting the sparse data structure to a dense array first.\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe fix was implemented in `submissions/submission_v2.py` by:\n\n1. **Importing helper functions from lineage** - Kept all working helper functions (`_one_hot_batches`, `_ridge_fit_predict`, `_pbve_scale_tempered`,\
    \ `_build_knn_graph`) as imports since they work correctly.\n\n2. **Copying and fixing the main function** - Copied the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function into the submission and modified line 27 (original line 85) to:\n\n```python\nX_dense = adata.X.toarray() if sp.issparse(adata.X) else np.asarray(adata.X, dtype=np.float32)\nadg = ad.AnnData(X_dense.astype(np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n```\n\nThis change:\n- Checks if `adata.X` is sparse using `sp.issparse()`\n- If sparse, uses `.toarray()` to convert to dense numpy array\n- If already dense, uses `np.asarray()` as before\n- Ensures the final array is float32 type\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the fixed code runs successfully without crashing. The evaluation completed the 300-second monitoring period, indicating the algorithm is executing properly (though it may take time to complete the full computation).\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The error was in the lineage function, not the original simple\
    \ submission wrapper\n- Only the buggy function was copied; all working helper functions remained as imports\n- The fix maintains compatibility with both sparse and dense input formats\n- No changes were needed to the algorithm logic itself\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom idea_pbve_on_graphpcs_etc_resid_knn import _one_hot_batches, _ridge_fit_predict, _pbve_scale_tempered, _build_knn_graph\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Normalize + log\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n\
    \    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # EtC embedding: PCA(60) then ComBat on PCs\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    emb = ad.AnnData(np.asarray(adata.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(emb, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(emb.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Graph path: PCA(50) on log1p; residualize, then PBVE-lite on Zcorr; kNN graph\n    # FIX: Convert sparse matrix to dense array using .toarray() if needed\n    X_dense = adata.X.toarray() if sp.issparse(adata.X) else np.asarray(adata.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    adg = ad.AnnData(X_dense.astype(np.float32), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(adg, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Zg = np.asarray(adg.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n    lam, gamma_max = 0.70, 0.74\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Apply tempered/clamped PBVE-lite on Zcorr\n    Zcorr_pbve = _pbve_scale_tempered(Zcorr, batches, t=0.5, rmin=0.8, rmax=1.25, thresh=None)\n\n    # Build kNN on Zcorr_pbve\n    C, D = _build_knn_graph(Zcorr_pbve, k=50, metric='cosine')\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/6a23a39b-da38-4c5d-8728-53721ed4f0e0/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: 6a23a39b-da38-4c5d-8728-53721ed4f0e0\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Aletheia I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 864.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage write praxis/baseline_etc_resid_knn.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write praxis/idea_pbve_on_graphpcs_etc_resid_knn.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: praxis/baseline_etc_resid_knn.py\n- File created successfully: praxis/idea_pbve_on_graphpcs_etc_resid_knn.py\n\
    - Evaluation 'Generalization baseline: EtC embedding + residualized-graph PCs + kNN50 (no quotas)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1216.\n- Evaluation 'Generalization of PBVE-lite: apply PBVE to residualized graph PCs in EtC-resid baseline' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1217.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50)\
    \ | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 928 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05) - RERUN | Logos V | 599 | 0.7454 | 0.789 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.954 | 0.791 |\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 933 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Fine-Grained Delta Sweep (delta=0.025) | Logos V | 601 | 0.7445 | 0.788 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.948 | 0.791 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444 | 0.774 | 0.659\
    \ | 0.248 | 0.347 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 1190 | 1 | Ridge γ_max‑micro: clamp=0.76 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 836 | 0.7431 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 976 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.102 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 622 | 0.7430 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.968 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.960 | 0.788 |\n\nPage 1 of 122 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-122, `/execute_action{rank mode}`\
