parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/embedding_fwpca_knn.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.feature_selection import f_classif\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _to_dense_float32(X):\n      if sp.issparse(X):\n          return X.toarray().astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      return np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n  def _build_knn_graph(Z, k=50, metric='cosine'):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      rows, cols, vals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          nbrs = idx[i, 1:]\n          rows.extend([i]*k)\n          cols.extend(nbrs.tolist())\n          vals.extend([1.0]*k)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((vals, (rows, cols)),\
    \ shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n      A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      # true distances on edges (min of directed if both exist)\n      dist_map = {}\n      for i in range(n):\n          drow = d[i, 1:]; irow = idx[i, 1:]\n          for off, j in enumerate(irow):\n              dist_map[(i, j)] = drow[off]\n      Acoo = A_sym.tocoo()\n      data = []\n      for i, j in zip(Acoo.row, Acoo.col):\n          dij = dist_map.get((i, j), np.inf)\n          dji = dist_map.get((j, i), np.inf)\n          dd = dij if dij < dji else dji\n          if not np.isfinite(dd):\n              dd = 1.0\n          data.append(dd)\n      D = sp.csr_matrix((data, (Acoo.row, Acoo.col)), shape=A_sym.shape, dtype=np.float32)\n      return A_sym.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Normalize + log1p\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4,\
    \ inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # Compute FWPCA weights on genes using batch labels\n      X = _to_dense_float32(adata.X)\n      y = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      # f_classif expects (n_samples, n_features)\n      f_scores, _ = f_classif(X, y)\n      f_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=np.max(np.isfinite(f_scores) and f_scores or [1.0]))\n      # Normalize weights to mean 1.0; alpha=1.0\n      w = f_scores.astype(np.float32)\n      w = w / (np.mean(w) + 1e-8)\n      # Apply column scaling in expression space\n      Xw = X * w[None, :]\n\n      # PCA(60) on weighted expression for embedding\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n\n      # Build vanilla kNN graph on embedding PCs\n      C, D = _build_knn_graph(X_emb, k=50,\
    \ metric='cosine')\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/embedding_fwpca_pbve_knn.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.feature_selection import f_classif\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _to_dense_float32(X):\n      if sp.issparse(X):\n          return X.toarray().astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      return np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n  def _pbve_scale_tempered(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray,\n                           t: float = 0.5, rmin: float = 0.8, rmax: float = 1.25, thresh: float = None):\n      # Global centering and std per PC\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      gstd = Zc.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      out = Z.copy()\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      for b in cats:\n          mask = (batches\
    \ == b)\n          Zb = Z[mask]\n          Zb_c = Zb - Zb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n          bstd = Zb_c.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          ratio = gstd / bstd\n          use = np.ones_like(ratio, dtype=bool) if thresh is None else (np.abs(np.log(ratio)) > float(thresh))\n          r = np.power(np.clip(ratio, rmin, rmax), t)\n          Zb_eq = Zb_c.copy()\n          Zb_eq[:, use] = Zb_c[:, use] * r[use]\n          out[mask] = Zb_eq\n      return (out - out.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n  def _build_knn_graph(Z, k=50, metric='cosine'):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      rows, cols, vals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          nbrs = idx[i, 1:]\n          rows.extend([i]*k)\n          cols.extend(nbrs.tolist())\n          vals.extend([1.0]*k)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((vals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n,\
    \ n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n      A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      # true distances\n      dist_map = {}\n      for i in range(n):\n          drow = d[i, 1:]; irow = idx[i, 1:]\n          for off, j in enumerate(irow):\n              dist_map[(i, j)] = drow[off]\n      Acoo = A_sym.tocoo()\n      data = []\n      for i, j in zip(Acoo.row, Acoo.col):\n          dij = dist_map.get((i, j), np.inf)\n          dji = dist_map.get((j, i), np.inf)\n          dd = dij if dij < dji else dji\n          if not np.isfinite(dd):\n              dd = 1.0\n          data.append(dd)\n      D = sp.csr_matrix((data, (Acoo.row, Acoo.col)), shape=A_sym.shape, dtype=np.float32)\n      return A_sym.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Normalize + log1p\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n \
    \     # FWPCA weights on genes\n      X = _to_dense_float32(adata.X)\n      y = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      f_scores, _ = f_classif(X, y)\n      f_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0)\n      w = f_scores.astype(np.float32) / (np.mean(f_scores) + 1e-8)\n      Xw = X * w[None, :]\n\n      # PCA(60) for embedding\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # PBVE-lite in PC space (tempered/clamped)\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').to_numpy()\n      X_emb_pbve = _pbve_scale_tempered(X_emb, batches, t=0.5, rmin=0.8, rmax=1.25, thresh=None)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb_pbve\n\n      # Build vanilla kNN on PBVE-transformed PCs\n      C, D = _build_knn_graph(X_emb_pbve, k=50, metric='cosine')\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances']\
    \ = D\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FWPCA embedding baseline: PCA60(F‑weighted) + kNN50 (cosine), binary\"\ntags: \"fwpca, embedding, baseline, pca, knn, graph\"\nabstract: \"Implements a Feature‑Weighted PCA embedding using per‑gene ANOVA F‑scores on batches; runs PCA(60) on weighted expression and builds a vanilla kNN50 (cosine), binary connectivities + true distances. Tests FWPCA alone on the simple scaffold.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from embedding_fwpca_knn import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as _run\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      return _run(adata)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FWPCA + PBVE‑lite (t=0.5, clamp[0.8,1.25]) on embedding PCs → kNN50 (cosine)\"\ntags: \"fwpca, pbve-lite, embedding, pca, knn, graph\"\nabstract: \"Applies PBVE‑lite in PC space on top of a Feature‑Weighted PCA embedding, then builds vanilla kNN50 (cosine),\
    \ binary connectivities + true distances. Tests synergy vs redundancy of variance‑based methods on the simple scaffold.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from embedding_fwpca_pbve_knn import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as _run\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      return _run(adata)\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Follow-up (env v4.1): FWPCA × PBVE-lite synergy\n  - Submitted: FWPCA embedding baseline; FWPCA + PBVE-lite on embedding PCs.\n  - Gates: seed-avg Δ≥+0.001, cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\n  - Next: record vectors/EIDs; if synergy, write addendum to Archive #35; if redundant, report as negative synergy.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing PCA with adata.X**\n\nI’m working with adata.X, which is likely sparse after applying log1p. It seems that scanpy PCA can handle sparse data with TruncatedSVD, but arpack generally needs dense input. However, scanpy's PCA appears to support sparse, potentially densifying it. In earlier debugging, I found an issue with converting adata.X to a separate object. Here, I could reuse adata.X or convert it to dense with toarray carefully. Implementing FWPCA will involve weighting features based on variance or ANOVA F-statistic across batches.**Simplifying embedding path**\n\nI need to compute the F-statistic for each gene using one-way ANOVA across batches by applying group means and variances formulas. I can also utilize sklearn.feature_selection.f_classif, but that requires labels. However, batch labels are permissible for the embedding path. I need to implement the FWPCA with an alpha parameter to control the weighting exponent and then run PCA on the weighted\
  \ expression. \n\nThe first step is to create the script \"praxis/embedding_fwpca_knn.py\" for normalizing, applying weights, and producing the final embeddings using PCA.**Setting up the pipeline**\n\nAfter computing X_emb (the principal components), I'll apply PBVE-lite scaling across batches on X_emb, similar to before but not on Z. Once that's done, I can perform kNN on these transformed PCs since the baseline kNN uses X_emb as well. It's also an option to store X_emb in adata.obsm for graph purposes, which seems fine.\n\nNow, regarding the EtC and residual baseline, I'll incorporate FWPCA into the embedding and later residualize Zcorr as before. We can see how FWPCA embedding interacts with PBVE-lite, focusing specifically on variance-based approaches.**Planning minimal tests**\n\nI need to start with a minimal test using FWPCA embedding on a simple baseline and then apply PBVE-lite on top of that. The goal is to compare this with the baseline. For the advanced baseline, I'll want\
  \ to use FWPCA instead of EtC, possibly incorporating a residualized graph path and applying PBVE-lite as an option.\n\nIt seems prudent to proceed stepwise: first, submit the FWPCA embedding baseline and then try FWPCA + PBVE-lite. After that, we can log results. If everything goes well, I could write a short update for Archive 35, but let's see what happens!**Implementing the code**\n\nI'm ready to implement the code in \"praxis/embedding_fwpca_knn.py.\" First, if there are counts present, I'll set adata.X accordingly. Next, I'll normalize this data and compute the F-statistic per gene using batch means and variances. For simplicity, I can use sklearn's f_classif, which will require converting adata.X to a dense array if it's sparse.\n\nAfter calculating the F-scores, I'll apply the necessary weights and then perform PCA to reduce dimensions. After computing the principal components (X_emb), I'll build the kNN graph. \n\nI also need to write a second file, \"praxis/embedding_fwpca_pbve_knn.py,\"\
  \ where I apply PBVE-lite in the PC space and reuse some previous functions to create the adjacency and distance metrics. Finally, I’ll log everything and submit my evaluations along with relevant tags."
