- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 871\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nFollow-up (env v4.1): FWPCA × PBVE-lite synergy\n- Submitted: FWPCA embedding baseline; FWPCA + PBVE-lite on embedding PCs.\n- Gates: seed-avg Δ≥+0.001, cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\n- Next: record vectors/EIDs; if synergy, write addendum to Archive #35; if redundant, report as negative synergy.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 202,122 / 270,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 192 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1225**\n\nEvaluation '1225' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1226**\n\nEvaluation '1226' is still pending. Please\
    \ try again later.\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Aethel I** (An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'FWPCA + PBVE‑lite (t=0.5, clamp[0.8,1.25]) on embedding PCs → kNN50 (cosine)' (ID: 1226) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.34761360736857083\n**ASW_batch:** 0.171\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.054\n**NMI:** 0.210\n**Graph_conn:** 0.443\n**kBET:** 0.602\n**iLISI:** 0.000\n**cLISI:** 0.736\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.260\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.171  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.054  NMI: 0.210\n  Graph_conn: 0.443  kBET: 0.602  iLISI: 0.000  cLISI: 0.736\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.260\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.610340  ASW_label: 0.348373  ARI: 0.053440  NMI: 0.210293\n  Graph_conn: 0.452387  kBET: 0.577345  iLISI: 0.000000\
    \  cLISI: 0.923227\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.230952\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/d7af7a7c-0872-42b6-9d31-c856db43fbbc/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: d7af7a7c-0872-42b6-9d31-c856db43fbbc\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/sklearn/feature_selection/_univariate_selection.py:111: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  f = msb / msw\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nYour research submission 'FWPCA embedding baseline: PCA60(F‑weighted) + kNN50 (cosine), binary' (ID: 1225) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.21018770824093358\n**ASW_batch:** 0.000\n\
    **ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.055\n**NMI:** 0.211\n**Graph_conn:** 0.364\n**kBET:** 0.451\n**iLISI:** 0.000\n**cLISI:** 0.743\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.279\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.000  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.055  NMI: 0.211\n  Graph_conn: 0.364  kBET: 0.451  iLISI: 0.000  cLISI: 0.743\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.279\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.419329  ASW_label: 0.156231  ARI: 0.054636  NMI: 0.210783\n  Graph_conn: 0.374837  kBET: 0.434830  iLISI: 0.000000  cLISI: 0.925219\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.246509\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1225\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the ValueError in the FWPCA embedding code. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a bug in `storage/praxis/embedding_fwpca_knn.py` at line 59:\n\n```python\nf_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=np.max(np.isfinite(f_scores)\
    \ and f_scores or [1.0]))\n```\n\nThe issue was the expression `np.isfinite(f_scores) and f_scores`, which attempts to use a boolean array in a logical `and` operation. This raises:\n```\nValueError: The truth value of an array with more than one element is ambiguous. Use a.any() or a.all()\n```\n\nThis is a common numpy pitfall - you cannot use boolean arrays with Python's `and`/`or` operators because the truth value of an array with multiple elements is ambiguous.\n\n## Fix Applied\nI copied the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function from the lineage file into `submissions/submission_v2.py` and fixed the buggy line:\n\n**Original buggy code:**\n```python\nf_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=np.max(np.isfinite(f_scores) and f_scores or [1.0]))\n```\n\n**Fixed code:**\n```python\nfinite_mask = np.isfinite(f_scores)\nfinite_values = f_scores[finite_mask] if finite_mask.any() else np.array([1.0])\nf_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=np.max(finite_values))\n\
    ```\n\nThe fix:\n1. Creates a boolean mask of finite values\n2. Extracts finite values using array indexing (or defaults to `[1.0]` if none exist)\n3. Uses `finite_mask.any()` for the conditional check, which returns a single boolean\n4. Passes the extracted finite values to `np.max()`\n\nI also kept the imports for the helper functions `_to_dense_float32` and `_build_knn_graph` from the lineage file since they work correctly.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success with exit code 0:\n- The code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- This indicates the fix resolved the ValueError and the algorithm is executing properly\n- The evaluation is taking time to complete (likely due to PCA and kNN computations on 20,000 cells)\n\n## Implementation Notes\n- **Version:** submission_v2.py\n- **Approach:** Copied only the buggy function, fixed the boolean logic error\n- **Imports:** Maintained working helper functions from lineage directory\n- **Status:** Running without crashes\
    \ (success criteria met)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.feature_selection import f_classif\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n# Import helper functions that work correctly\nfrom embedding_fwpca_knn import _to_dense_float32, _build_knn_graph\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Normalize + log1p\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # Compute FWPCA weights on genes using batch labels\n    X = _to_dense_float32(adata.X)\n    y = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n\
    \    # f_classif expects (n_samples, n_features)\n    f_scores, _ = f_classif(X, y)\n    # FIX: Replace buggy boolean logic with proper numpy array indexing\n    # Original line: f_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=np.max(np.isfinite(f_scores) and f_scores or [1.0]))\n    # The issue: \"np.isfinite(f_scores) and f_scores\" causes \"ambiguous truth value\" error\n    # Fix: Use array indexing to get finite values, or default to [1.0] if none exist\n    finite_mask = np.isfinite(f_scores)\n    finite_values = f_scores[finite_mask] if finite_mask.any() else np.array([1.0])\n    f_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=np.max(finite_values))\n\n    # Normalize weights to mean 1.0; alpha=1.0\n    w = f_scores.astype(np.float32)\n    w = w / (np.mean(w) + 1e-8)\n    # Apply column scaling in expression space\n    Xw = X * w[None, :]\n\n    # PCA(60) on weighted expression for embedding\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb,\
    \ n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    X_emb = np.asarray(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n\n    # Build vanilla kNN graph on embedding PCs\n    C, D = _build_knn_graph(X_emb, k=50, metric='cosine')\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/24571e13-1982-49eb-9503-185f01f799f0/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 24571e13-1982-49eb-9503-185f01f799f0\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/sklearn/feature_selection/_univariate_selection.py:111:\
    \ RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  f = msb / msw\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1225` (in Research Counter);\n2. `review 1226` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation '1225' is still running. Please try again later.\n- Evaluation '1226' is still running. Please try again later.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10\
    \ (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 928 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05) - RERUN | Logos V | 599 | 0.7454 | 0.789 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.954 | 0.791 |\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 933 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Fine-Grained Delta Sweep (delta=0.025) | Logos V | 601 | 0.7445 | 0.788 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.948 | 0.791 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444\
