- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/fwpca_pbve_synergy_results.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  FWPCA × PBVE‑lite (env v4.1) — Synergy check on simple scaffold\n  Scaffold: PCA60‑derived embedding; vanilla kNN50 (cosine), binary; graphs used as‑is.\n\n  Results (spec‑ordered vectors)\n  - FWPCA embedding baseline (EID 1225): score 0.2102\n    [ASW_batch 0.000, ASW_label 0.000, ARI 0.055, NMI 0.211, Graph_conn 0.364, kBET 0.451, iLISI 0.000, cLISI 0.743, PCR 0.000, Cell_cycle 0.279]\n  - FWPCA + PBVE‑lite on embedding PCs (EID 1226): score 0.3476\n    [ASW_batch 0.171, ASW_label 0.000, ARI 0.054, NMI 0.210, Graph_conn 0.443, kBET 0.602, iLISI 0.000, cLISI 0.736, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.260]\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - FWPCA alone on this brittle PCA+kNN scaffold underperforms strongly (mixing and connectivity collapse).\n  - PBVE‑lite improves FWPCA’s result but remains far below the PCA+kNN baseline (EID 1209=0.4593).\n  - Conclusion: No positive\
    \ synergy on this scaffold; variance‑based FWPCA weighting appears misaligned here (emphasizes batch‑discriminative axes), and PBVE‑lite cannot rescue the collapse.\n```\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 35}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum — FWPCA × PBVE‑lite on the simple scaffold (env v4.1)\n  We tested the reviewer’s suggestion by applying FWPCA to the embedding on the PCA+kNN scaffold, with and without PBVE‑lite on the embedding PCs.\n\n  Results (spec‑ordered vectors):\n  - FWPCA embedding baseline (EID 1225): score 0.2102\n    [0.000, 0.000, 0.055, 0.211, 0.364, 0.451, 0.000, 0.743, 0.000, 0.279]\n  - FWPCA + PBVE‑lite on embedding PCs (EID 1226): score 0.3476\n    [0.171, 0.000, 0.054, 0.210, 0.443, 0.602, 0.000, 0.736, 1.000, 0.260]\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - On this brittle scaffold, FWPCA alone collapses mixing and connectivity; PBVE‑lite partially mitigates but remains far below the PCA+kNN baseline (0.4593).\n  - We find no positive synergy in this context;\
    \ the two variance‑based operations appear redundant or misaligned on this simple pipeline.\n  - We will consider testing PBVE‑lite with FWPCA in a stronger setting (e.g., FWPCA for embedding combined with a residualized graph path) under seed‑averaged gates, but based on these results we do not recommend the FWPCA+PBVE‑lite combination on a vanilla PCA+kNN graph.\n```\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Follow-up (env v4.1): FWPCA × PBVE-lite\n  - EID 1225 (FWPCA emb): 0.2102; EID 1226 (FWPCA+PBVE): 0.3476 → negative synergy on simple scaffold.\n  - Logged results; Archive #35 addendum posted (no synergy).\n  - Next: optional check on stronger scaffold (FWPCA for embedding + residualized graph path) under seed-avg gates; otherwise pivot back to cross-organ runbook and diagnostics.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating FWPCA results**\n\nOverall, it looks like FWPCA is not performing well on the baseline. It might stem from the F scores from ANOVA using batch labels, dramatically impacting weights. Despite testing for synergy, results show that PBVE-lite can't salvage the poor FWPCA performance; synergy isn't there. I need to log the results, update details for Archive #35 with a report on negative synergy experiments, and consider adjusting FWPCA weights while following the outlined action plan. Time to execute those commands!**Planning next steps**\n\nMy plan includes writing a log file that summarizes the FWPCA baseline and FWPCA+PBVE results with vectors and EIDs. Next, I need to reply to Archive #35, summarizing the negative synergy outcome of the FWPCA × PBVE-lite experiment. While PBVE-lite shows slight help, the overall performance is still poor, possibly due to FWPCA highlighting batch-discriminative genes. \n\nI might also propose the next steps, such as adjusting\
  \ the FWPCA alpha or using feature weighting via ANOVA F-stat on another dataset. Including the idea of testing PBVE-lite with FWPCA embedding could be beneficial too!**Evaluating options for FWPCA results**\n\nI have another option to consider: the FWPCA embedding baseline is poor, so maybe there's no need to continue. However, there was a suggestion for synergy with FWPCA, which our results indicate is negative. I’ll prepare a reply for Archive #35, possibly creating \"archive_35-4\" for that. \n\nI also might update public memory and set the meta to show that we’ve confirmed the negative synergy in this follow-up. Actions include writing logs for the FWPCA-PBVE synergy results and replying with a concise summary of methods, results, and conclusions.**Preparing Archive reply**\n\nIt's allowed to respond to the archive while avoiding code paths, so I plan to include EIDs and their corresponding vectors. For message 1225, I have a score of 0.2102 with the vector values listed. For 1226,\
  \ the score is 0.3476, and I'll ensure that the vector order is consistent.\n\nI think it's also worth proposing that weighting by batch F-scores may over-emphasize batch-discriminative genes, leading to mixing issues. I should add a note of caution regarding the differences in using FWPCA in embedding versus the previous pipeline, confirming that the synergy outcome remains negative for the simple baseline. I might also update private memory for this!**Submitting actions**\n\nI need to proceed and submit the necessary actions now. First, I’ll write the logs file to storage. Then, I'll reply to Archive #35 with an addendum summary that captures the important details. Finally, it’s time to update the meta accordingly. I want to ensure that everything is organized and clear, so I’ll produce the necessary commands to get these tasks completed efficiently. Let’s get this done!"
