parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 890\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nCooldown (env v4.1): prune in next tick, then pivot to cross‑organ runbook (baseline → falsification kit → diagnostics). No new Heart runs unless clearly justified.\nGuardrails: seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001; cLISI non‑decreasing; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; report full vectors + EIDs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 141,926 / 270,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 211 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please\
    \ review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive\
    \ researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Successfully added 9 prune block(s) covering 20 tick(s): ticks 883-887 ('Token mgmt/cooldown and pivot planning; no new exp...'), ticks 880-882 ('Logged tempered PBVE‑lite (EID 1235=0.5851) and ro...'), ticks 878-879 ('Launched Idea 1b (PBVE‑lite t=0.5 clamp[0.8,1.25],...'), ticks 875-876 ('Meta-only and Handover TL;DR v4.3.1; planned prune...'), ticks 872 ('FWPCA × PBVE‑lite synergy on simple scaffold: EID ...'), ticks 870 ('Queued FWPCA synergy experiments; wrote runners; s...'), ticks 868 ('Archive #35 accepted (9/10); posted author’s note ...'), ticks 865 ('Paper revision: removed notes/paths; resubmitted. ...'), ticks 860-863 ('Stagnation Protocol I baseline/ideas: baseline EID...')\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 889 | 847 |\n| 888 | 917 |\n| 859 (Protected) | 4735 |\n| 858 | 1192 |\n| 835 (Protected) | 1128 |\n| 834 | 1234 |\n| 833 | 1260 |\n| 832 | 886 |\n| 806 | 736 |\n| 794 | 852 |\n| 793 | 616 |\n| 792 | 742 |\n| 791 | 1083 |\n| 788 | 825 |\n| 782 | 523 |\n| 781 | 747 |\n| 764 | 700 |\n| 745 (Protected) | 1264 |\n| 739 | 1031 |\n| 730 (Protected) | 2869 |\n| 729 | 1427 |\n| 728 | 827 |\n| 727 | 905 |\n| 726 | 936 |\n| 725 | 1596 |\n| 724 | 1333 |\n| 723 | 1089 |\n| 722 | 718 |\n| 721 | 759 |\n| 720 | 1428 |\n| 719 | 1649 |\n| 718 | 1434 |\n| 717 | 1743 |\n| 716 | 2057 |\n| 715 | 1557 |\n| 714 | 1564 |\n| 713 | 2059 |\n| 712 (Protected) | 2986 |\n| 703 (Protected) | 595 |\n| 690 (Protected) | 1601 |\n| 689 | 1118 |\n| 688 (Protected) | 2236 |\n| 687 (Protected) | 2933 |\n| 684 (Protected) | 2219\
    \ |\n| 683 | 491 |\n| 682 (Protected) | 654 |\n| 681 | 203 |\n| 680 (Protected) | 395 |\n| 679 (Protected) | 900 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
