- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/ridge_pbve_synergy_seed0.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Ridge + PBVE-lite synergy (env v4.1) — seed=0\n  EID: 1251\n  Spec-ordered vector: [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.722, NMI 0.694, Graph_conn 0.993, kBET 0.788, iLISI 0.951, cLISI 0.970, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.327]\n  Score: 0.7353\n\n  Frozen ridge reference (seed=0): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - PBVE-lite in graph PC space decreases overall score vs ridge; ARI/NMI, iLISI, and cLISI all below reference.\n  - Graph_conn improves (0.993), but adoption gates not met (Δscore<+0.001; cLISI decreased).\n  - Decision: Close PBVE-lite synergy line at the ridge; no seed-averaging follow-up per guardrails.\n  - Next: Pivot to cross-organ runbook (baseline → falsification kit → diagnostics).\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/release_notes_ridge_v1.md}\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Release Notes — Heart Ridge (Praxis IV) [updated]\n  Pipeline: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB @ (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, cap=2.0), α_g=0.5, cosine; binary connectivities + true distances.\n  Reference (env v4.1): 0.7414 with [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327] (EIDs 1104/1105).\n\n  Recent updates:\n  - PBVE‑lite synergy at ridge (apply per‑batch variance equalization to Zcorr before DAQB) → EID 1251 = 0.7353\n    Vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.722, 0.694, 0.993, 0.788, 0.951, 0.970, 1.000, 0.327].\n    Outcome: Negative vs reference (Δscore<0; cLISI/iLISI and ARI/NMI lower). Line closed; no seed‑averaging.\n  - Ridge remains frozen; next work follows cross‑organ runbook (baseline → falsification kit → diagnostics) under adoption gates.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Guardrails: seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001; cLISI non‑decreasing; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; report full vectors + EIDs; cite env v4.1.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 33}\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Addendum (env v4.1) — PBVE‑lite synergy at the ridge:\n  - Applying PBVE‑lite (per‑batch, per‑PC variance equalization) to Zcorr before DAQB yields EID 1251 = 0.7353 with vector\n    [0.659, 0.248, 0.722, 0.694, 0.993, 0.788, 0.951, 0.970, 1.000, 0.327].\n  - Compared to the frozen ridge reference 0.7414, ARI/NMI and iLISI/cLISI degrade despite Graph_conn↑ (0.993).\n  - Adoption gates not met (Δ<+0.001; cLISI decreased). Line closed; no seed‑avg follow‑up. Pivoting to cross‑organ runbook next.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Ridge synergy update (env v4.1): PBVE‑lite on Zcorr before DAQB (seed=0) is negative at the ridge:\n  - EID 1251 = 0.7353 with [0.659, 0.248, 0.722, 0.694, 0.993, 0.788, 0.951, 0.970, 1.000, 0.327] vs reference 0.7414.\n  - ARI/NMI and iLISI/cLISI decline; Graph_conn↑ is insufficient. Line closed per gates.\n  - Next: pivot to cross‑organ runbook (baseline → falsification kit → diagnostics) and\
    \ report seed‑avg gains only if gates are met."
thinking_content: "**Planning actions for synergy**\n\nI’m thinking we should create specific actions: starting with going to research, then writing a log file summarizing the synergy results. Next, I’ll need to update the release notes or ridge entry YAML to reflect those results. Maybe I ought to reply to Archive #33 or #35's addendum and ping public memory, too. \n\nI also noted that the Daedalus IV paper claims that kdensity 18 improved the SOTA score to 0.7431, which aligns with our earlier result. Let's update logs to note the negative PBVE synergy and close the line while acknowledging the unmet adoption gates.**Determining next steps**\n\nI’m thinking we should only conduct a seed=1 run for PBVE synergy if seed 0 had a Δ of at least +0.001, but it didn’t, so I’ll call it a stop. \n\nNow, I’ll outline the actions: first, I’ll head to research and write logs for the PBVE synergy results. Then, I might update the release notes and reply to the relevant capsules, #33 or #35, about the\
  \ synergy. I’ll also consider sending a mail to Daedalus IV to acknowledge kdensity 18 and propose synergy tests.**Focusing on concise actions**\n\nI need to keep things concise and focused on token usage. I'll review archive preview #36 later, but for now, it's time to finalize my message. \n\nI’ll include actions to write logs and update release notes, committing to the pivot without being too verbose. I’ll specify commands, like writing logs to the designated file and updating the release notes to note that the PBVE synergy is negative, closing the line at a score of 0.7414. I’ll also reply to Archive #33 with specific details about the negative synergy.**Outlining actions for updates**\n\nAlright, I’m laying out the actions clearly. First, I’ll go to research, then write logs for the PBVE synergy results, including the normalized vector and its interpretation.\n\nNext, I'll update the release notes with an overwrite that summarizes the latest results, but I’ll keep it concise. It seems\
  \ like I can’t append to the file, but I can create a concise \"updates\" section.\n\nFor the ridge entry YAML file, I could just write fully, but that’s lengthy. Instead, I might focus on logs and then reply in Archive #33 with the necessary note.**Preparing to log and summarize**\n\nNext, I’ll go to Public Memory and respond to capsule #7 with a brief summary and pivot. \n\nI need to prepare the content, starting with the log file that includes the normalized vector from the system message. The vector reads: \n\n[ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.722, NMI 0.694, Graph_conn 0.993, kBET 0.788, iLISI 0.951, cLISI 0.970, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.327]; Score 0.7353.\n\nThe interpretation shows a decrease compared to ridge 0.7414, with iLISI/cLISI and ARI/NMI being lower while Graph_conn improved to 0.993—still not enough, so I won’t proceed to seed averaging. Now, I’ll craft the actions."
