  \ with specific parameters.\n\nFor handling the clip, I’ll create a new file \"mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe_clip.py\" to manage clip integration more smoothly.**Planning file storage and experiments**\n\nI’m organizing my code storage, starting with writing \"mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe.py\", \"best_anscombe_k50.py\", \"best_anscombe_k52.py\", \"mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe_clip.py\", and \"best_anscombe_k50_clip6288.py\".\n\nNext, I need to submit two experiments. I'll start with the anscombe baseline (k=50) to generate an EID, although we previously had EIDs 1171 and 1175 for our anscombe variant. \n\nTo meet the review requirements for experiments, I’ll run two additional probes on the baseline: k=52 and clip, which will bring my total to six experiments, as suggested.**Updating logs and managing tasks**\n\nI need to include content logs and update the release notes, but I want to keep it minimal. Managing token usage is also important; I've used about 121k tokens, which is 45%, so that's acceptable\
  \ for now. \n\nFirst, I’ll ensure proper YAML formatting, especially when there are colons in titles. Then, I’ll proceed with several actions, including writing \"mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe.py\" using the anscombe transform and reusing the build_density_adaptive_bbsg. \n\nFor runner k50, I'll create \"best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_anscombe.py\" and for k52, \"best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k52_anscombe.py\". I'll handle the clip version with \"mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe_clip.py\" to import the clip builder, using specific values, and then implement the clip runner. Finally, I'll submit evaluations for both k=52 anscombe and anscombe clip.**Composing the code structure**\n\nI need to provide the code carefully, making sure to include all necessary imports and function names. The evaluation calls will reference the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` in the content stub that imports from the runner file, which seems fine.\n\nNext, I should create the appropriate actions based on this structure. Maybe adding small logs to\
