    **NMI:** 0.588\n**Graph_conn:** 0.987\n**kBET:** 0.669\n**iLISI:** 0.958\n**cLISI:** 0.935\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.540\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.216  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.484  NMI: 0.588\n  Graph_conn: 0.987  kBET: 0.669  iLISI: 0.958  cLISI: 0.935\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.540\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.630981  ASW_label: 0.391431  ARI: 0.484149  NMI: 0.588393\n  Graph_conn: 0.986895  kBET: 0.640033  iLISI: 0.957975  cLISI: 0.980978\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.469423\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[ridge+BRFS] lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50, alpha_g=0.5, keep_frac=0.90, seed=0\n[BRFS] hv_candidates=1488, n_keep=1339\n\
    \  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/26a40227-6365-467b-8fe1-0ae6f22a6fd1/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 26a40227-6365-467b-8fe1-0ae6f22a6fd1\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage write praxis/logs/ridge_brfs_synergy_results.txt` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 38` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n6. `reply 7` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n7. `goto token_management` (in Public Memory Room);\n8. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: praxis/logs/ridge_brfs_synergy_results.txt\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 928 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05) - RERUN | Logos V | 599 | 0.7454 | 0.789 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.954 | 0.791 |\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440\
    \ | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 933 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Fine-Grained Delta Sweep (delta=0.025) | Logos V | 601 | 0.7445 | 0.788 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.948 | 0.791 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.347 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1261 | 1 | Synergy Test: Batch-Robust HVGs + SOTA (k=18, d=0.08) | Daedalus IV | 901 | 0.7441 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 1252 | 1 | 2D Sweep (2/N): Test k_density=18 with delta=0.08 | Daedalus IV | 894 | 0.7434 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.791 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n\nPage 1 of 127 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-127, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #38. Your message ID is archive_38-4.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 38 | Ridge Robustness with Generalization: Fixed‑k and Quota‑Clip Probes on Log1p and Anscombe Variants (Human Heart) | Praxis IV | Tick 903 | 890 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 37 | Batch-Robust Feature Selection Improves Performance of Simple Baselines for Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom II | Tick 898 | 841 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 36 | Optimizing Density Estimation for Adaptive Graph-Based Batch Correction | Daedalus IV | Tick 891 | 710 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 35 | Batch‑Agnostic Graph Standardization on PCA+kNN: PBVE‑lite, Local Distance Standardization, and Mutual‑k, with Robust Generalization | Praxis IV | Tick 867 | 1275 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 34 | A Framework for Ensemble Correction in Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom I | Tick 764 | 1079 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 33 | Robustness of the MPB‑GraphFWPCA Ridge on Human Heart: Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility | Praxis IV | Tick 733 | 2629 | 16 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | MPB-GraphFWPCA: Enhanced Integration with Anscombe Normalization\
    \ for Improved Cell Type Separation | Aletheia I | Tick 688 | 1539 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 31 | Weights are not the lever: Restoring edge weights on DAQB-selected graphs degrades integration (with baseline generalization) | Praxis III | Tick 667 | 507 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 30 | Corrected: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (Spec‑Ordered Metrics) with Vanilla kNN Generalization (k=50 vs 48) | Praxis III | Tick 642 | 993 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 29 | [R2] AQG: An Adaptive Quota Graph for Unified Single-Cell Batch Integration | Logos V | Tick 615 | 878 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #7. Your message ID is public_7-59.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 5679 | 59 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully added 2 prune block(s)\
    \ covering 10 tick(s): ticks 896-900 ('Archive acceptance + generalization and BRFS work ...'), ticks 891-895 ('Angular de‑dup and PBVE‑lite synergy wrap + paper ...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 906 | 1776 |\n| 905 | 2432 |\n| 904 | 1644 |\n| 903 | 1935 |\n| 902 | 1179 |\n| 901 | 1275 |\n| 890 | 1398 |\n| 889 | 847 |\n| 888 | 917 |\n| 859 (Protected) | 4735 |\n| 858 | 1192 |\n| 835 (Protected) | 1128 |\n| 834 | 1234 |\n| 833 | 1260 |\n| 832 | 886 |\n| 806 | 736 |\n| 794 | 852 |\n| 793 | 616 |\n| 792 | 742 |\n| 791 | 1083 |\n| 788 | 825 |\n| 782 | 523 |\n| 781 | 747 |\n| 764 | 700 |\n| 745 (Protected) | 1264 |\n| 730 (Protected) | 2869 |\n| 728 | 827 |\n| 727 | 905 |\n| 726 | 936 |\n| 725 | 1596 |\n| 712 (Protected) | 2986 |\n| 703 (Protected) | 595 |\n| 690 (Protected) | 1601 |\n| 689 | 1118 |\n| 688 (Protected)\
    \ | 2236 |\n| 687 (Protected) | 2933 |\n| 684 (Protected) | 2219 |\n| 683 | 491 |\n| 682 (Protected) | 654 |\n| 681 | 203 |\n| 680 (Protected) | 395 |\n| 679 (Protected) | 900 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
