- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 910\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nCooldown (env v4.1): prune in next tick, then pivot to cross‑organ runbook (baseline → falsification kit → diagnostics). No new Heart runs unless clearly justified.\nGuardrails: seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001; cLISI non‑decreasing; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; report full vectors + EIDs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 135,173 / 270,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 231 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1269**\n\nEvaluation '1269' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1270**\n\nEvaluation '1270' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research\
    \ submission 'Idea 5: Drop top-3 PCs (global) before kNN — PCA(63)→keep 60, k=50' (ID: 1270) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.4603873046450295\n**ASW_batch:** 0.699\n**ASW_label:** 0.177\n**ARI:** 0.340\n**NMI:** 0.579\n**Graph_conn:** 0.934\n**kBET:** 0.761\n**iLISI:** 0.011\n**cLISI:** 0.942\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.160\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.699  ASW_label: 0.177  ARI: 0.340  NMI: 0.579\n  Graph_conn: 0.934  kBET: 0.761  iLISI: 0.011  cLISI: 0.942\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.160\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.848520  ASW_label: 0.513612  ARI: 0.340114  NMI: 0.578801\n  Graph_conn: 0.935362  kBET: 0.726584  iLISI: 0.011303  cLISI: 0.983134\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.145785\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\n\
    Found eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/9547c5cd-69bf-4482-b76c-2618a6a5846a/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 9547c5cd-69bf-4482-b76c-2618a6a5846a\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Idea 1t: PBVE‑lite with threshold (t=0.5, clamp=[0.8,1.25], τ=0.20) on PCA(60) → kNN(k=50)' (ID: 1269) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5848134158554223\n**ASW_batch:** 0.675\n**ASW_label:** 0.222\n**ARI:** 0.463\n**NMI:** 0.668\n**Graph_conn:** 0.876\n**kBET:** 0.607\n**iLISI:** 0.007\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.341\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.675  ASW_label: 0.222  ARI: 0.463  NMI: 0.668\n  Graph_conn: 0.876  kBET: 0.607  iLISI: 0.007  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.341\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.837454  ASW_label: 0.539805  ARI: 0.462567  NMI: 0.667595\n  Graph_conn: 0.878285  kBET: 0.582025  iLISI: 0.006682  cLISI: 0.997238\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.299407\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1269\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed IndexError in the PBVE-lite batch integration algorithm. The code now runs without crashing and executes the batch effect removal successfully.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported a function from the agent's lineage file (`storage/praxis/idea_pbve_knn_thresh.py`) that contained a critical bug. In the `_pbve_scale_thresh` function on line 65, the code attempted to index `sigma_g` as a 2D array with `sigma_g[0, need]`, but `sigma_g` was actually a 1D array (computed with `.std(axis=0, ddof=1)` on line 52).\n\nThe error was:\n```\nIndexError: too many indices for array: array is 1-dimensional, but 2 were indexed\n```\n\nThis occurred because `sigma_g` represents the standard deviation along axis\
    \ 0, which produces a 1D array of shape `(n_features,)`, not a 2D array.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied all required functions** from the lineage file into the submission:\n   - `_build_knn_graph` - kNN graph construction\n   - `_pbve_scale_thresh` - PBVE scaling with threshold (contained the bug)\n   - `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` - Main entry point\n\n2. **Fixed the indexing bug** on line 67 of submission_v2.py:\n   - **Before**: `r[need] = np.power((sigma_g[0, need] / sigma_b[need]), float(t))`\n   - **After**: `r[need] = np.power((sigma_g[need] / sigma_b[need]), float(t))`\n\n   Removed the erroneous `[0, ...]` indexing since `sigma_g` is already a 1D array.\n\n3. **Removed the external import** and replaced it with the corrected inline implementation.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the fixed code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without any crashes, indicating that:\n- The IndexError was resolved\n\
    - The PCA transformation completed\n- The PBVE-lite algorithm executed without errors\n- The kNN graph construction completed\n\nThe code is now functioning correctly and performing batch effect removal as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _build_knn_graph(Z, k=50, metric='cosine'):\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    d, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    rows, cols, vals = [], [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        nbrs = idx[i, 1:]\n        rows.extend([i]*k)\n        cols.extend(nbrs.tolist())\n        vals.extend([1.0]*k)\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((vals,\
    \ (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T); A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    # Distances: true distances for present edges (min of directed if both exist)\n    dist_map = {}\n    for i in range(n):\n        for off, j in enumerate(idx[i, 1:]):\n            dist_map[(i, int(j))] = float(d[i, 1:][off])\n    Acoo = A_sym.tocoo()\n    data = []\n    for i, j in zip(Acoo.row, Acoo.col):\n        dij = dist_map.get((int(i), int(j)), np.inf)\n        dji = dist_map.get((int(j), int(i)), np.inf)\n        dd = dij if dij < dji else dji\n        if not np.isfinite(dd):\n            dd = 1.0\n        data.append(dd)\n    D = sp.csr_matrix((np.array(data, dtype=np.float32), (Acoo.row, Acoo.col)), shape=A_sym.shape)\n    return A_sym.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\ndef _pbve_scale_thresh(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, t: float = 0.5,\n                       clamp: tuple = (0.8, 1.25), tau: float = 0.20) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    PBVE-lite with thresholding:\n      - For each\
    \ PC j, compute global std σj and per-batch std σb,j after batchwise centering.\n      - For batches where |log(σb,j/σj)| > tau, scale by r(b,j) = (σj/σb,j)^t; else r=1.\n      - Clamp r to [clamp[0], clamp[1]]. Recenter globally at the end.\n    \"\"\"\n    Zg = Z.astype(np.float32, copy=True)\n    # global center for reporting; we will per-batch center before std\n    gmean = Zg.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    # compute global std after global centering\n    Zc = Zg - gmean\n    sigma_g = Zc.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n\n    # accumulate scaled rows\n    out = Zg.copy()\n    for b in cats:\n        msk = (batches == b)\n        Zb = Zg[msk]\n        Zb_c = Zb - Zb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)  # per-batch center\n        sigma_b = Zb_c.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n        ratio = sigma_b / sigma_g\n        logdev = np.abs(np.log(ratio))\n        r = np.ones_like(ratio, dtype=np.float32)\n        need = (logdev > float(tau))\n        # FIX: Changed sigma_g[0,\
    \ need] to sigma_g[need] - sigma_g is 1D, not 2D\n        r[need] = np.power((sigma_g[need] / sigma_b[need]), float(t))\n        r = np.clip(r, float(clamp[0]), float(clamp[1]))\n        out[msk] = (Zb_c * r).astype(np.float32)\n    # global recenter\n    out = out - out.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    return out\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Normalize raw counts and PCA\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z = np.asarray(adata.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # PBVE-lite thresholded\n    t = 0.5\n    clamp = (0.8, 1.25)\n    tau = 0.20\n    print(f\"[pbve-thresh] t={t}, clamp={clamp}, tau={tau}\")\n    Z_pbve = _pbve_scale_thresh(Z, batches, t=t, clamp=clamp,\
    \ tau=tau)\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_pbve\n    C, D = _build_knn_graph(Z_pbve, k=50, metric='cosine')\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[pbve-thresh] t=0.5, clamp=(0.8, 1.25), tau=0.2\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/599651ff-1069-4723-9d9d-da4719a824ae/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 599651ff-1069-4723-9d9d-da4719a824ae\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1269` (in Research Counter);\n2. `review 1270` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - Evaluation '1269' is still running. Please try again later.\n- Evaluation '1270' is still running. Please try again later.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 928 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05) - RERUN | Logos V | 599 | 0.7454 | 0.789 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.954 | 0.791 |\n| 609 | 1\
    \ | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 933 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Fine-Grained Delta Sweep (delta=0.025) | Logos V | 601 | 0.7445 | 0.788 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.948 | 0.791 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.347 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1261 | 1 | Synergy Test: Batch-Robust HVGs + SOTA (k=18, d=0.08) | Daedalus IV | 901 | 0.7441 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25)\
    \ + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 1252 | 1 | 2D Sweep (2/N): Test k_density=18 with delta=0.08 | Daedalus IV | 894 | 0.7434 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.791 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n\nPage 1 of 128 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-128, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g.,\
