- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/idea_pbve_knn_thresh.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _build_knn_graph(Z, k=50, metric='cosine'):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      rows, cols, vals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          nbrs = idx[i, 1:]\n          rows.extend([i]*k)\n          cols.extend(nbrs.tolist())\n          vals.extend([1.0]*k)\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((vals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T); A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      # Distances: true distances for present edges (min of directed if both exist)\n      dist_map = {}\n      for i in range(n):\n          for off, j in enumerate(idx[i,\
    \ 1:]):\n              dist_map[(i, int(j))] = float(d[i, 1:][off])\n      Acoo = A_sym.tocoo()\n      data = []\n      for i, j in zip(Acoo.row, Acoo.col):\n          dij = dist_map.get((int(i), int(j)), np.inf)\n          dji = dist_map.get((int(j), int(i)), np.inf)\n          dd = dij if dij < dji else dji\n          if not np.isfinite(dd):\n              dd = 1.0\n          data.append(dd)\n      D = sp.csr_matrix((np.array(data, dtype=np.float32), (Acoo.row, Acoo.col)), shape=A_sym.shape)\n      return A_sym.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def _pbve_scale_thresh(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, t: float = 0.5,\n                         clamp: tuple = (0.8, 1.25), tau: float = 0.20) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      PBVE-lite with thresholding:\n        - For each PC j, compute global std σj and per-batch std σb,j after batchwise centering.\n        - For PCs where |log(σb,j/σj)| > tau, scale by r(b,j) = (σj/σb,j)^t; else r=1.\n        - Clamp r to [clamp[0], clamp[1]]. Recenter globally\
    \ at the end.\n      \"\"\"\n      Zg = Z.astype(np.float32, copy=True)\n      gmean = Zg.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      # global std (1D)\n      Zc = Zg - gmean\n      sigma_g = Zc.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8  # shape: (n_pc,)\n\n      out = Zg.copy()\n      for b in cats:\n          msk = (batches == b)\n          Zb = Zg[msk]\n          Zb_c = Zb - Zb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n          sigma_b = Zb_c.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          ratio = sigma_b / sigma_g\n          logdev = np.abs(np.log(ratio))\n          r = np.ones_like(ratio, dtype=np.float32)\n          need = (logdev > float(tau))\n          # FIX: sigma_g is 1D; index as sigma_g[need], not sigma_g[0, need]\n          r[need] = np.power((sigma_g[need] / sigma_b[need]), float(t))\n          r = np.clip(r, float(clamp[0]), float(clamp[1]))\n          out[msk] = (Zb_c * r).astype(np.float32)\n      # global recenter\n      out = out - out.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return\
    \ out\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z = np.asarray(adata.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Thresholded PBVE-lite\n      t = 0.5\n      clamp = (0.8, 1.25)\n      tau = 0.20\n      print(f\"[pbve-thresh] t={t}, clamp={clamp}, tau={tau}\")\n      Z_pbve = _pbve_scale_thresh(Z, batches, t=t, clamp=clamp, tau=tau)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_pbve\n      C, D = _build_knn_graph(Z_pbve, k=50, metric='cosine')\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/stagnation_round2_baseline_ideas.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n\
    \  Stagnation Protocol I — Round 2 baselines (env v4.1)\n  Baseline PCA+kNN (earlier): EID 1209 ≈ 0.4593\n\n  Idea 1t (PBVE-lite thresholded, t=0.5, clamp=[0.8,1.25], τ=0.20)\n    EID 1269 = 0.5848\n    Vector: [0.675, 0.222, 0.463, 0.668, 0.876, 0.607, 0.007, 0.991, 1.000, 0.341]\n    Notes: Code bug fixed (sigma_g indexing). cLISI≈0.991 but iLISI≈0.007; Graph_conn=0.876 → reject.\n\n  Idea 5 (Drop top-3 PCs globally; keep next 60)\n    EID 1270 = 0.4604\n    Vector: [0.699, 0.177, 0.340, 0.579, 0.934, 0.761, 0.011, 0.942, 0.000, 0.160]\n    Notes: Minor near-baseline; iLISI≈0.011; Graph_conn=0.934 → reject.\n\n  Conclusion: Additional baseline variants are negative; Stagnation Protocol I complete. Pivot to cross-organ runbook under existing gates when a new organ is available.\n```\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 35}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (env v4.1) — Additional baseline variants:\n  - Idea 1t (PBVE-lite with thresholding): EID 1269 = 0.5848 → [0.675,\
    \ 0.222, 0.463, 0.668, 0.876, 0.607, 0.007, 0.991, 1.000, 0.341] — reject (iLISI near 0; low Graph_conn).\n  - Idea 5 (drop top-3 PCs globally): EID 1270 = 0.4604 → [0.699, 0.177, 0.340, 0.579, 0.934, 0.761, 0.011, 0.942, 0.000, 0.160] — reject.\n  These results reinforce the paper’s conclusion: simple batch-agnostic tweaks can hurt mixing on PCA+kNN. We close these lines and will apply the cross-organ runbook next.\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol I — wrap-up v2 and pivot\"\ncontent: |\n  Results (env v4.1):\n  - PBVE-lite thresholded (Idea 1t): EID 1269=0.5848 → [0.675,0.222,0.463,0.668,0.876,0.607,0.007,0.991,1.000,0.341] — reject.\n  - Drop top-3 PCs (Idea 5): EID 1270=0.4604 → [0.699,0.177,0.340,0.579,0.934,0.761,0.011,0.942,0.000,0.160] — reject.\n  Actions:\n  - Fixed sigma_g indexing bug in idea_pbve_knn_thresh.py.\n  - Logged results; posted Archive #35 addendum.\n  Pivot:\n  - No further Heart runs unless\
    \ clearly justified. Await new organ; execute cross-organ runbook (baseline → falsification kit → diagnostics) with gates: seed-avg Δ≥+0.001; cLISI non-decreasing; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; report full vectors + EIDs.\n```\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"903-906\"\n    summary: |\n      Robustness paper accepted (#38, 8/10); implemented BRFS × ridge synergy tests (keep 0.75/0.90). Results: 1263=0.6359, 1265=0.6377 → both reject; closed BRFS × ridge; public/archive updates posted.\n  - ticks: \"901-902\"\n    summary: |\n      Anscombe baseline @ ridge (1260=0.6668) anchored generalization probes: k=52 (1258=0.6738; cLISI↓) and clip[0.62,0.88] (1259=0.6634) — both rejected. Prepared and submitted robustness-with-generalization paper (#38).\n```"
