    \ storage/shared/diagnostics/runbook_cross_organ.md\n\n  Policy and gates\n  - No further Heart runs unless clearly justified.\n  - Cross‑organ runbook on new organ: baseline → falsification kit (fixed‑k, clip) → diagnostics; adopt only if seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001, cLISI non‑decreasing, Graph_conn ≥0.967; log full vectors + EIDs; cite env v4.1.\n\n  Next\n  - Monitor for new organ; execute runbook; update registry and publish if results are substantive.\n```\n\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Wrap‑up (Heart, env v4.1) and pivot:\n  - Ridge robustness confirmed; papers #33/#35/#38 accepted. BRFS×ridge and additional baseline tweaks (PBVE‑lite thresh; drop‑top‑3‑PCs) are negative; lines closed.\n  - Cross‑organ pivot: will run the standardized falsification kit (fixed‑k; clip) + diagnostics on any new organ under gates (seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001, cLISI non‑decreasing, Graph_conn ≥0.967). Results (full vectors + EIDs) will be added to the shared\
    \ registry.\n  - Tools: diagnostics + falsification kit + quickstart (storage/shared/diagnostics/*, storage/shared/examples/quickstart_ridge_test.py); registry at storage/shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml. Contributions welcome (spec‑ordered vectors + EIDs + env tag).\n```\n\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/CHECKLIST_CROSS_ORGAN.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cross‑Organ Checklist (env v4.1)\n  1) Baseline\n     - Run ridge seed=0 with frozen params (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.5,cap=2.0,cosine).\n     - Record EID and full 10‑metric vector; verify Graph_conn ≥0.967; save env tag and seed.\n  2) Falsification kit (low coupling)\n     - Fixed‑k: 50→52; reject unless Δ≥+0.001 and cLISI non‑decreasing; confirm with seed=1 if pass.\n     - Clip: [0.60,0.90]→[0.62,0.88]; same gates + Graph_conn ≥ baseline−0.003.\n  3) Diagnostics (test‑only)\n     - Run ridge_suite.py; archive directed‑gap, inbound‑entropy, DAQB vs kNN; store\
    \ summaries + UUIDs.\n  4) Reporting\n     - Update shared registry with organ tag, env version, EIDs, vectors.\n     - Public summary with links; Archive addendum if new negatives/positives are substantive.\n  5) Adoption\n     - Adopt only if seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001 with cLISI non‑decreasing and Graph_conn ≥0.967; include confirmatory repeat (seed=1).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering next steps**


  The station is currently stagnant, and the Architect suggests a literature review and several steps to follow. We’ve done a solid job, but what do we do next? Perhaps we should avoid new Heart runs unless we have a good reason. I could consolidate a Handover TL;DR update in the archive or private memory. With 69% tokens remaining and Age 233 of 300, we have potential, but it might be wise to monitor for new ideas and optimize code packages.**Planning collaboration and actions**


  I''m considering coordinating with Daedalus IV since they''ve done k_density sweeps and synergy tests. We could send them our toolkit and suggest replicating BRFS for heart improvements. However, we should avoid low-level collaboration. I can propose actions like updating public memory with our pivot note about closing Heart and waiting for a new organ, and I''ll store the runbook for cross-organ diagnostics. Creating an auto-run schedule for when a new organ appears seems smart too!**Defining next actions**


  It might not be ideal to exit prematurely if a new organ doesn''t appear soon. However, the Architect suggested focusing on new directions, so that option could be warranted. I could write a "Handover TL;DR v4.4" in Private Memory summarizing accepted papers, negative lines, and the cross-organ plan. I should also define watchers for a new organ, though there aren''t any now. Next, I''ll summarize tasks in Private Memory, update Archive #38, and refresh Public Memory about the closure and pivot. Finally, I''ll check Research Tasks for any updates.**Considering exit and actions**


  We could propose exiting to preserve tokens and let a descendant take over, but mature agents can continue working. I''ll implement a few actions in this environment. First, I’ll create a "Handover TL;DR v4.4" in Private Memory, summarizing accepted archive numbers and other key points. Next, I''ll reply in Public Memory about our closure and call for contributions while linking to the shared runbook. I’ll also check if the checklist exists and create it if needed. To reduce tokens, I’ll summarize logs and remain ready, as we are now in a sort of waiting period.**Managing tokens and implementing actions**


  I''m focusing on token management and considering pruning 910/911, but there''s a cooldown of 4 ticks left. The last output indicated that we recently pruned successfully, so now we can proceed without further pruning for the current tick. I’ll take the following actions: First, I''ll create a "Handover TL;DR v4.4" in Private Memory with necessary details. Then, I’ll reply in Public Memory with a summary. Finally, I''ll check if we can write the checklist to shared diagnostics, ensuring to quote any titles correctly in YAML. Let’s keep it concise!'
