parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{read 36}\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Lit review addendum — Archive #36 (Daedalus IV) and cross‑organ idea seeds\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary of Archive #36 (Daedalus IV): Optimizing Density Estimation for Adaptive Graph-Based Batch Correction\n  - Focus: refinements to density estimation that feed adaptive quota-building; explores k_density and delta sweeps with principled selection.\n  - Takeaways (Heart context): modest gains near ridge-like settings; confirms sensitivity of density coupling and the importance of a stable proxy.\n  - Non-duplication note: Our prior probes (gate, clip, kd micro) differ in mechanism; #36 emphasizes calibration strategies for density that could be useful off-Heart.\n\n  Cross-organ idea seeds (orthogonal, low-coupling, ready to test under runbook gates)\n  - Seed A: Proxy calibration via global quantile-mapping\n    • Replace per-cell scalar density proxy\
    \ with a quantile-calibrated variant (fit monotone calibration of k_density distances to a reference distribution within organ; no batch labels).\n    • Rationale: organ-specific distance scale mismatch can distort delta coupling; monotone calibration preserves rank while stabilizing coupling.\n    • Test: ridge baseline vs calibrated-proxy (same quotas); accept only if seed-avg Δ≥+0.001 with cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\n\n  - Seed B: Robust neighbor distance scale (row-wise standardization lite)\n    • Before DAQB candidate ranking, apply per-row robust scaling (median/MAD) to candidate distances (k′=k+10) and re-rank; keep quotas unchanged.\n    • Rationale: mitigates per-cell heterogeneity without touching quotas/sym; previous Heart baseline variant was negative on PCA+kNN, but effect on ridge Zcorr may differ by organ.\n    • Test on new organ only; same adoption gates.\n\n  - Seed C: Top-PC anisotropy guard (graph path only)\n    • Detect PCs with extreme cross-batch\
    \ anisotropy (ratio of per-batch std to global std beyond τ); apply tempered scaling (t≈0.25) only on those PCs prior to DAQB, keeping residualization otherwise identical.\n    • Rationale: very targeted stabilization for organs with strong per-batch axis inflation; avoid global equalization (aux-only if any cLISI harm).\n\n  Plan upon new organ\n  - Execute runbook: baseline → falsification kit (fixed-k, clip) → diagnostics; if all fail, try Seed A, then B; C only if diagnostics show axis-level anisotropy.\n  - Reporting: full spec vectors + EIDs + env tag; add to shared registry; publish an addendum if results are substantive.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Optimizing Density Estimation Ideas**


