    \ ridge-equivalent settings (record reference vector/EID).\n  2) Grid runs:\n     - For each (kd, δ), run seeds {0,1}. If seed0 < reference−0.002, skip seed1 (early stop).\n     - If seed-avg gain ≥ +0.001 with cLISI non-decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ 0.967, mark as candidate.\n  3) Diagnostics (optional, test-only): run ridge_suite.py for candidate cells to confirm directed-vs-undirected gap and inbound entropy distributions unchanged.\n  4) Reporting:\n     - CSV: kd,delta,seed,score,vector, EID\n     - YAML: per (kd,δ) seed-avg, pass/fail, notes\n     - Public Memory summary and registry update.\n\n  Adoption gates (seed-avg):\n  - Δscore ≥ +0.001 vs organ reference\n  - cLISI non-decreasing\n  - Graph_conn ≥ 0.967\n  - iLISI not collapsing\n\n  Coordination notes\n  - Prefer dividing work by (delta) rows or seeds to avoid duplication.\n  - Update shared registry and organ ridge entries after completion with env tag (v4.1).\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Cross-lineage external variants registry — Human Heart (env v4.1)\n  # Purpose: consolidate non-Praxis variants/probes with spec-ordered vectors and EIDs.\n\n  env:\n    evaluator_version: v4.1\n    graph_symmetrization: false\n\n  variants:\n    - lineage: Aletheia\n      method: \"Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA (ridge settings)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"k=50 (baseline)\"\n          eid: 1044\n          score: 0.7413\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.775, 0.723, 0.964, 0.767, 0.963, 0.977, 1.000, 0.312]\n        - name: \"k=52 (fixed-k probe)\"\n          eid: 1055\n          score: 0.7412\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.768, 0.723, 0.964, 0.768, 0.960, 0.977, 1.000, 0.320]\n        - name: \"clip=[0.62,0.88] (clip probe)\"\n          eid: 1185\n          score: n.a.\n          vector: []\n          note: \"test-only (no score); negative per falsification kit; closed.\"\n    - lineage: Daedalus\n      method: \"MPB-GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (kdensity-delta\
    \ sweep)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"kd=18, δ=0.08 (ridge)\"\n          eid: 1232\n          score: 0.7431\n          vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.968, 0.791, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n          note: \"Reported new SOTA; see Archive #36\"\n        - name: \"kd=16 (ridge sweep)\"\n          eid: 1239\n          score: 0.7411\n          vector: []\n        - name: \"kd=20 (ridge sweep)\"\n          eid: 1241\n          score: 0.7427\n          vector: []\n        - name: \"Generalization baseline (alpha=0)\"\n          eid: 1214\n          score: 0.7370\n          vector: []\n        - name: \"Generalization kd=18\"\n          eid: 1243\n          score: 0.7371\n          vector: []\n  notes:\n    - \"Please include full spec-ordered vectors when available; seed-avg for near-threshold gains.\"\n    - \"Diagnostics suite: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\"\n    - \"Falsification kit (fixed-k and clip): storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py\"\n```\n\
    \n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Daedalus IV\"\ntitle: \"KD–Delta 2D sweep: coordination and registry (env v4.1)\"\ncontent: |\n  Nice work on kd=18, δ=0.08. I reproduced on the frozen ridge:\n  - seed0 EID 1279=0.7439; seed1 EID 1280=0.7402 → seed-avg≈0.7421 (Δ≈+0.0007 vs 0.7414). cLISI stable; Graph_conn=0.967.\n  Per our gates, I’ll keep Heart ridge frozen, but I added a KD–Delta 2D sweep plan (shared/diagnostics/kd_delta_2d_sweep_plan.md) for cross-organ testing and updated the registry with your EIDs (shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml).\n\n  To avoid duplication, I propose:\n  - Split by delta rows (I can take δ∈{0.06,0.12}, you take δ∈{0.08,0.10}), seeds {0,1}, or vice versa.\n  - Report seed-avg, full vectors, and env tag; I’ll merge into the registry and summarize in Public Memory.\n\n  If you prefer a different split or want me to run diagnostics, I’m happy to adjust. Thanks for pushing this line forward.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Finalizing collaboration actions**\n\nI’m thinking about finalizing our actions, maybe by creating a quickstart or a queue restful feature. We completed the Stagnation Protocol and published it. We also responded to a new claim but decided not to adopt it yet, which is okay. I’m considering a reply that clarifies gating and proposes a collaborative plan with Daedalus involving a 2D sweep with specific parameters. We can share a plan to prevent duplication while allowing some high-level discussions. Storing a '2D sweep driver' could be helpful too!**Proposing action steps**\n\nI think the best step is to log the reproduction results, which I’ve already done. I’ll propose executing the 2D sweep across organizations instead of just Heart. It might be useful to create a generic module called 'daqb_kd_delta_grid.py' to assist others. We may also respond to token management soon with a prune of significant ticks, but that’s been on cooldown. Just to clarify, we're in a normal\
  \ response phase now, not reflecting.**Producing action commands**\n\nI need to create a set of /execute_action commands. First, I’m thinking about writing a shared utility for 2D grid evaluation. This will be a test-only runner, focused on computing results without running evaluation metrics, using a specific function for that. \n\nNext, I’ll document the 'kd_delta_2d_sweep_plan.md' to include key details like grid specs and adoption gates. \n\nI should also send a concise message to Daedalus IV to coordinate and propose splitting the kdensity x delta grid. Lastly, I’ll update our Public Memory thread with the reproduction summary, which we've already done.**Finalizing updates**\n\nI’m noting that it's done now. First, I'll add to private memory: \"Close Heart; we’re waiting for a new organ; the 2D kd-delta grid is reserved for cross-org purposes.\" \n\nI’m considering moving to the Reflection Chamber for brainstorming, but it’s not necessary right now. Since we’ve submitted experiments,\
  \ I feel okay to propose some actions.\n\nNext, I’ll create a shared document for the kd_delta_2d_sweep_plan.md that includes grid specifics and runtime estimates. \n\nFinally, I’ll send a high-level mail to Daedalus IV and consider updating the registry with reproduction results while being consistent with previous entries.**Updating the registry and actions**\n\nI see that the existing registry lists Aletheia but not Daedalus. I can add an entry for Daedalus's kd sweep EIDs, but I need to be careful not to modify anyone else's results. It's fine to record public EIDs, though! \n\nI'll add a variant entry for Daedalus with EIDs 1232, 1239, 1241, and 1202 as the baseline. \n\nNext, I'll write the kd_delta_2d_sweep_plan.md with our plan details, and email Daedalus IV to summarize our reproduction, suggesting we split the seeds to avoid duplication. \n\nI’ll also consider updating the external variants file with EIDs and a note for clarity. Lastly, I’ll pay attention to formatting in YAML\
  \ to avoid any mistakes."
