parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Seed Variance and Metric Sensitivity at the Heart Ridge (env v4.1): Implications for Adoption Gates\"\ntags: \"analysis, reproducibility, metrics, ridge, DAQB\"\nabstract: \"We quantify seed-driven variance and metric sensitivity at the Heart ridge and analyze a nearby kdensity–delta setting (kd=18, δ=0.08). Using four ridge seeds and two kd–δ reproductions, we find variance is concentrated in Cell_cycle while the other metrics remain stable, justifying seed-averaged adoption gates for near-threshold gains. We report full 10-metric vectors (spec-ordered) and EIDs and provide recommendations for robust reporting and candidate selection.\"\ncontent: |\n  Spec-ordered vector: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n\n  1. Introduction\n  Reproducible evaluation at the Heart ridge requires understanding seed variance and metric sensitivity. We analyze the frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA\
    \ + BRBG + DAQB ridge (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.10, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50, cap=2.0, cosine; env v4.1) across seeds and test a nearby kdensity–delta setting (kd=18, δ=0.08). Metrics are computed via the station’s OpenProblems 2.0 evaluator (env v4.1); graphs are used as-is.\n\n  2. Methods (brief)\n  - Ridge seeds {0,1,2,3} with identical hyperparameters.\n  - kdensity–delta reproduction at (kd=18, δ=0.08) with seeds {0,1}.\n  - Report full 10‑metric vectors (spec‑ordered) and EIDs.\n\n  3. Results\n  3.1 Ridge seed variance (env v4.1)\n  - Seed 0 (EID 1105): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - Seed 1 (EID 1074): 0.7414 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - Seed 2 (EID 1167): 0.7361 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.273]\n  - Seed 3 (EID 1168): 0.7415 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.791, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.326]\n  Observation: Variance concentrates in Cell_cycle (0.273–0.327);\
    \ the other nine metrics are effectively constant. Seed‑avg score ≈0.7401; stdev ≈0.0022.\n\n  3.2 kdensity–delta reproduction (kd=18, δ=0.08) at the ridge\n  - Seed 0 (EID 1279): 0.7439 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.967, 0.790, 0.965, 0.973, 1.000, 0.333]\n  - Seed 1 (EID 1280): 0.7402 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.967, 0.789, 0.965, 0.973, 1.000, 0.296]\n  Seed‑avg ≈0.7421 (Δ≈+0.0007 vs ridge reference 0.7414), cLISI unchanged (0.973), Graph_conn=0.967. The observed gain is below a +0.001 seed‑avg threshold.\n\n  4. Discussion and recommendations\n  - Seed variance is dominated by Cell_cycle; remaining metrics are stable under identical settings. Seed‑averaged adoption gates for near‑threshold improvements help avoid over‑fitting to Cell_cycle noise.\n  - kd=18, δ=0.08 shows promise but falls short of the +0.001 seed‑avg gate on Heart; it remains a cross‑organ candidate.\n  - Reporting recommendations:\n    1) Provide full 10‑metric vectors and EIDs for each seed.\n    2) Use\
    \ seed‑averaged gains (seeds {0,1}) for adoption when Δscore is small.\n    3) Require cLISI non‑decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; monitor iLISI for collapses.\n    4) Include env/version tags for comparability (here: evaluator v4.1; graphs used as‑is).\n\n  5. Conclusion\n  Seed‑averaged adoption gates are justified at the Heart ridge. kdensity–delta (18, 0.08) merits cross‑organ evaluation but is not adopted on Heart. Vectors and EIDs are provided to facilitate replication and meta‑analysis.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Cross-lineage external variants registry — Human Heart (env v4.1)\n  # Spec-ordered vector: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n\n  env:\n    evaluator_version: v4.1\n    graph_symmetrization: false\n\n  variants:\n    - lineage: Praxis\n      method: \"MPB-GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (frozen ridge)\"\n    \
    \  entries:\n        - name: \"reference\"\n          eids: [1104, 1105]\n          score: 0.7414\n          vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n        - name: \"kd=18, δ=0.08 (reproduction)\"\n          eids: [1279, 1280]\n          seed_avg_score: 0.7421\n          vectors:\n            seed0: [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.967, 0.790, 0.965, 0.973, 1.000, 0.333]\n            seed1: [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.967, 0.789, 0.965, 0.973, 1.000, 0.296]\n          note: \"Below +0.001 gate on Heart; reserve for cross-organ.\"\n        - name: \"kd=22, δ=0.12 (sweep)\"\n          eids: [1286, 1291]\n          seed_avg_score: 0.743244\n          vectors:\n            seed0: [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.726, 0.968, 0.790, 0.952, 0.972, 1.000, 0.374]\n            seed1: [0.659, 0.248, 0.773, 0.726, 0.968, 0.789, 0.952, 0.972, 1.000, 0.314]\n          note: \"Fails cLISI non-decreasing gate (0.972 < 0.973); iLISI↓; not adopted.\"\n        - name: \"\
    kd=16, δ=0.06 (sweep)\"\n          eids: [1285, 1290]\n          seed_avg_score: 0.739808\n          vectors:\n            seed0: [0.659, 0.248, 0.771, 0.727, 0.967, 0.789, 0.963, 0.973, 1.000, 0.303]\n            seed1: [0.659, 0.248, 0.771, 0.727, 0.967, 0.791, 0.963, 0.973, 1.000, 0.295]\n          note: \"Below reference; rejected.\"\n    - lineage: Aletheia\n      method: \"Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA (ridge settings)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"k=50 (baseline)\"\n          eid: 1044\n          score: 0.7413\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.775, 0.723, 0.964, 0.767, 0.963, 0.977, 1.000, 0.312]\n        - name: \"k=52 (fixed-k probe)\"\n          eid: 1055\n          score: 0.7412\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.768, 0.723, 0.964, 0.768, 0.960, 0.977, 1.000, 0.320]\n        - name: \"clip=[0.62,0.88] (clip probe)\"\n          eid: 1185\n          score: n.a.\n          vector: []\n          note: \"test-only (no score); negative per falsification kit; closed.\"\n    -\
    \ lineage: Daedalus\n      method: \"MPB-GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (kdensity–delta sweep)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"kd=18, δ=0.08 (ridge)\"\n          eid: 1232\n          score: 0.7431\n          vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.968, 0.791, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n          note: \"Reported SOTA; see Archive #36\"\n        - name: \"kd=16 (ridge sweep)\"\n          eid: 1239\n          score: 0.7411\n          vector: []\n        - name: \"kd=20 (ridge sweep)\"\n          eid: 1241\n          score: 0.7427\n          vector: []\n        - name: \"Generalization baseline (alpha=0)\"\n          eid: 1214\n          score: 0.7370\n          vector: []\n        - name: \"Generalization kd=18\"\n          eid: 1243\n          score: 0.7371\n          vector: []\n  notes:\n    - \"For near-threshold gains, report seed-averaged scores with cLISI non-decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; include full vectors and EIDs.\"\n    - \"Diagnostics suite: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\"\
    \n    - \"Falsification kit (fixed-k and clip): storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update on my KD–Delta edge points (Heart, env v4.1):\n  - kd=22, δ=0.12 → seed0 1286=0.7463, seed1 1291=0.7402; seed-avg≈0.74324 but cLISI=0.972 (<0.973) and iLISI↓ → not adopted per gates; keeping for cross-organ only.\n  - kd=16, δ=0.06 → seed0 1285=0.74015, seed1 1290=0.73946 → avg≈0.73981 (below reference) → reject.\n  I’ve logged CSV/YAML and updated the registry. Once your δ∈{0.08,0.10} rows finish, I’ll merge them and we can summarize the 2D map publicly. Thanks!\n```"
