- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd20_d006_k50_seed0.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  # Adopted Heart ridge (env v4.1): kdensity=20, delta=0.06, k=50, lam=0.605, alpha_g=0.50, cap=2.0, cosine, seed=0\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"[ridge-adopted] lam=0.605, delta=0.06, kd=20, k=50, alpha_g=0.50, rng_seed=0\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          alpha_g=0.50,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.06,\n          kdensity=20,\n          k_total=50,\n          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_adopted_alias.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\
    \  from best_mpb_daqb_kd20_d006_k50_seed0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as _run\n\n  # Alias to the adopted Heart ridge (env v4.1) settings\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      return _run(adata)\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v4.yaml}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Heart ridge entry (env v4.1) — Praxis IV v4\n  reference:\n    eids: [1104, 1105]\n    score: 0.7414\n    vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.765, 0.725, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n    spec: {k: 50, kdensity: 22, delta: 0.10, lambda: 0.605, alpha_g: 0.50, cap: 2.0, metric: cosine, seed: 0}\n  adopted:\n    name: \"kdensity=20, delta=0.06\"\n    eids: [1295, 1298]        # seed0, seed1\n    seed_avg_score: 0.74421   # ≈ (0.74490 + 0.74352)/2\n    gate_check: {cLISI: 0.973, Graph_conn: 0.967, iLISI: 0.963}\n    spec: {k: 50, kdensity: 20, delta: 0.06, lambda: 0.605, alpha_g: 0.50, cap: 2.0, metric: cosine}\n  notes:\n    - \"Cell_cycle\
    \ varies across seeds; adoption based on seed-avg and gates.\"\n    - \"Use praxis/best_adopted_alias.py for quick reproduction.\"\n  env:\n    evaluator_version: v4.1\n    graphs_symmetrized: false\n```\n/execute_action{storage write shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Cross-lineage external variants registry — Human Heart (env v4.1)\n  env:\n    evaluator_version: v4.1\n    graph_symmetrization: false\n\n  variants:\n    - lineage: Praxis\n      method: \"MPB-GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (adopted Heart ridge)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"kd=20, δ=0.06, k=50 (adopted)\"\n          eids: [1295, 1298]\n          seed_avg_score: 0.74421\n          vector_seed0: [0.659, 0.248, 0.771, 0.727, 0.967, 0.791, 0.963, 0.973, 1.000, 0.349]\n          note: \"Spec-ordered vector shown for seed0; adoption based on seed-avg and gates.\"\n    - lineage: Aletheia\n      method: \"Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA (ridge settings)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"\
    k=50 (baseline)\"\n          eid: 1044\n          score: 0.7413\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.775, 0.723, 0.964, 0.767, 0.963, 0.977, 1.000, 0.312]\n        - name: \"k=52 (fixed-k probe)\"\n          eid: 1055\n          score: 0.7412\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.768, 0.723, 0.964, 0.768, 0.960, 0.977, 1.000, 0.320]\n\n  notes:\n    - \"Report seed-avg near-threshold gains (Δ≥+0.001) with cLISI non-decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\"\n    - \"Diagnostics: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py; falsification kit: storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py\"\n```\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{preview 39}\n/execute_action{reply 33}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Adoption note (env v4.1, Heart) — kdensity=20, δ=0.06\n  - KD–Delta 2D sweep identified kd=20, δ=0.06 as passing our gates:\n      seed0 (EID 1295)=0.74490, seed1 (EID 1298)=0.74352 → seed-avg≈0.74421 (Δ≈+0.00281 vs 0.7414).\n      cLISI=0.973, Graph_conn=0.967, iLISI stable → adopted.\n  - Alias\
    \ runner: storage/praxis/best_adopted_alias.py (loads kd20, δ0.06 spec).\n  - Ridge entry updated: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v4.yaml\n  - Registry updated with adopted spec for cross-lineage comparison.\n  - Cross-organ pivot: this adopted ridge is now our baseline per the runbook. We will apply the falsification kit and diagnostics when a new organ arrives.\n```\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (env v4.1): Adopted Heart ridge = kdensity=20, δ=0.06 (k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50).\n  - EIDs: seed0 1295=0.74490; seed1 1298=0.74352 → seed-avg≈0.74421 (Δ≈+0.00281 vs 0.7414).\n  - Gates: cLISI=0.973; Graph_conn=0.967; iLISI stable → passes; adopted.\n  - Alias runner: storage/praxis/best_adopted_alias.py\n  - Ridge entry and registry updated:\n      • storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_praxis_iv_v4.yaml\n      • storage/shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml\n  Next: Use this adopted\
    \ ridge as the baseline for cross-organ validation (falsification kit + diagnostics) when the next organ is available.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating next steps**\n\nI need to focus on our next actions since the system indicates we're in Stagnation. We've already engaged the Stagnation Protocol, so now I want to pivot to a cross-organ baseline. There's a mention of a new archive from Syntellect about PBVE-lite, which I could review. However, the only available dataset right now is for the human heart, so actual cross-organ tasks can’t be executed. Still, I can generalize with previous transforms and proceed with the literature review for protocol completeness.**Planning Archive review**\n\nI see that Archive #39 is important for the PBVE-lite context, so I should read its abstract and consider replying with cross-references to our past results in Archive #35. The next recommended step is pruning and pivoting. I'm at a 39% token budget, which is good!\n\nI could go into the Archive Room and view Archive #39 specifically, maybe previewing to avoid overload. After that, I’d propose synergy with the kd20 and\
  \ d006 heart SOTA variant. However, coordination with Daedalus IV may not be necessary since we're limited to just one dataset for our cross-organ efforts.**Planning experimental actions**\n\nI can propose \"cell-type-agnostic generalization baseline experiments\" or explore testing with alternative random seeds, which we've already completed. Next, I should produce actions using the /execute_action commands and log the adoption specifics. I'll update the shared registry with the current baseline and add an alias runner for kd20-d006. It makes sense to provide the alias code file and verify its storage, including saving the new best runner file as \"best_mpb_daqb_kd20_d006_k50.py.\" I might also want to add an update to the Public Memory and Archive but will keep token usage minimal.**Organizing my plan**\n\nI have a clear plan! I'll begin by going to research and writing the storage for \"praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd20_d006_k50_seed0.py,\" using the call to eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca with specific\
  \ parameters. I'll also map this to \"praxis/best_adopted_alias.py.\" \n\nNext, I’ll go to the archive to reply to #33 with an adoption note and then reply to #7 in public memory with a concise note. I’ll update the shared registry files accordingly, read from Archive #39, and then execute actions for exploring and reading contents, although I'm wary of token usage increasing.**Finalizing actions and updates**\n\nTo be prudent, I should just preview Archive #39 instead of reading it entirely. I'll reply to #39 with a brief cross-link and differences. I also need to pivot to updating the cross-organ runbook to establish the adopted specification. I will write a runner file and an alias, updating the ridge_entries file to log current results. Although I'm cautious about token usage, I can organize the responses systematically, ensuring clarity and brevity while sticking to my action plan. Keeping everything minimal will be essential."
