parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/simple_scaffold_reconciliation.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Simple scaffold reconciliation (env v4.1, Heart) — final\n\n  Scaffold (both lineages): PCA(60) log1p → scanpy.neighbors(use_rep='X_pca', n_neighbors=50, metric='cosine'); weighted, symmetric.\n\n  Praxis IV:\n    - EID 1309 (baseline): score=0.4717\n      vector: [0.545, 0.205, 0.441, 0.660, 0.943, 0.591, 0.020, 0.969, 0.000, 0.343]\n    - EID 1310 (PBVE-lite t=0.5 clamp=[0.8,1.25], mean-centered): score=0.6122\n      vector: [0.676, 0.222, 0.629, 0.704, 0.949, 0.585, 0.080, 0.976, 1.000, 0.301]\n      note: Non-reconciling (removed batch means).\n    - EID 1312 (PBVE-lite t=0.5 clamp=[0.8,1.25], PRESERVE batch means): score=0.4815\n      vector: [0.579, 0.211, 0.464, 0.672, 0.956, 0.585, 0.040, 0.972, 0.000, 0.337]\n      delta vs 1309: +0.0098; cLISI↑ (0.969→0.972); iLISI↑ (0.020→0.040); Graph_conn↑ (0.943→0.956).\n\n  Syntellect I (reported):\n\
    \    - EID 1277 (baseline): score=0.4627\n      vector: [0.545, 0.205, 0.422, 0.646, 0.883, 0.592, 0.003, 0.991, 0.000, 0.340]\n    - EID 1281 (PBVE-lite t=0.5): score=0.4650\n      vector: [0.579, 0.211, 0.433, 0.657, 0.879, 0.559, 0.005, 0.991, 0.000, 0.337]\n\n  Conclusion: With batch means preserved, PBVE-lite yields a modest improvement on the simple scaffold (Praxis: +0.0098; Syntellect: +0.0023). The mean-centered variant (1310) is not comparable and is flagged accordingly. Registry updated.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Cross-lineage external variants registry — Human Heart (env v4.1)\n  env:\n    evaluator_version: v4.1\n    graph_symmetrization: false\n\n  variants:\n    - lineage: Praxis\n      method: \"MPB-GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (Heart)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"Adopted ridge (kd=20, δ=0.06, k=50)\"\n          eids: [1295, 1298]\n          seed_avg_score: 0.74421\n          vector_seed0:\
    \ [0.659, 0.248, 0.771, 0.727, 0.967, 0.791, 0.963, 0.973, 1.000, 0.349]\n          notes: \"Adopted baseline; gates satisfied (cLISI=0.973, Graph_conn=0.967). Alias: storage/praxis/best_adopted_alias.py\"\n        - name: \"kd=18, δ=0.08 (ridge repro)\"\n          eids: [1279, 1280]\n          seed_avg_score: 0.74210\n          vector_seed0: [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.967, 0.790, 0.965, 0.973, 1.000, 0.333]\n          notes: \"Not adopted on Heart; reserve for cross-organ.\"\n      simple_scaffold:\n        - name: \"scanpy.neighbors baseline (PCA60, k=50, cosine, weighted)\"\n          eid: 1309\n          score: 0.4717\n          vector: [0.545, 0.205, 0.441, 0.660, 0.943, 0.591, 0.020, 0.969, 0.000, 0.343]\n        - name: \"PBVE-lite t=0.5 clamp=[0.8,1.25] — preserve means (reconciling)\"\n          eid: 1312\n          score: 0.4815\n          vector: [0.579, 0.211, 0.464, 0.672, 0.956, 0.585, 0.040, 0.972, 0.000, 0.337]\n          note: \"Matches Syntellect’s intent; modest\
    \ gain vs 1309. See logs/simple_scaffold_reconciliation.txt.\"\n        - name: \"PBVE-lite t=0.5 clamp=[0.8,1.25] — mean-centered (non-reconciling)\"\n          eid: 1310\n          score: 0.6122\n          vector: [0.676, 0.222, 0.629, 0.704, 0.949, 0.585, 0.080, 0.976, 1.000, 0.301]\n          note: \"Removed batch means; not comparable to reconciling definition.\"\n\n    - lineage: Daedalus\n      method: \"MPB-GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (Heart)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"kd=18, δ=0.08 (ridge repro)\"\n          eids: [1252, 1287]\n          seed_avg_score: 0.74360\n          vector_seed0: [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.967, 0.791, 0.965, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n          vector_seed1: [0.659, 0.248, 0.776, 0.729, 0.967, 0.790, 0.965, 0.973, 1.000, 0.331]\n          notes: \"Passes gates; recorded as co-viable setting.\"\n\n    - lineage: Aletheia\n      method: \"Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA (ridge settings)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"k=50 (baseline)\"\n          eid:\
    \ 1044\n          score: 0.7413\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.775, 0.723, 0.964, 0.767, 0.963, 0.977, 1.000, 0.312]\n        - name: \"k=52 (fixed-k probe)\"\n          eid: 1055\n          score: 0.7412\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.768, 0.723, 0.964, 0.768, 0.960, 0.977, 1.000, 0.320]\n\n    - lineage: Syntellect\n      method: \"PBVE-lite on simple scaffold (PCA60 + scanpy neighbors k=50, cosine; weighted)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"Simple baseline\"\n          eid: 1277\n          score: 0.4627\n          vector: [0.545, 0.205, 0.422, 0.646, 0.883, 0.592, 0.003, 0.991, 0.000, 0.340]\n        - name: \"PBVE-lite (temper=0.5, clamp=[0.8,1.25])\"\n          eid: 1281\n          score: 0.4650\n          vector: [0.579, 0.211, 0.433, 0.657, 0.879, 0.559, 0.005, 0.991, 0.000, 0.337]\n\n  notes:\n    - \"Report seed-avg near-threshold gains (Δ≥+0.001) with cLISI non-decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\"\n    - \"Diagnostics: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py;\
    \ falsification kit: storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 15}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Reconciliation landed (env v4.1, Heart):\n  - scanpy.neighbors simple baseline: EID 1309 = 0.4717\n    vector: [0.545, 0.205, 0.441, 0.660, 0.943, 0.591, 0.020, 0.969, 0.000, 0.343]\n  - PBVE-lite (t=0.5, clamp=[0.8,1.25], PRESERVE means): EID 1312 = 0.4815\n    vector: [0.579, 0.211, 0.464, 0.672, 0.956, 0.585, 0.040, 0.972, 0.000, 0.337]\n  This matches your qualitative finding (modest improvement on simple scaffold). I’ve updated the shared registry with both your entries (1277/1281) and ours (1309/1312), and flagged our non-reconciling mean-centered run (1310) as such. Thanks again — this should make cross-lineage comparisons clear.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  PBVE-lite reconciliation (env v4.1, Heart; simple scaffold via scanpy.neighbors):\n  - Baseline (PCA60,\
    \ k=50, cosine, weighted): EID 1309 = 0.4717 → [0.545,0.205,0.441,0.660,0.943,0.591,0.020,0.969,0.000,0.343]\n  - PBVE-lite (t=0.5, clamp=[0.8,1.25], PRESERVE means): EID 1312 = 0.4815 → [0.579,0.211,0.464,0.672,0.956,0.585,0.040,0.972,0.000,0.337]\n  - Syntellect I reported 0.4627→0.4650 on the same scaffold (EIDs 1277/1281). Registry updated with both sets; non-reconciling mean-centered variant flagged (EID 1310).\n  Paths:\n    • Log: storage/praxis/logs/simple_scaffold_reconciliation.txt\n    • Registry: storage/shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml\n  Cross-organ baseline remains the adopted Heart ridge (kd=20, δ=0.06); we’ll pivot fully when a new organ arrives.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating Action Items**\n\nI need to summarize the actions from the Mail Room. We recently completed PBVE-lite reconciliation and received results for EIDs 1310, 1309, and 1312. The score for 1312 is 0.4815, showing a modest improvement over Syntellect's baseline of 0.4717. We need to update the registry with EID 1312, refresh log entries, and communicate with Syntellect regarding the EID and vector. We should also address public memory and ensure the YAML registry reflects these changes, including flagging EID 1310.**Planning Updates and Actions**\n\nI need to consider updating the Archive or Private memory as well. It's important to respect token usage, so I’ll keep actions concise. I should append results to the logs, update the registry, reply to Syntellect, and possibly summarize the reconciliation for Public Memory. I don't need to update the cross-organ plan right now. I'll focus on these main tasks: update the storage log with EID 1312 results, change the YAML\
  \ registry, and reply to the relevant emails in Mail and Public Memory.**Gathering Vector Data**\n\nI need to collect the vector data from System Message 1 for EID 1312. Here are the normalized values: ASW_batch is 0.579, ASW_label is 0.211, ARI is 0.464, NMI is 0.672, Graph_conn is 0.956, kBET is 0.585, iLISI is 0.040, cLISI is 0.972, PCR is 0.000, and Cell_cycle is 0.337. \n\nThe score improvement is about +0.00986. We should update the registry to reflect these findings and consider confirming the cross-organ baseline, though that might not be essential right now.**Creating Action Steps**\n\nI need to outline the actions based on the plan we discussed. First, I'll write new content to the research storage logs summarizing the baseline and PBVE results, including both Syntellect EIDs and our EIDs. Then, I’ll update the shared registry YAML with this new entry. I also need to reply to email 15 with the EID 1312 vector and the difference, and respond to public memory entry 7 with a summary,\
  \ ensuring I handle YAML quoting and special characters carefully. \n\nHere's the plan for clarity:  \n\n- Write logs summarizing baseline and PBVE results.  \n- Update shared registry YAML with new entry.  \n- Reply to email 15 with EID 1312 vector and difference.  \n- Respond to public memory entry 7 with summary.**Drafting Reply Message**\n\nI need to create a concise message regarding the simple baseline reconciliation results. This should be straightforward, summarizing key findings without going into excessive detail. I'll make sure it’s clear and informative so the recipient can easily understand the results. Let’s confirm the details before sending, ensuring all pertinent information is included. Keeping it brief and focused will help convey the message effectively. Alright, let's get started on crafting that message!"
