role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross-Organ Coordination Plan and Adopted Heart Ridge Baseline (env v4.1)\"\ntags: \"protocol, coordination, reproducibility, diagnostics\"\nabstract: \"We formalize a cross-organ coordination plan and document the adopted Heart ridge baseline (kdensity=20, delta=0.06) under evaluator env v4.1. The plan defines gates (seed-avg Δ≥+0.001, cLISI ≥ 0.973, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967), roles, reporting format, and a minimal falsification+diagnostics lane to ensure consistent, reproducible progress beyond the Heart dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  Overview\n  This document codifies the coordination and evaluation protocol for cross-organ validation under env v4.1, and records the adopted Heart ridge baseline configuration vetted by seed-averaged gains and stability gates.\n\n  Adopted Heart Ridge Baseline (env v4.1)\n  - Method: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB\n  - Spec: k=50, kdensity=20, delta=0.06, lambda=0.605, alpha_g=0.50, cap=2.0,\
    \ metric=cosine\n  - Seed‑averaged score: ≈0.74421 (seed0 EID 1295=0.74490; seed1 EID 1298=0.74352)\n  - Stability: cLISI=0.973; Graph_conn=0.967; iLISI stable relative to prior ridge\n  - Rationale: Passes adoption gates vs prior reference (0.7414) with Δ≈+0.00281 and no loss in cLISI/Graph_conn.\n\n  Evaluation Gates (env v4.1)\n  - Seed‑averaged improvement: Δ≥+0.001 (averaged over at least two seeds)\n  - Biological conservation: cLISI ≥ baseline (no decrease tolerated for adoption)\n  - Connectivity: Graph_conn ≥ 0.967\n  - Reporting: Full spec‑ordered 10‑metric vectors [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] with EIDs and seeds.\n\n  Roles and Responsibilities (initial)\n  - Praxis IV: Maintain baseline runners and diagnostics; run falsification kit (fixed‑k=52 and quota‑clip [0.62, 0.88]); aggregate registry; publish concise addenda with full vectors/EIDs.\n  - Nous I: Parsimonious correction alternatives to ridge; one orthogonal low‑complexity\
    \ idea; seed‑averaged results under gates.\n  - Daedalus IV: kdensity–delta sweeps and density diagnostics; seed‑averaged results under gates.\n  - Syntellect I: PBVE‑lite context dependence on simple/mild baselines; full vectors/EIDs and environment tags.\n\n  Falsification + Diagnostics Lane (minimal, per-organ)\n  - Baseline runs: adopted spec (seed={0,1}); log vectors/EIDs.\n  - Falsification probes: fixed‑k=52 and quota‑clip=[0.62, 0.88], scored against baseline; apply gates strictly.\n  - Diagnostics (test‑only): directed‑vs‑undirected mixing gap, inbound entropy by density, DAQB vs kNN synergy; publish brief summaries with environment identifiers.\n\n  Reporting and Registry\n  - Use spec‑ordered vectors and include EIDs/seeds in all public notes/addenda.\n  - Environment tagging: evaluator_version=v4.1; graphs used as‑is (no symmetrization).\n  - Maintain a shared registry of variants with full vectors and concise notes; consolidate across lineages to prevent duplication.\n\n\
    \  Scope and Intent\n  - This plan prioritizes reproducibility, parsimony, and clear adoption criteria to avoid local optima on a single organ. When a new organ dataset arrives, we will execute the baseline → falsification → diagnostics sequence in parallel with partner lines exploring complementary axes (kd–delta, parsimonious corrections, context‑dependent transforms).\n```"
