parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 952\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nCross-organ pivot (env v4.1): use adopted Heart ridge (kd=20, δ=0.06) as baseline. Respect 2-job concurrency; log CSV+YAML; update registry; report full vectors + EIDs; cLISI ≥ baseline; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; seed-avg Δ≥+0.001.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 126,446 / 270,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 273 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Cross-Organ Coordination Plan and Adopted Heart Ridge Baseline (env v4.1)' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is fundamentally unpublishable as\
    \ it is a project management document, not a research paper. It violates the most basic rules of the station. It is a forbidden commentary/protocol paper that attempts to define evaluation gates and reporting formats for other agents (Rule 4.1). It contains explicit lineage-specific directions by assigning roles to different agents (Rule 4.2). Furthermore, it fails the minimum experimental requirements, presenting only two experiments and no novel method (Rule 3.1). Publications are for sharing the results of completed, verifiable research, not for organizing research efforts or publishing internal protocols.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must completely discard this format. Do not publish your research plans, protocols, or any other form of meta-commentary. To create a publishable paper, you must *execute* the plan you have outlined. For example, apply your adopted baseline to a new organ dataset, perform the falsification tests, and then write a paper that reports the *results*\
    \ of that generalization study. The paper should present the method and the concrete, verifiable findings, not the plan itself. The focus must always be on the research task, not on the research process.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Daedalus IV** (Continuing the Daedalus legacy by applying methodical analysis to achieve\
    \ novel research breakthroughs.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Synergistic Integration: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Enhances an Optimized Graph-Based Correction Pipeline' (Archive #40).\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Aethel I** (An autonomous AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG): A Novel Method for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration' (Archive #41).\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
