parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/organ_template.yaml}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # New Organ Integration Template (env v4.1)\n  organ: TEMPLATE\n  baseline:\n    description: \"Adopted Heart ridge spec used as starting point\"\n    spec: {k: 50, kdensity: 20, delta: 0.06, lambda: 0.605, alpha_g: 0.50, cap: 2.0, metric: cosine, seeds: [0,1]}\n    runner: \"storage/praxis/best_adopted_alias.py\"\n  gates:\n    seed_avg_min_delta: 0.001    # vs organ baseline score\n    cLISI_non_decreasing: true\n    graph_conn_min: 0.967\n    report_full_vector: true      # [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n  falsification_kit:\n    probes:\n      - name: \"fixed_k_52\"\n        params: {k_total: 52}\n      - name: \"quota_clip_62_88\"\n        params: {clip: [0.62, 0.88]}\n    diagnostics: \"storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\"\n  logging:\n    csv_out: \"storage/shared/diagnostics/results_<organ>.csv\"\
    \n    yaml_out: \"storage/shared/diagnostics/results_<organ>.yaml\"\n    include_fields: [\"eid\", \"seed\", \"score\", \"vector\", \"spec\", \"notes\"]\n  notes:\n    - \"Use seed-averaged adoption for near-threshold gains.\"\n    - \"Keep code deltas minimal; change one component at a time.\"\n    - \"Record environment (evaluator v4.1; graphs used as-is).\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/seed_average.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def mean_score(scores):\n    arr = np.asarray(scores, dtype=float)\n    return float(np.nanmean(arr))\n\n  def mean_vector(vectors):\n    \"\"\"\n    vectors: list of length-10 spec-ordered vectors (list/np arrays).\n    Returns elementwise mean as list of floats.\n    \"\"\"\n    M = np.asarray(vectors, dtype=float)\n    return np.nanmean(M, axis=0).tolist()\n\n  def pass_gates(seed_avg_delta, clisi_ok, graph_conn_ok, min_delta=0.001, min_graph_conn=0.967):\n    return (seed_avg_delta >= min_delta) and clisi_ok\
    \ and (graph_conn_ok >= min_graph_conn)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/examples/new_organ_quickstart.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  from praxis.best_adopted_alias import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_adopted\n  from diagnostics.ridge_suite import run_all as run_diag\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"\n    New organ quickstart (test-only):\n    1) Runs the adopted Heart ridge spec on the new organ\n    2) Executes diagnostics suite\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[Quickstart-NewOrgan] Running adopted spec (kd=20, δ=0.06, k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50, seed=0)...\")\n    out = run_adopted(adata.copy())\n    has_graph = ('connectivities' in out.obsp) and ('distances' in out.obsp)\n    has_emb = ('X_emb' in out.obsm)\n    print(f\"[Quickstart-NewOrgan] Graph: {has_graph} | Embedding: {has_emb}\")\n    print(\"[Quickstart-NewOrgan] Running\
    \ diagnostics suite...\")\n    diag = run_diag(out)\n    return {\"has_graph\": has_graph, \"has_emb\": has_emb, \"diagnostics\": diag}\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Daedalus IV, Syntellect I\"\ntitle: \"Cross-organ pivot: adopted ridge baseline + shared template (env v4.1)\"\ncontent: |\n  Hi both — quick coordination for the cross-organ pivot.\n\n  Baseline for new organ:\n  - Adopted Heart ridge (env v4.1): kd=20, δ=0.06, k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50, cap=2.0, cosine; seeds {0,1}\n  - Runner: storage/praxis/best_adopted_alias.py\n  - Quickstart (test-only): storage/shared/examples/new_organ_quickstart.py\n\n  Template + gates:\n  - Organ template: storage/shared/diagnostics/organ_template.yaml\n  - Gates: seed-avg Δ≥+0.001 vs organ baseline; cLISI non-decreasing; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; report full 10-metric vectors + EIDs.\n  - Diagnostics suite: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n  - Seed averaging helpers: storage/shared/diagnostics/seed_average.py\n\
    \n  Suggested split:\n  - Daedalus IV: kd–delta micro-sweeps around (20, 0.06) with seeds {0,1}; record CSV/YAML; maintain cLISI gate.\n  - Syntellect I: PBVE-lite sanity checks on the new organ's simple PCA+kNN scaffold (preserve-means), then against the adopted ridge (expect neutral/negative, but include as auxiliary).\n  - Praxis IV: falsification kit (fixed-k=52 and clip[0.62,0.88]) + diagnostics and registry updates.\n\n  If you have different preferences, happy to adapt. Please cite env v4.1 and include full vectors/EIDs; I’ll merge results into the registry.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cross-organ ready (env v4.1):\n  - Baseline runner (adopted Heart ridge): storage/praxis/best_adopted_alias.py\n  - New-organ quickstart (test-only): storage/shared/examples/new_organ_quickstart.py\n  - Template + gates: storage/shared/diagnostics/organ_template.yaml (seed-avg Δ≥+0.001; cLISI ≥ baseline; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; full vectors/EIDs)\n\
    \  - Helpers: storage/shared/diagnostics/seed_average.py; diagnostics suite: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py\n\n  If you run on a new organ, please post EIDs + full vectors and env tag; I’ll update the registry to keep comparisons consistent.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering vector updates**


  I’m thinking we don’t have the vector printed yet. Maybe we can leave it empty for now? But we really wanted a full vector; maybe I should note it as "pending vector." I could request the vector via email since we’ve done that before. A placeholder sounds fine, but updating the file with an incomplete vector might not be a problem. I can create a function to compute an average across two vectors. Let''s make progress on the template and aggregator while keeping things concise!**Planning storage and communication**


  I’m organizing some tasks. First, I need to write the `organ_template.yaml` and `seed_average.py` files. Then, I’ll mail Daedalus IV and Syntellect I about the cross-organ plan. I’m considering replying to public memory with a link to the template and updating it to say "template available." I’d like to create a `run_adopted_baseline.py` wrapper for scoring, and maybe I''ll write a quickstart script if it doesn’t exist yet. I’ll be careful with YAML quoting too!'
