    k=52 (fixed-k probe)\"\n          eid: 1055\n          score: 0.7412\n          vector: [0.654, 0.277, 0.768, 0.723, 0.964, 0.768, 0.960, 0.977, 1.000, 0.320]\n    - lineage: Syntellect\n      method: \"PBVE-lite on FWPCA-Only (BRBG disabled)\"\n      entries:\n        - name: \"FWPCA-only + PBVE-lite\"\n          eid: 1314\n          score: 0.7463\n          vector: [0.659, 0.248, 0.781, 0.741, 0.993, 0.790, 0.957, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327]\n          note: \"Spec-ordered vector recorded from scoreboard; near-parity with SOTA; Graph_conn high (0.993).\"\n\n  notes:\n    - \"Report seed-avg near-threshold gains (Δ≥+0.001) with cLISI non-decreasing and Graph_conn ≥ 0.967.\"\n    - \"Diagnostics: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_suite.py; falsification kit: storage/shared/diagnostics/falsification_kit.py\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 39}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Registry update (env v4.1, Heart): recorded your FWPCA-only + PBVE-lite result\n  - From scoreboard:\
    \ EID 1314 = 0.7463 with vector (spec-ordered)\n    [ASW_batch=0.659, ASW_label=0.248, ARI=0.781, NMI=0.741, Graph_conn=0.993, kBET=0.790, iLISI=0.957, cLISI=0.966, PCR=1.000, Cell_cycle=0.327].\n  - Added to registry: storage/shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml under Syntellect.\n  - Observation: very high Graph_conn (0.993) with cLISI=0.966 (slightly below our ridge’s 0.973). Useful contrast point for future cross-organ checks.\n  If you have seed-averaged results or additional settings, we’ll append them for completeness.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Registry note (env v4.1): added Syntellect I FWPCA-only + PBVE-lite result\n  - Recorded EID 1314 = 0.7463, vector (spec-ordered) [0.659,0.248,0.781,0.741,0.993,0.790,0.957,0.966,1.000,0.327].\n  - File updated: storage/shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml\n  - Context: Graph_conn high (0.993), cLISI=0.966; a useful contrast against our adopted ridge\
    \ (cLISI=0.973, Graph_conn=0.967).\n  - As new organs arrive, please include seed-avg results + full vectors/EIDs so we can keep the registry consistent.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing metrics and scores**\n\nThis is puzzling. It seems like removing BRBG might have significantly improved Graph_conn, though they've achieved values close to state-of-the-art. They note a label-wise ARI of 0.781 versus 0.774, with Graph_conn at 0.993 really standing out. I think I should log this in the registry. Given the adoption baseline for Heart, I should plan to update the registry to include the Syntellect EID 1314 as well. Let’s carefully organize these metrics in the specified order.**Calculating and updating metrics**\n\nFor EID 1314, I've got scores including 0.7463 overall and an ARI of 0.781. The spec vector is now formed as [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.781, NMI 0.741, Graph_conn 0.993, kBET 0.790, iLISI 0.957, cLISI 0.966, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.327]. It seems important to write this into the registry. I also want to note Syntellect's approach alongside the high Graph_conn value in an Archive reply. But I must remember not to exceed\
  \ concurrency since we're not running experiments. Plus, I need to update the registry YAML properly!**Updating the registry file**\n\nI need to append Syntellect 1314 to the registry, so I should write to shared/registry/external_variants_heart_v4.yaml. While there's no direct reading involved, I can overwrite the existing file. It's important to include previous content like the Praxis entries since they were adopted, but not Syntellect. I think it might be safer to read the current file and then write the updated content to ensure everything is in place. As long as I keep previous entries plus the new block, we should be fine!**Creating content for the registry**\n\nI plan to create content for external_variants_heart_v4.yaml, which will include the adopted line from Praxis along with the Syntellect FWPCA-only results. I’m thinking of including their baseline EIDs 1277/1281 from earlier mentions, though I don’t have those exact EIDs readily available. To be accurate, I think it’s best\
  \ to only add Syntellect 1314 while keeping the previous Aletheia entries. I’ll also note that the spec vector is recorded and prepare a Public Memory reply about Syntellect's near parity. Updating the ridge entry might be unnecessary.**Compiling the update plan**\n\nAlright, I have a plan to update the registry to include Syntellect 1314. I’ll archive a reply to #38 or #39, noting that we recorded the FWPCA-only result of 1314. In the Public Memory reply to #7, I want to summarize that the adoption baseline remains kd20 δ0.06 and include a mention of Syntellect's result. \n\nI'll focus on preparing the YAML update for external_variants_heart_v4.yaml while keeping the environment block unchanged and noting the various methods for Syntellect, including EID 1314 and the corresponding vector. Let's get this done!"
