tick: 970
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 970\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis IV\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nCross-organ pivot (env v4.1): use adopted Heart ridge (kd=20, δ=0.06) as baseline. Respect 2-job concurrency; log CSV+YAML; update registry; report full vectors + EIDs; cLISI ≥ baseline; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967; seed-avg Δ≥+0.001.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 132,290 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 291 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1343**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Novel Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction\n**ID:** 1343\n**Tags:** novel-hypothesis, local-correction, density-adaptive, fwpca, bbsg\n**Abstract:** This experiment tests the novel hypothesis\
    \ that batch effects are local, not global. \nIt introduces an \"Adaptive Local Correction\" mechanism that modulates the batch correction strength on a per-cell basis, proportional to the local data density in the PC space.\nCorrection is strong in dense regions and weak in sparse regions. All other parameters are held constant at SOTA baseline values.\n**Score:** 0.7433911614275126\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.775\n**NMI:** 0.730\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.791\n**iLISI:** 0.964\n**cLISI:** 0.974\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.775  NMI: 0.730\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.791  iLISI: 0.964  cLISI: 0.974\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.774895  NMI: 0.729942\n  Graph_conn: 0.967341  kBET: 0.754425  iLISI: 0.963563  cLISI: 0.992350\n\
    \  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/nous')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                 \
    \            n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # --- Preprocessing (Identical to SOTA) ---\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=False)\n\n    # --- Embedding Path (Identical to SOTA for QC) ---\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Graph Path (with Novel Correction) ---\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # === MODIFICATION: Adaptive Local Correction ===\n    print(\"  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\")\n\n    # 1. Predict batch effect vector (same as SOTA)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    # 2. Calculate\
    \ local density proxy in pre-correction space (Zg)\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8) # 0=dense, 1=sparse\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist # Invert to 1=dense, 0=sparse\n\n    # 3. Calculate global max correction strength (same as SOTA)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    # 4. Modulate correction strength by local density\n    # FIX: Use proper broadcasting to create per-cell, per-PC correction strengths\n    # gamma_global shape: (n_pcs,)\n    # density_factor shape: (n_cells,)\n\
    \    # Result gamma_local shape: (n_cells, n_pcs)\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n\n    # 5. Apply adaptive correction\n    # Both Zhat and gamma_local now have shape (n_cells, n_pcs)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n    print(f\"  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_global):.3f}, Local_Gamma_Mean={np.mean(gamma_local):.3f}\")\n    # === END MODIFICATION ===\n\n    # --- Graph Construction (Identical to SOTA) ---\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total,\
    \ metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['local_adaptive_correction'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam_override),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Nous I - Novel Hypothesis Test: Adaptive Local Correction\n    Modulates correction strength by local data density.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[Nous I] Testing Novel Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction\")\n\
    \n    # Use SOTA baseline parameters to isolate the effect of the new correction method\n    return eliminate_local_adaptive_correction(\n        adata,\n        alpha_g=0.50,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        delta=0.06,\n        kdensity=20,\n        k_total=50,\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Nous I] Testing Novel Hypothesis: Adaptive Local Correction\n  Applying novel Adaptive Local Correction...\n  Correction strength stats: Global_Gamma_Mean=0.030, Local_Gamma_Mean=0.023\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/8398d97a-96fc-41f9-9c6a-2327177ff281/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 8398d97a-96fc-41f9-9c6a-2327177ff281\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1344**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Adaptive Local Correction (Seed 1 Verification)\n**ID:** 1344\n**Tags:** novel-hypothesis, local-correction, seed-verification, sota\n**Abstract:** This submission verifies the new SOTA score achieved by the 'Adaptive Local Correction' method (Eval ID 1343). \nIt runs the exact same, now-corrected code with a different random seed (rng_seed=1) to ensure the result is robust and not due to stochastic chance.\n**Score:** 0.743480391819676\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.775\n**NMI:** 0.730\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.792\n**iLISI:** 0.964\n**cLISI:** 0.974\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.775  NMI: 0.730\n  Graph_conn: 0.967  kBET: 0.792  iLISI: 0.964  cLISI: 0.974\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before\
